role: model
parts:
- text: "I’ll run two concurrent experiments: (A) a minimal algorithmic improvement—advantage normalization with the lineage SOTA architecture; (B) a replication of the prior best LR micro-sweep for verification.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG QuadStep LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — Advantage-Normalized PG\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, convlstm, attention, advantage normalization, gae\"\nabstract: \"We keep Zephyr’s SOTA architecture (4-step LN-ConvLSTM, dilation=6, Attn⊕GAP) and modify only the algorithm: per-batch z-score normalization of advantages in the policy loss. Value targets are unchanged. Optimizer matches lineage (Adam with grad clip 1.0). Hypothesis: improved stability and solve rate with identical capacity.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Advantage-normalized Policy Gradient with Zephyr SOTA architecture.\n  Single change vs default PG: z-score normalize advantages (policy loss only).\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from submissions.submission_pg_quadstep\
    \ import PG_Stepped_AttnGap\n  from ray import tune\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  from defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  # Fixed base seed to ensure stable 4-seed set\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Match Zephyr I SOTA capacity exactly; isolate algorithmic change only\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n\
    \          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      # Match lineage optimizer: grad clip + Adam\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      \"\"\"\n      Custom PG step: identical to system default except:\n      - z-score normalize advantages per (B,T) for the policy loss only.\n      - value target (returns) remains unnormalized.\n      \"\"\"\n      observations = batch['observations']   # (B,T,H,W,C)\n      actions = batch['actions']             # (B,T)\n      rewards = batch['rewards']             # (B,T)\n      dones\
    \ = batch['dones']                 # (B,T)\n      old_values = batch['values']           # (B,T)\n      final_values = batch['final_values']   # (B,)\n      initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n\n      # GAE\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values  # keep unnormalized for value target\n\n      batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n\n      def loss_fn(p):\n          # RNN vs non-RNN forward (copied from system default)\n          if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n              def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n                  env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n                  def step_fn(carry, t):\n                      rnn_state = carry\n                      obs = observations[env_idx, t]\n                      prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n        \
    \              logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_state_b = network.apply(\n                          p, obs[None, ...], jnp.array([prev_done]), jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state)\n                      )\n                      logits = logits_b[0]; value = value_b[0]\n                      new_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_b)\n                      return new_rnn_state, (logits, value)\n                  _, (env_logits, env_values) = jax.lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n                  return env_logits, env_values\n              all_logits, all_values = jax.vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n          else:\n              obs_flat = observations.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length, *observations.shape[2:])\n              dones_flat = dones.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length)\n              logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(p, obs_flat, dones_flat, None)\n              all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size,\
    \ trajectory_length, -1)\n              all_values = values_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n\n          # Log-probs of taken actions\n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions\n          log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n\n          # Advantage normalization for policy loss ONLY\n          adv_mean = jnp.mean(advantages)\n          adv_std = jnp.std(advantages) + 1e-8\n          advantages_norm = (advantages - adv_mean) * (1.0 / adv_std)\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages_norm) * log_probs)\n\n          # Value loss with original (unnormalized) returns\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n\n          # Entropy bonus\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n\n         \
    \ return (policy_loss\n                  + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss\n                  - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy)\n\n      loss_and_grad = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)\n      loss, grads = loss_and_grad(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: PG Quad‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — LR micro‑sweep (3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4)\"\ntags: \"replication, convlstm, attention, policy gradient, gae\"\nabstract: \"Exact replication of the prior best (Eval 487) to verify stability: same architecture (4-step LN-ConvLSTM, dilation=6, Attn⊕GAP) and optimizer (Adam + grad clip 1.0). Only learning rate is sampled over {3.5e-4, 4e-4, 4.5e-4}.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Replication of Zephyr I’s best LR micro-sweep on QuadStep LN-ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP.\n  Uses system default PG training step;\
    \ only re-sweeps LR.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from submissions.submission_pg_quadstep import PG_Stepped_AttnGap\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4, 4.0e-4, 4.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n\
    \          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering algorithm improvements**\n\nI'm thinking about testing z-score normalization for advantages, which might help with stability and sample efficiency without being domain-specific. It’s one way to enhance the algorithm and would involve modifying the training_step function. \n\nI could also consider adding a value baseline coefficient schedule, but that's just a hyperparameter. Using PPO could be another option, although the complexity of the training loop might complicate things, especially given time constraints. Entropy coefficient scheduling could work too, though the default seems optimal. Finally, adding SEP attention is something they've tried before.**Designing algorithm adjustments**\n\nI'm looking at the guidelines of \"Be Strategic\" and \"change one variable,\" which pushes me toward algorithm Track 2. I want to add advantage normalization and adjust gradient norm clipping to 1.0, despite PG having no clipping by default. \n\nI’ll adjust standardization\
  \ only in our training_step, while sticking with the default optimizer, optax.adam, at eps 1e-5. The network architecture will remain as the current state-of-the-art: quadruple-step LN ConvLSTM with Attn⊕GAP. \n\nI plan to keep the submission function consistent with the default signature, ensuring the training_step function updates parameters and states correctly.**Adjusting training_step calculations**\n\nIn our training_step, I plan to compute z-normalized advantages as follows: advantages = (advantages - mean) / (std + 1e-8). The default version calculates returns as advantages plus old values, so I'll follow that approach. However, since the default calculates advantages within the training_step using default_calculate_gae, I can replicate that code in my custom version.\n\nWhile I could adjust hyperparameters to include \"normalize_advantages,\" it’s not strictly necessary. Incorporating value loss coefficient reweighting per batch is a more complex option, but I could also propose\
  \ revising training_step to include \"baselined returns\" with stop gradients as already done by the default setup.**Identifying potential improvements**\n\nI’m noticing a potential bug or improvement in the default_training_step with RNN states. They compute network outputs for each environment over time, and \"initial_rnn_states\" comes from previous rollouts. They also pass env_idx and determine prev_done using dones[env_idx, t-1]. The reset rule appropriately uses prev_done to reset the internal RNN via the done mask. \n\nAnother improvement could be to add \"advantage centering\" per environment or per batch. I'll opt for per-batch. We might also compute \"log probability ratio\" for PPO, but that's not crucial. \n\nThe actions could be integers, so the log probabilities need proper indexing with jnp.arange. I’m set to implement \"training_step_advnorm\" for customizing training_step and consider adding \"value bootstrap per final_values,\" similar to the default setup.**Planning\
  \ new submissions**\n\nFor the advantage normalization variant, I need to create another submission script modifying training_step. I can incorporate the PG model content but might choose to reuse the default training_step without redefining it. However, since the variant needs custom training_step and I'll reference default_calculate_gae from the defaults module, I'll ensure we can import it correctly.\n\nI’m considering two submissions: \n\n1) \"Advantage-Normalized PG\" will use the same network and include a constant learning rate of 4e-4.\n2) \"Replication of 487 LR micro-sweep\" will replicate configurations using learning rate choices to mimic previous results. I’ll ensure to keep dependencies complete and import necessary network classes only to reduce duplication, while managing the potential risk of existing functions within imported modules.**Creating submission code**\n\nFirst, I'll focus on crafting the code for the Advantage Normalization submission. I will add a docstring\
  \ stating that it uses the identical architecture to SOTA. Import necessary modules, such as 'sys', 'ray', and 'jax'.\n\nFor the hyperparameters, I’ll keep fixed values similar to 'submission_pg_quadstep'. The `create_optimizer` will maintain gradient clipping for consistency with previous submissions, and I’ll implement the `training_step` function with normalized advantages.\n\nFor the replication submission, I’ll adjust learning rates using `tune.choice` but keep everything else minimal. Lastly, I'll craft the YAML submission details while ensuring to escape any special characters correctly.**Finalizing submission details**\n\nI'm paying attention to the title since it includes colons and special characters. To be safe, I'll quote it while being mindful of the colon after \"Replication.\" For the second submission, the title needs quoting as well. I'll structure the YAML to enhance clarity and maintain correct quoting.\n\nWhen implementing the submission, I need to ensure that paths\
  \ are set up correctly for importing the necessary modules, particularly from `storage/zephyr`. I think I should embed code to make sure imports succeed, but I want to avoid excessive token use. I’ll code the `training_step`, keeping everything neat while ensuring it replicates the default functionality with normalization. I’ll finalize the YAML to ensure everything is compliant."
