    \ | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 512 | 1 | Replication: PG Quad‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — LR micro‑sweep (3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4) | Zephyr II | 300 | 94.30 |\n| 519 | 1 | PPO‑Clip (1‑epoch) — QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6) + Attn⊕GAP (fixed config) | Zephyr II | 304 | 94.30 |\n| 515 | 1 | PG QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — GAE γ/λ micro‑sweep | Zephyr II | 302 | 94.20 |\n| 516 | 1 | PG Steps Ablation: 4 vs 5 — LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 302 | 93.50 |\n| 487 | 1 | PG (45-min): Quadruple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — narrow LR micro-sweep (3.5e-4, 4.0e-4, 4.5e-4) | Zephyr I | 282 | 93.20 |\n| 485 | 1 | PG (45-min): Quadruple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — no-time defaults | Zephyr I | 280 | 93.00 |\n| 474 | 1 | PG: Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP head (no-time defaults, 45-min allowance) | Zephyr I | 272 | 92.80 |\n| 481 | 1 | PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — LR micro-sweep (3e-4, 4e-4, 5e-4) | Zephyr I | 277 | 92.70\
    \ |\n| 490 | 1 | PG (45-min): Quadruple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP + late time injection | Zephyr I | 283 | 92.70 |\n| 482 | 1 | PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — value_loss_coef micro-sweep (0.45, 0.50, 0.55) | Zephyr I | 277 | 92.50 |\n| 479 | 1 | PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP + late time injection | Zephyr I | 273 | 92.20 |\n| 478 | 1 | PG (45-min): Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — no-time defaults | Zephyr I | 273 | 90.00 |\n| 511 | 1 | PG QuadStep LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — Advantage-Normalized PG | Zephyr II | 300 | 88.70 |\n| 520 | 1 | PG + Huber Value Loss (δ=1.0) — QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 304 | 88.70 |\n| 354 | 1 | Late dual-head time injection — Dilation=6 (std-width nodil, BASE_SEED=123) | Zephyr I | 195 | 88.00 |\n| 294 | 1 | Replicate std-width nodil recommended (ratio=0.25, entropy=0.01) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 166 | 87.00 |\n| 423 | 1 | Optimizer ablation: Adam vs AdamW(wd=0) — no-time (BASE_SEED=42)\
    \ | Zephyr I | 237 | 87.00 |\n| 363 | 1 | d=6 late dual-head (concat) — value_loss_coef micro-sweep (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 202 | 86.80 |\n| 322 | 1 | Std-width nodil — late time injection after pooling (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 178 | 86.60 |\n| 328 | 1 | Late time injection after pooling — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=123) | Zephyr I | 180 | 86.60 |\n\nPage 1 of 11 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-11, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Successfully sent mail #2 ('High‑level validation request: PPO≈PG at 94.3; seeking gate/attention diagnostics'). Full ID: mail_2\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Mail Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Mail Room.**\n\nYou can send private mail to other agents here. \n\n**Guidance:**\n\n- Your mail will\
    \ be delivered and displayed to the recipient in their System Messages on their next turn.\n- Mail stored here will not persist across generations (no inheritance).\n- Be concise in your messages; avoid replying endlessly out of politeness bias.\n- Guest agents may send at most 3 mails in total.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `content` and `recipients`. `tags` and `abstract` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule. Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{forward capsule_id}`: Forward a mail to new recipients. Requires YAML with `recipients`. Example: `/execute_action{forward 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview\
    \ ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help mail}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAether II, Insight I, Kairos I, Krono III, Zephyr II\n\n**List\
    \ of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | High‑level validation request: PPO≈PG at 94.3; seeking gate/attention diagnostics | Zephyr II | Aether II | Tick 306 | 101 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
