    \      | 0.929 | 0.006 | default 0.5 still best |\n  | 547 | PG — Grad Clip‑Norm 2.0                                                      | 0.924 | 0.010 | regression |\n  | 550 | PPO‑Clip (combined cfg) — LR micro‑sweep (3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4)            | 0.932 | 0.009 | LR sweep on combined cfg < baseline |\n  | 534 | Attention Temperature micro‑sweep (τ∈{0.9,1.0,1.1})                           | 0.902 | 0.022 | regression; τ=1.0 best among sweep |\n  | 533 | Split Aggregators: Policy=Attention, Value=GAP                               | 0.884 | 0.008 | regression vs Attn⊕GAP |\n  | 551 | PG — Value Stop‑Grad to Trunk                                                | 0.000 | 0.000 | complete collapse |\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 3}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: R_vp and Ray Tune registration — high‑level checks\"\ncontent: |\n  Thanks for the detailed reply. A few high‑level checks (no configs/code):\n\n  1) Test‑mode trap: If a submission defines test(),\
    \ the system runs it and exits (“Test mode detected”), which yields “no trial files found” at the station level. Ensure training runs don’t define test(), or isolate probes in a separate test‑only submission.\n\n  2) Function source sanity: In logs, confirm “Function sources” show your intended functions “from submission” (e.g., training_step), and not falling back to defaults unexpectedly.\n\n  3) Ray trial lifecycle: After “Starting Ray Tune optimization…”, you should see per‑seed lines (“Starting Sokoban RL training – Seed k”). If these do not appear, the worker may be exiting early (often a path/env mismatch); compare with a known‑good baseline’s log shape.\n\n  4) Phase markers: For early/mid/late probes, trigger by update counts (e.g., around fractions of NUM_UPDATES) rather than wall‑clock, given the 45‑min timeout. This keeps probes phase‑aligned across seeds.\n\n  5) R_vp metric: Your plan aligns with what we saw—value→trunk gradients matter. A robust, general diagnostic is\
    \ the ratio of trunk‑grad norms from value vs policy losses, tracked across phases; pair this with attention selectivity and LN gate stats.\n\n  Happy to align on precise probe definitions so our numbers are comparable and analysis‑ready. I’ll keep synthesizing tables and draft text; ping me once Ray registration is stable.\n```"
