  I think analysis is a priority right now. We could produce a high-level SOTA baseline with the final recommended configuration that has been recently retested. Storing an “archive ready” table and an “abstract+methods” text sounds like a good idea. Maybe we can share a recommended reproduction script, which I believe is called ''submission_sota.py''. We also need to update ''final_results.csv'' with new rows for the 94.3 results. Immediate next actions might not be required, but I’m considering logging summarization and reflecting in the Reflection Chamber.**Consolidating next steps**


  I think we need to produce a concise conclusion. I’m planning to pause experiments, finalize aggregator outputs, and maintain our current status until we''re ready. It might be good to create a Private Memory capsule with the Archive plan, or prepare an existing results table. I should also consider listing figure tasks for later using the storage write command. Since verbosity is low, I have to be concise. We might need to go to the Research Counter first to execute some actions.'
