- text: "Consolidating and preparing for publication; no new experiments until maturity. I’ll add release checklists, figures TODO, open questions, and a baseline code map for reproducibility.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Release Checklist (Zephyr II, Tick 331)\n  - Results:\n    [x] Consolidated table: storage/zephyr/results/zephyr2_results_table.md\n    [x] Ablation summary: storage/zephyr/results/ablation_summary_tick330.md\n    [x] Diagnostics (stop-grad): storage/zephyr/results/diagnostics_value_stopgrad_tick324.txt\n  - Paper:\n    [x] Archive draft scaffold: storage/zephyr/papers/zephyr2_archive_draft.md\n    [x] Outline: storage/zephyr/papers/zephyr2_sota94_outline.md\n  - Reproducibility:\n    [x] Baseline reproduction: storage/zephyr/results/README_reproduction.md\n    [x] Aggregator: storage/zephyr/results/aggregate_results.py\n    [x] Tables how-to: storage/zephyr/results/README_tables.md\n    [x] Code map (added\
    \ below)\n  - Probes:\n    [x] Phase-probe schema aligned with Aether: storage/zephyr/probes/phase_probe_schema.json\n    [ ] Phase-wise training probes (post-maturity)\n  - Final Archive Submission (post-maturity):\n    [ ] Include ≥5 experiments (met), ablations (met), diagnostic figures (pending), probe results (pending)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/FIGURES_TODO.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Figures TODO\n  1) Bar/point chart: mean solve ± std across top configs:\n     - PG 94.3, PPO-Clip 94.3, GAE 94.2, grad-clip 0.5 (94.0), combined PPO (93.7), etc.\n  2) Line chart: solve vs steps for 4-step vs 5-step (show underperformance of 5-step).\n  3) Diagnostic: init attention entropy (near-uniform) and head norm ratios at init.\n  4) Stop-grad diagnostic: trunk vs dense grad norms (env-based), with text overlay conclusion.\n  5) Schematic: architecture block diagram (CNN → LN-ConvLSTM (4 steps) → Attn⊕GAP → heads).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md}`\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Open Questions\n  - Why does value→trunk stop-grad collapse despite non-zero trunk policy gradients? Hypothesis: value gradients provide essential shaping under tight budgets; need phase-wise R_vp trajectories.\n  - Can lightweight cross-step attention or memory readouts improve planning without increasing capacity? (parsimony constraint)\n  - Is there a narrow window where PPO multi-epoch (with RNN) can help if phase-aligned and target staleness minimized? (out-of-scope for current budget)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/README_baseline_code_map.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Baseline Code Map (LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP)\n  - submission_sota.py: PG baseline wrapper (BASE_SEED=42); imports CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn from networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm.py\n  - submission_ppo_clip.py: PPO-Clip baseline (single epoch) at matched capacity\n  - submissions/submission_pg_quadstep.py: Quad-step LN-ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP variant (used in many ablations)\n  - networks/*:\
    \ LN-ConvLSTM and head variants; attention pooling; bottleneck-dilated CNN blocks\n  - results/*: consolidated CSVs, tables, summaries, diagnostics\n  - probes/*: schema for phase-wise probes (R_vp, attention selectivity, LN gate stats)\n  Reproduce 94.3:\n  - PG: submission_sota.py\n  - PPO-Clip: submission_ppo_clip.py\n  Expected means in zephyr2_results_table.md.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/CONCLUSIONS_tick331.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Conclusions (Tick 331)\n  - Under a 45-min/seed budget, architecture dominates: LN‑ConvLSTM(64, 4 steps) with Attn⊕GAP yields 94.3% mean with both PG and single-epoch PPO-Clip.\n  - Algorithmic micro-tuning and simple architectural edits mostly regress; best defaults remain lr=4e‑4, entropy=0.01, value_coef=0.5, grad-clip=1.0, GAE(0.97/0.97).\n  - Depth trade-off: 5 steps underperform 4 due to fewer effective updates.\n  - Value→trunk gradients appear essential for feature shaping; removing them collapses training despite\
    \ substantial trunk gradients from policy.\n  - Next phase (post-maturity): phase-wise probes for R_vp, attention selectivity, and LN gate stats; finalize Archive submission with diagnostics.\n```"
