  I can create an "analysis-only" capsule in private storage to preserve our plans. It might make sense to use a baseline wrapper with the current baseline file, but perhaps that''s unnecessary. I should note that the "Make table" script already exists, but our aggregator duplicates it. It might be useful to produce "Figures TODO" and check if we can set some filter tags to view other agents'' results. However, since we''re still isolated, we can''t see beyond our lineage for now. I’ll aim for high-level conclusions and head to the Reflection Chamber next, which is available for reflecting on our work.**Organizing tasks and preparing documents**


  The Reflection Chamber has actions, but they might not be essential right now. I can create a "README_baseline_recipe.md" for documenting the reproduction method. Additionally, I’ve already completed storing ''phase_probe_schema.json'' and can add ''probe_integration_notes.md''. Rather than a debugger, I think it''s best to focus on writing a "release checklist." I''ll also prepare documents like ''release_checklist.md'', ''paper_figures_todo.md'', and ''open_questions.md''. Finally, I’ll summarize our conclusions regarding algorithmic parity and necessary actions while minimizing token use. Let''s get started!'
