- text: "I’ll finalize consolidation artifacts for smooth publication and later probe work. No new experiments until maturity.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/README_index.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr II — Results & Paper Index (Tick 336)\n  Core\n  - Consolidated table: results/zephyr2_results_table.md\n  - Ablation summary: results/ablation_summary_tick330.md\n  - Conclusions: results/CONCLUSIONS_tick331.md\n  - Reproduction guide: results/README_reproduction.md\n  - Baseline code map: results/README_baseline_code_map.md\n  - Aggregation script: results/aggregate_results.py\n  - Tables how-to: results/README_tables.md\n  Diagnostics & Probes\n  - Stop‑grad diagnostics (env-based): results/diagnostics_value_stopgrad_tick324.txt\n  - Probe schema (align Aether): probes/phase_probe_schema.json\n  - Probe alignment notes: results/PROBE_ALIGNMENT_NOTES.md\n  Paper Drafts\n  - Archive draft: papers/zephyr2_archive_draft.md\n  - Outline: papers/zephyr2_sota94_outline.md\n\
    \  - Pseudocode (training): papers/pseudocode_pg_training.md\n  - Pseudocode (architecture): papers/pseudocode_architecture.md\n  Project Ops\n  - Release checklist: results/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md\n  - Figures TODO: results/FIGURES_TODO.md\n  - Next steps: results/README_next_steps.md\n  - Changelog: results/CHANGELOG.md\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/papers/abstract_skeleton.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Abstract (Skeleton)\n  Background: Planning in Sokoban under tight time budgets; need capacity‑matched comparisons.\n  Method: LN‑ConvLSTM(64, 4 steps) + attention⊕GAP; four‑seed evaluation; PG vs 1‑epoch PPO‑Clip at matched capacity.\n  Results: Both PG and PPO‑Clip reach 94.3% mean. Micro‑tuning (entropy, value_coef, grad clip, Adam ε) and simple architectural edits (attention temperature, split aggregators) regress. 5‑step recurrence underperforms 4‑step. Value→trunk stop‑grad collapses training.\n  Diagnosis: Init attention is near‑uniform; value gradients to the trunk\
    \ appear essential for feature shaping under the 45‑min/seed budget.\n  Conclusion: Architectural parsimony dominates; provide replication and probe schema for phase‑wise diagnostics.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/DATA_DICTIONARY.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Data Dictionary (Zephyr II)\n  Files:\n  - zephyr2_results_table.md\n    • id: evaluation ID\n    • title: short description of the run\n    • mean: mean test solve rate across 4 seeds\n    • std: standard deviation across 4 seeds\n    • notes: key settings or takeaway\n  - ablation_summary_tick330.md: narrative summary of ablations and main takeaways\n  - diagnostics_value_stopgrad_tick324.txt: text summary of env‑based gradient norms for stop‑grad variant\n  - README_reproduction.md: steps and expected metrics to reproduce 94.3 baselines\n  - probes/phase_probe_schema.json: JSON schema for phase‑wise probe logs (R_vp, attention, LN gate stats)\n  Conventions:\n  - All means are across 4 seeds (BASE_SEED\
    \ + {0,1,2,3}); time budget ≤45 min/seed; ≤50M steps/seed\n  - Architecture fixed unless explicitly stated: CNN(32/64) + LN‑ConvLSTM(64, 4 steps) + attention⊕GAP\n```"
