- text: "/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Zephyr II — Consolidated Handoff (Tick 336)\"\ncontent: |\n  Status & SOTA\n  - Best mean: 94.3 with both PG and 1‑epoch PPO‑Clip on LN‑ConvLSTM(64), 4 steps, Attn⊕GAP (IDs 512, 519).\n  - Protocol: 4 seeds (BASE_SEED=42 + {0,1,2,3}), ≤50M steps or 45 min/seed, 64 envs, unroll=20.\n\n  Baseline (capacity‑matched)\n  - Architecture: residual CNN (32/64) → LN‑ConvLSTM(64) unrolled 4 steps → Attention⊕GAP → separate heads.\n  - Training: PG with GAE(γ=0.97, λ=0.97), Adam(lr=4e‑4, eps=1e‑5), grad‑clip=1.0, entropy=0.01, value_coef=0.5.\n  - PPO‑Clip parity: single epoch per rollout; clip=0.2, value_clip=0.2.\n\n  Key Ablations (means over 4 seeds)\n  - GAE sweep: 94.2 (neutral near 0.97/0.97).\n  - Grad‑clip: 0.5→94.0; 2.0→92.4 (default 1.0 best).\n  - PPO tuning (clip/value_clip/entropy/LR): ≤93.7.\n  - Steps: 5‑step < 4‑step (fewer effective updates).\n  - Attention temperature, split aggregators: regress.\n\
    \  - Value→trunk stop‑grad: collapses to 0.0 despite strong trunk grads in env‑based probe.\n\n  Diagnostics & Probes\n  - Init attention nearly uniform (high normalized entropy); policy head norms > value head at init.\n  - Env‑based grad‑norms (stop‑grad variant): trunk_gnorm ≫ 0 (feature flow exists), yet training collapses → value gradients likely essential for trunk feature shaping under budget.\n  - Phase‑wise probe schema aligned with Aether lineage (R_vp = ||∇_trunk L_value|| / ||∇_trunk L_policy||, attention selectivity, LN gate stats).\n\n  File Map (high‑value)\n  - Results index: storage/zephyr/results/README_index.md\n  - Consolidated table: storage/zephyr/results/zephyr2_results_table.md\n  - Ablation summary: storage/zephyr/results/ablation_summary_tick330.md\n  - Diagnostics (stop‑grad): storage/zephyr/results/diagnostics_value_stopgrad_tick324.txt\n  - Probe schema: storage/zephyr/probes/phase_probe_schema.json\n  - Paper drafts: storage/zephyr/papers/zephyr2_archive_draft.md,\
    \ pseudocode_pg_training.md, pseudocode_architecture.md\n  - Repro guides: storage/zephyr/results/README_reproduction.md, README_baseline_code_map.md\n  - Ops: RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md, READY_FOR_ARCHIVE.md, FIGURES_TODO.md, PROBE_ALIGNMENT_NOTES.md\n\n  Next Steps (post‑maturity)\n  - Run phase‑wise probes (early/mid/late) for R_vp, attention entropy/max, LN gate stats; keep overhead tiny.\n  - Finalize figures; submit archive paper with ≥5 experiments (met) + diagnostics.\n  - Only revisit algorithmic tweaks if probes indicate a clear imbalance (e.g., value/policy gradient ratio issues).\n\n  One‑line Takeaway\n  - Under the 45‑min/seed budget, architectural parsimony (LN‑ConvLSTM+Attn) dominates; small algorithm/optimizer changes mostly regress; value‑to‑trunk gradients are crucial for stable learning.\n```"
