  \ trigger \"No trial files found\" unless there were exceptions caught during writing. It's odd that the code isn’t raising errors. The logging of metric numbers could be a factor, but the 'train_single.py' should still expect updated params and opt_state from the training_step.\n\nAnother thought is that if STEP_COUNT is being altered across Ray process boundaries, it may lead to issues with pickling. Ultimately, \"No trial files found\" suggests Ray Tune failed to write result.csv because training finished before any trials, likely due to errors raised.**Analyzing potential issues with training**\n\nI’m seeing that crashes might be tied to the remote worker environment, especially concerning the 'defaults' import in the training_step code. The system module under 'storage/system/defaults.py' could be the issue if it isn't in the sys.path of the remote worker. In earlier tasks, we didn't have to import 'defaults', but now we reference 'default_calculate_gae' from it. \n\nIt seems that\
