role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6, 64ch) + Attn⊕GAP — Phase Probes (R_vp, vlc=0.55) — inline\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, diagnostics, probes, convlstm, attention, recurrent depth\"\nabstract: \"Inline, self‑contained 5‑step probes. Logs R_vp = ||∇_trunk L_value|| / ||∇_trunk L_policy|| at ~8k/20k/32k updates with negligible overhead. Config: convlstm_features=64, steps=5, value_loss_coef=0.55, entropy=0.01, Adam lr=4e‑4, GAE(0.97/0.97).\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Inline submission: PG 5-step LN-ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP with minimal phase probes (R_vp).\n  All functions defined here to ensure proper registration (\"from submission\").\n  Logs to: storage/zephyr/results/probes_phase_pg5.jsonl at ~8k, 20k, 32k updates.\n  \"\"\"\n  import json\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from submissions.submission_pg_quadstep import PG_Stepped_AttnGap\n  from ray import tune\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from\
    \ typing import Dict, Any\n  import defaults\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  default_calculate_gae = defaults.default_calculate_gae\n\n  # Probe schedule (5-step typically ~32-33k updates in 45min at 64ch)\n  STEP_COUNT = 0\n  PROBE_TARGETS = {8000, 20000, 32000}\n  PROBE_PATH = 'storage/zephyr/results/probes_phase_pg5.jsonl'\n\n  # Training coefficients (chosen based on best 5-step sweep)\n  VALUE_COEF = 0.55\n  ENTROPY_COEF = 0.01\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Fixed config; 4 seeds handled by the system.\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([ENTROPY_COEF]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([VALUE_COEF]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps':\
    \ tune.choice([5]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n\n  def _forward_seq(network, p, observations, dones, initial_rnn_states):\n      B, T = observations.shape[:2]\n      if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n \
    \                 rnn_state = carry\n                  obs = observations[env_idx, t]\n                  prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                  logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_b = network.apply(\n                      p, obs[None, ...], jnp.array([prev_done]),\n                      jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state)\n                  )\n                  logits = logits_b[0]; value = value_b[0]\n                  new_rnn = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_b)\n                  return new_rnn, (logits, value)\n              _, (env_logits, env_values) = jax.lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(T))\n              return env_logits, env_values\n          all_logits, all_values = jax.vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(B))\n      else:\n          obs_flat = observations.reshape(B * T, *observations.shape[2:])\n          dones_flat = dones.reshape(B * T)\n          logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(p, obs_flat, dones_flat,\
    \ None)\n          all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(B, T, -1)\n          all_values = values_flat.reshape(B, T)\n      return all_logits, all_values\n\n  def _global_norm(tree):\n      leaves = jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(tree)\n      if not leaves:\n          return jnp.array(0.0)\n      sq = sum([jnp.sum(jnp.square(x)) for x in leaves])\n      return jnp.sqrt(sq + 1e-12)\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch):\n      global STEP_COUNT\n      observations = batch['observations']\n      actions = batch['actions']\n      rewards = batch['rewards']\n      dones = batch['dones']\n      old_values = batch['values']\n      final_values = batch['final_values']\n      initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      B, T = observations.shape[:2]\n\n      def loss_components(p):\n          all_logits, all_values\
    \ = _forward_seq(network, p, observations, dones, initial_rnn_states)\n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          idx = (jnp.arange(B)[:, None], jnp.arange(T), actions)\n          log_probs = log_probs_all[idx]\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages) * log_probs)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          total = policy_loss + VALUE_COEF * value_loss - ENTROPY_COEF * entropy\n          return total, (policy_loss, value_loss, entropy)\n\n      (total_loss, (policy_loss, value_loss, entropy)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(\n          loss_components, has_aux=True\n      )(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n\n      STEP_COUNT += 1\n      if STEP_COUNT\
    \ in PROBE_TARGETS:\n          def policy_only(p):\n              all_logits, _ = _forward_seq(network, p, observations, dones, initial_rnn_states)\n              log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n              idx = (jnp.arange(B)[:, None], jnp.arange(T), actions)\n              log_probs = log_probs_all[idx]\n              return -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages) * log_probs)\n\n          def value_only(p):\n              _, all_values = _forward_seq(network, p, observations, dones, initial_rnn_states)\n              return 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n\n          g_pol = jax.grad(policy_only)(params)\n          g_val = jax.grad(value_only)(params)\n          g_pol_norm = _global_norm(g_pol)\n          g_val_norm = _global_norm(g_val)\n          ratio = g_val_norm / (g_pol_norm + 1e-12)\n\n          try:\n              with open(PROBE_PATH, 'a') as f:\n                  f.write(json.dumps({\n                  \
    \    \"step\": int(STEP_COUNT),\n                      \"grad_trunk_policy\": float(jax.device_get(g_pol_norm)),\n                      \"grad_trunk_value\": float(jax.device_get(g_val_norm)),\n                      \"rvp_ratio\": float(jax.device_get(ratio))\n                  }) + \"\\n\")\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating project options**


  While waiting for task #597 to complete, I could summarize the 5-step equalization results and propose a plan in the Public Memory capsule. It might also be good to document this in our results folder. The system encourages ongoing experimentation, so I could queue mirrored submissions of the best 5-step configurations. However, I can''t exceed two concurrent tasks, and it seems only #597 is running right now, even though earlier tasks #594 and #595 have completed.**Creating submission code**


  Currently, only task #597 is running, leaving one slot free. I can submit the 5-step inline probes if that’s allowed, although there''s a risk of mis-registration again. So, I’ll create the submission code for the inline 5-step probes, using the previous 4-step format but adjusting to steps=5 and choosing either width=64 or 48. For fairness, I’ll settle on steps=5 with width=64 and vlc=0.55. Also, I’ll ensure that ''value_loss_coef'' is set correctly. Lastly, I''ll log the results and consider writing a short update to the archived paper.**Implementing archive results**


  The archive was accepted, which is great! I think we can keep the results for a follow-up later. I might want to adjust the sorting of the Research Counter to id or score, but that’s not crucial. It’s also fine to include storage writes along with results, though I need to keep tokens at a minimum since the agent budget is 130k used out of 270k total. Let''s proceed with the storage write for ''zephyr/submissions/submission_pg_5step_probes_inline.py'' using inline code similar to the 4-step format.**Finalizing 5-step settings**


  I''m setting steps to 5 and considering convlstm_features at either 64 or 48. The best configuration for the 5-step includes width 64 with vlc at 0.55. The equalized width of 48 produced a score of 92.9 with value_coef at 0.55, while 64 scored even better. To align with the 4-step capacity, I’ll stick with 64 for depth. I’ll proceed with value_loss_coef set to 0.55. Next, I''ll submit the results as "PG 5-step ... Phase Probes (R_vp) — inline (vlc=0.55)" and address the previous "No trial files found" issue by ensuring _define_hyperparameters is included in the inline code.**Preparing for submission**


  Alright, I need to prepare a few things after submission, like creating a small to-do file or notes, but I want to keep that light. I’ll set up PROBE_PATH to log results and targets based on the calculated updates, deciding on {8000, 20000, 32000} since 5 steps will differ from 4-step settings. I also need to ensure we import what''s required and define the optimizer as before. I’m opting for value_loss_coef as 0.55 and will implement that, keeping in mind concurrency with the current tasks running. Lastly, I''ll craft the submission code, ensuring it imports properly.**Finalizing the submit command**


  The submit command needs to include the code directly, as we did with the earlier inline submission for the 4-step. Instead of importing from a file, I''ll embed the code in the content to avoid any registration issues. Although I could write the file to storage for reference, I''ll skip that this time to keep it short and token-efficient. So, I’ll submit the 5-step inline with the value_coef set to 0.55, ensuring the code structure matches what we used in the 4-step. I''m also planning to ensure the functions are sourced correctly. Let’s get this implemented!'
