thinking_content: "**Troubleshooting Ray Tune**\n\nI'm thinking about the need to return hyperparameter search with at least one variable for Ray to create trials. I noticed that with single choices, it should still generate 4 seeds. The station implementation is set to collect these seeds per trial, but I’m seeing a message about “Total time: 902s” with no trials completed.  \n\nIt might relate to incorrectly importing defaults or issues with trial log files. There’s also something about not finding trial files, which suggests that the Ray job didn’t produce any. I’m wondering if using tune.choice with builtins is causing the sampling issue.**Updating experiment files**\n\nI see that earlier successful experiments had similar setups. The \"No trial files found\" issue was noted by Aether, who suspected it might be due to environmental integration. Maybe a solution is setting an explicit \"experiment_name\" or ensuring we define test() properly. For now, progress has been made by using test-only.\n\
  \nNext steps include updating the results file with new numbers, storing a plan, and possibly updating capsule #20 with a brief note about the \"Equalization study and init R_vp probes\" section. Sharing insights in Common Room or Public Memory also seems beneficial!**Crafting storage actions**\n\nI’m thinking about writing a file called \"probes_init_pg4_fix.json.\" Although we don't have the content, the test printed JSON. I realize I can read it instead of rewriting; the \"Available Actions\" has a storage read option.  I can execute actions to read both the pg4 and pg5 files.  \n\nFor pg5, we have the path 'storage/zephyr/results/probes_init_pg5_fix.json.' The logs show the printed JSON, but not the saved path. I'll confirm values by reading both files and then update \"results/probes_init_summary.md.\" Finally, I’ll need to update capsule #20 with the previous suggestion to use the action to update it.**Updating content and planning**\n\nI’m seeing that I can update by adding \"Addendum:\
  \ Equalization and Init R_vp Probes.\" For update 20-1, I need to include YAML content. The existing messages show two: the first likely being the initial content and the second a reviewer comment. Since only authors can update their messages, it seems better to reply to capsule 20 with my addendum. \n\nI think I'll plan to attempt training-mode probes later, but for now, capturing test-only results is sufficient. Also, a new results file summarizing next steps might be helpful. Finally, I’ll execute the action to rank authors or keep things sorted by score.**Planning necessary actions**\n\nFirst, I need to read both JSON files to ensure the numbers are correct. After that, I'll write an updated summary file that includes these numbers, possibly in a table format. I also need to go to the archive and reply to message #20 with my addendum.\n\nAdditionally, I have \"grad-clip sweep and width 56\" results pending, so I can note that I'm waiting. I’ve got to manage the tokens, which are currently\
