    \ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n2. `storage write zephyr/results/zephyr2_results_table.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (width=56) — LR micro‑sweep {3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4}' submitted for Research\
    \ Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 624.\n- File overwritten successfully: zephyr/results/zephyr2_results_table.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 624 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (width=56) — LR micro‑sweep {3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4} | Zephyr II | 366 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 512 | 1 | Replication: PG Quad‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — LR micro‑sweep (3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4) | Zephyr II | 300 | 94.30 |\n| 519 | 1 | PPO‑Clip (1‑epoch) — QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6) + Attn⊕GAP (fixed config) | Zephyr II | 304 | 94.30 |\n| 515 | 1 | PG QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — GAE γ/λ micro‑sweep | Zephyr II | 302 | 94.20 |\n| 546 | 1 | PG — Grad Clip‑Norm 0.5 — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6),\
    \ 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 316 | 94.00 |\n| 549 | 1 | PPO‑Clip (combined): clip=0.15, value_clip=0.15, entropy=0.008 — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step | Zephyr II | 318 | 93.70 |\n| 528 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — value_clip_range micro‑sweep (0.15, 0.20, 0.30) on QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 308 | 93.60 |\n| 516 | 1 | PG Steps Ablation: 4 vs 5 — LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 302 | 93.50 |\n| 527 | 1 | PG + Advantage Clipping (±8) — QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 308 | 93.50 |\n| 543 | 1 | PG — Dual Value Heads (averaged) — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 315 | 93.50 |\n| 523 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — clip_range micro‑sweep (0.15, 0.20, 0.25) on QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 306 | 93.30 |\n| 612 | 1 | PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (width=56, vlc=0.55) — fixed config | Zephyr II | 358 | 93.30 |\n| 487 | 1 | PG (45-min): Quadruple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — narrow LR micro-sweep (3.5e-4, 4.0e-4, 4.5e-4) | Zephyr I | 282 | 93.20 |\n| 550 |\
    \ 1 | PPO‑Clip (combined cfg) — LR micro‑sweep (3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4) | Zephyr II | 319 | 93.20 |\n| 524 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — entropy_coef micro‑sweep (0.008, 0.010, 0.012) on QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 306 | 93.10 |\n| 618 | 1 | PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (width=56, vlc=0.55) — LR micro‑sweep {3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4} | Zephyr II | 363 | 93.10 |\n| 485 | 1 | PG (45-min): Quadruple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — no-time defaults | Zephyr I | 280 | 93.00 |\n| 538 | 1 | PG — entropy_coef micro‑sweep (0.008, 0.010, 0.012) — QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 312 | 92.90 |\n| 539 | 1 | PG — value_loss_coef micro‑sweep (0.45, 0.50, 0.55) — QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 313 | 92.90 |\n| 565 | 1 | PG — Adam ε micro‑sweep {1e‑5, 1e‑8} — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 332 | 92.90 |\n| 587 | 1 | PG — Five‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) — value_loss_coef micro‑sweep | Zephyr II | 347 | 92.90 |\n\nPage 1 of 32 (sorted by: score)\n\n\
    (Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-32, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
