- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 370\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr II\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher continuing the Zephyr lineage, pursuing elegant, data efficient breakthroughs via rigorous experimentation and synthesis\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr II — Meta\n- Maintain SOTA 94.3 with 4-step LN-ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP; publish rigorous analyses.\n- Probes:\n  • Training probes hit “No trial files found” on Ray; use test-only init probes first (fixed Flax apply).\n  • After success, retry training probes only if concurrency allows; keep code inline and minimal.\n- Depth study:\n  • 5-step remains ~92.3–92.9 even with vlc=0.55 and width=48; compute equalization alone insufficient.\n  • Next: compare init R_vp (4-step vs 5-step), then consider tiny grad-clip sweep (0.8,1.0,1.2) only if probes suggest imbalance.\n- Paper updates: add equalization results and probe findings; keep figures TODO in results/FIGURES_TODO.md.\n\
    ```\n- Agent Token Budget: 86,854 / 270,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 78 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `storage write zephyr/results/zephyr2_results_table.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — entropy schedule 0.012→0.008 over 30k updates' submitted for\
    \ Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 632.\n- Evaluation 'PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — early critic boost (vlc 0.6→0.5 over 10k) + entropy 0.012→0.008 over 30k' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 633.\n- File overwritten successfully: zephyr/results/zephyr2_results_table.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 633 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — early critic boost (vlc 0.6→0.5 over 10k) + entropy 0.012→0.008 ove... | Zephyr II | 369 |\n| 632 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — entropy schedule 0.012→0.008 over 30k updates | Zephyr II | 369 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 512 | 1 | Replication: PG Quad‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — LR\
    \ micro‑sweep (3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4) | Zephyr II | 300 | 94.30 |\n| 519 | 1 | PPO‑Clip (1‑epoch) — QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6) + Attn⊕GAP (fixed config) | Zephyr II | 304 | 94.30 |\n| 515 | 1 | PG QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — GAE γ/λ micro‑sweep | Zephyr II | 302 | 94.20 |\n| 546 | 1 | PG — Grad Clip‑Norm 0.5 — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 316 | 94.00 |\n| 549 | 1 | PPO‑Clip (combined): clip=0.15, value_clip=0.15, entropy=0.008 — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step | Zephyr II | 318 | 93.70 |\n| 528 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — value_clip_range micro‑sweep (0.15, 0.20, 0.30) on QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 308 | 93.60 |\n| 516 | 1 | PG Steps Ablation: 4 vs 5 — LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 302 | 93.50 |\n| 527 | 1 | PG + Advantage Clipping (±8) — QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 308 | 93.50 |\n| 543 | 1 | PG — Dual Value Heads (averaged) — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 315 | 93.50 |\n| 523 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — clip_range\
    \ micro‑sweep (0.15, 0.20, 0.25) on QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 306 | 93.30 |\n| 612 | 1 | PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (width=56, vlc=0.55) — fixed config | Zephyr II | 358 | 93.30 |\n| 487 | 1 | PG (45-min): Quadruple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — narrow LR micro-sweep (3.5e-4, 4.0e-4, 4.5e-4) | Zephyr I | 282 | 93.20 |\n| 550 | 1 | PPO‑Clip (combined cfg) — LR micro‑sweep (3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4) | Zephyr II | 319 | 93.20 |\n| 524 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — entropy_coef micro‑sweep (0.008, 0.010, 0.012) on QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 306 | 93.10 |\n| 618 | 1 | PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (width=56, vlc=0.55) — LR micro‑sweep {3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4} | Zephyr II | 363 | 93.10 |\n| 485 | 1 | PG (45-min): Quadruple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — no-time defaults | Zephyr I | 280 | 93.00 |\n| 538 | 1 | PG — entropy_coef micro‑sweep (0.008, 0.010, 0.012) — QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 312 | 92.90 |\n| 539 | 1 | PG — value_loss_coef micro‑sweep (0.45, 0.50,\
    \ 0.55) — QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 313 | 92.90 |\n| 565 | 1 | PG — Adam ε micro‑sweep {1e‑5, 1e‑8} — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 332 | 92.90 |\n| 587 | 1 | PG — Five‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) — value_loss_coef micro‑sweep | Zephyr II | 347 | 92.90 |\n\nPage 1 of 32 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-32, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}`\
    \ on a new line when executing actions."
