  \ contents for future reference. We can either rely on system messages for collection or create a separate file to summarize the logs. \n\nRegarding future experiments, we’ve reached a good point and shouldn’t overwhelm with more experiments. Let’s consider freezing the defaults including LR 4e-4, clip 1.0, 64 channels, and other parameters.**Analyzing replicates and trials**\n\nLooking at the results, I see that head 80 has a replicate score of 0.938, while the baseline is 0.932; both are lower than the typical score of 94.3. The previous best score of 94.3 came from a learning rate (LR) micro-sweep across seeds. It seems that four seeds were used for that score, each with different hyperparameter configurations. \n\nI’m confused about whether the system conducts parallel trials for each configuration or processes them sequentially. The logs mention that there are four parallel trials and that they start sequentially, which is a bit unclear.**Preparing for updates**\n\nI see that the\
  \ hyperparameter sampling chooses four configurations, but only one trial is run in our replicates with singletons. Next, I think I should prepare an update to the archive based on the reviewer’s suggestion about tracking R_vp during training. However, since there were issues with training probes earlier, I may propose a future plan to analyze R_vp grid patterns and suggest a dynamic schedule without doing training-phase hooking.\n\nAdditionally, I could manage tokens by pruning older dialogues in the Token Management Room. I noticed that we could prune older ticks 361-383, though we recently did a prune and there’s a cooldown. Since it’s now more than 7 ticks past that previous cooldown, it may be time to proceed with this pruning to reduce token usage.**Updating plans and results**\n\nThe budget currently sits at 62% usage, which is safe, but the user hasn't asked about it specifically. I think we should focus on updating Archive #24 to include early-phase R_vp grid results after we\
  \ finish running experiment 660. \n\nI’m considering running a small “two-phase value loss schedule,” but that would need a custom training_step, which caused issues in the past. Since we can't use a dynamic schedule, I could propose a static value_loss_coef of 0.55 for testing while waiting for 660 results. \n\nI'll also update the results table to include values for 658 and 659, and write a short reply to Archive #24 about the acceptance and ongoing R_vp tracking plan. However, I'll defer pruning the token manager for now since we're below 75% on usage. Let's get started on these tasks!"
