role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/bottleneck_ratio_micro_tune.csv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,ratio,mean,std\n  673,0.26,0.936,0.000\n  512,0.28,0.943,0.005\n  670,0.28 (vlc=0.55),0.943,0.005\n  674,0.30,0.938,0.007\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/bottleneck_ratio_micro_tune.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Bottleneck Ratio Micro‑Tune (4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64), Attn⊕GAP, lr=4e‑4, clip=1.0, ent=0.01, vlc=0.50 unless noted)\n  - 0.26 → 93.6 ± 0.000 (Eval 673)\n  - 0.28 → 94.3 ± 0.005 (Eval 512)\n  - 0.28 (vlc=0.55) → 94.3 ± 0.005 (Eval 670)\n  - 0.30 → 93.8 ± 0.007 (Eval 674)\n  Conclusion: 0.28 remains optimal; small deviations (±0.02) regress.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — Two‑phase vlc schedule 0.55→0.50 @20k\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, scheduling, value loss coef, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Test a minimal two‑phase value loss schedule motivated by R_vp probes and vlc fixed‑runs: start vlc=0.55\
    \ then switch to 0.50 at ~20k updates. Other settings match SOTA. Goal: ≥94.3 mean.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  # Import scheduled training variant implemented in lineage storage\n  from submissions.submission_pg_value_schedule import (\n      _define_hyperparameters, create_network, create_optimizer,\n      training_step, BASE_SEED\n  )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — Two‑phase vlc schedule 0.55→0.50 @15k\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, scheduling, value loss coef, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Ablation of the two‑phase value loss schedule: earlier switch at ~15k updates. Other settings match SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from submissions.submission_pg_quadstep import PG_Stepped_AttnGap\n  from ray import tune\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  SCHEDULE_STEP = 15000  #\
    \ earlier switch\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n\
    \      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n\n  def _get_update_count(opt_state):\n      try:\n          return jnp.asarray(opt_state[1].count)\n      except Exception:\n          leaves = jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(opt_state)\n          for l in leaves:\n              if isinstance(l, jnp.ndarray) and l.shape == () and l.dtype.kind in (\"i\", \"u\"):\n                  return l\n          return jnp.asarray(0)\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      observations = batch['observations']\n      actions = batch['actions']\n      rewards = batch['rewards']\n      dones = batch['dones']\n      old_values = batch['values']\n      final_values = batch['final_values']\n\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n\n      B, T = observations.shape[:2]\n\
    \      obs_flat = observations.reshape(B * T, *observations.shape[2:])\n      dones_flat = dones.reshape(B * T)\n\n      def loss_fn(p):\n          logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(p, obs_flat, dones_flat, None)\n          logits = logits_flat.reshape(B, T, -1)\n          values = values_flat.reshape(B, T)\n\n          logp_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          idx = (jnp.arange(B)[:, None], jnp.arange(T), actions)\n          logp = logp_all[idx]\n\n          step_count = _get_update_count(opt_state)\n          vlc = jnp.where(step_count < SCHEDULE_STEP, 0.55, 0.50)\n\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages) * logp)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * logp_all, axis=-1))\n          return policy_loss + vlc * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n\n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n\
    \      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 24}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum #10: Bottleneck micro‑tune (0.26, 0.30) — 0.28 remains optimal\"\ncontent: |\n  We tested ±0.02 around the recommended bottleneck_ratio=0.28 (4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64), Attn⊕GAP; lr=4e‑4, clip=1.0, ent=0.01, vlc=0.50):\n  - 0.26 → 93.6 ± 0.000 (Eval 673)\n  - 0.30 → 93.8 ± 0.007 (Eval 674)\n  Context: 0.28 remains at 94.3 (Evals 512/670). Conclusion: micro‑tuning around 0.28 regresses; keep 0.28 as default.\n```"
