tick: 403
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/stagnation_protocol/lit_review_summary_tick402.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stagnation Protocol I — Literature Review (tick 402)\n\n  Scope: Archive previews (#1–#24) synthesized.\n  Key themes:\n  - Recurrent capacity: LN‑ConvLSTM with attention pooling dominates; double/quad steps and width tuning drive gains (60–94% across eras).\n  - Receptive field: Dilations materially help; bottleneck blocks enable efficient capacity (Krono/Aether).\n  - Algorithm fit: PPO prefers simple heads; PG benefits from richer readouts (attention⊕GAP). Value_loss_coef is architecture‑dependent.\n  - Negative synergy: Channel attention (SE) degrades SOTA ConvLSTM under PPO; head complexity hurts PPO.\n  - Baselines: Simple CNN+PG ≈ 25% (ID 1); CNN‑LSTM+PG ≈ 41% (ID 2). These are robust but far below SOTA, hence suitable for novel ideas.\n  - Scheduling: Our own dynamic vlc schedules collapsed on SOTA (catastrophic). Constants remain\
    \ robust.\n  Gaps for exploration on simple CNN baseline:\n  - Regularization and optimization variants (AdamW, wd).\n  - Lightweight normalization changes in CNN trunk (e.g., GroupNorm) instead of heavy architectural overhauls.\n  - Loss shaping (e.g., Huber value) on low‑capacity baselines, even if it regressed at SOTA.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/stagnation_protocol/baseline_and_plan_tick402.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Baseline Selection and Plan (tick 402)\n  - Baseline: System CNN+PG (ID 1 reference; ~0.25 mean). Chosen for simplicity and robustness.\n  - Reproduction: Submitted as Eval 684 (fixed hparams). Variant with AdamW(wd=2e-4) submitted as Eval 685.\n  - Three ideas (single-change, CNN baseline):\n    1) Optimizer: AdamW with mild weight decay (submitted: 685). Hypothesis: improves generalization with minimal capacity.\n    2) Loss: Huber value loss (δ=1.0) with otherwise default PG. Hypothesis: robust targets help low-capacity CNN.\n    3) Normalization:\
    \ Replace conv‑block activations with GroupNorm+ReLU in the CNN trunk. Hypothesis: stabilizes gradients without head changes.\n  - Protocol: Reproduce baseline → test each idea one at a time with fixed hparams → compare mean±std over 4 seeds. If any idea helps, then test on stronger LN‑ConvLSTM SOTA later.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/cnn_pg_huber.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  CNN + PG with Huber value loss (δ=1.0).\n  Changes only the value loss; keeps default network, optimizer, and PG.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  from defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  # Fix hyperparameters (no sampling)\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      from ray import tune\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n\
    \          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  # Use default optimizer and network (no overrides)\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      observations = batch['observations']   # [B,T,H,W,C]\n      actions = batch['actions']             # [B,T]\n      rewards = batch['rewards']             # [B,T]\n      dones = batch['dones']                 # [B,T]\n      old_values = batch['values']           # [B,T]\n      final_values = batch['final_values']   # [B]\n\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n\n      B, T = observations.shape[:2]\n      obs_flat = observations.reshape(B * T, *observations.shape[2:])\n      dones_flat = dones.reshape(B * T)\n\n      def loss_fn(p):\n          logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(p, obs_flat, dones_flat)\n          logits = logits_flat.reshape(B, T, -1)\n          values = values_flat.reshape(B,\
    \ T)\n\n          logp_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          idx = (jnp.arange(B)[:, None], jnp.arange(T), actions)\n          logp = logp_all[idx]\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages) * logp)\n\n          # Huber value loss\n          residual = values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n          v_loss = jnp.mean(optax.huber_loss(residual, delta=1.0))\n\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * logp_all, axis=-1))\n          return policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * v_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n\n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/cnn_pg_groupnorm.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  CNN + PG with GroupNorm in the CNN trunk.\n\
    \  Single change vs DefaultResidualCNN: insert GroupNorm(num_groups=8) before ReLU in conv blocks.\n  Uses default PG training step and Adam optimizer.\n  \"\"\"\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Optional, Tuple\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      from ray import tune\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  class GNResidualCNN(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      num_groups: int = 8\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          B = x.shape[0]\n\n          # Block 1\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\
    \ use_bias=False)(x)\n          x = nn.GroupNorm(num_groups=self.num_groups)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Block 2 (residual)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', use_bias=False)(x)\n          y = nn.GroupNorm(num_groups=self.num_groups)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', use_bias=False)(y)\n          y = nn.GroupNorm(num_groups=self.num_groups)(y)\n          x = nn.relu(x + y)\n\n          # Block 3\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', use_bias=False)(x)\n          x = nn.GroupNorm(num_groups=self.num_groups)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Block 4 (residual)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', use_bias=False)(x)\n          y = nn.GroupNorm(num_groups=self.num_groups)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', use_bias=False)(y)\n          y = nn.GroupNorm(num_groups=self.num_groups)(y)\n\
    \          x = nn.relu(x + y)\n\n          x = x.reshape((B, -1))\n          x = nn.Dense(256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          # Policy head\n          ph = nn.Dense(64)(x); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          logits = nn.Dense(4)(ph)\n          # Value head\n          vh = nn.Dense(64)(x); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return logits, value, None\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return GNResidualCNN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          num_groups=8\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/stagnation_protocol/next_submit_queue.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Queue after 684/685 finish (respect 2-concurrent limit):\n  - Submit: CNN+PG + Huber value loss (file: submissions/cnn_pg_huber.py)\n  - Submit: CNN+PG + GroupNorm trunk (file: submissions/cnn_pg_groupnorm.py)\n  Fixed hparams: lr=4e-4, ent=0.01, vlc=0.5, BASE_SEED=42. Compare\
    \ vs reproduction.\n  Then:\n  - If either > baseline, run tiny sweep (entropy {0.008,0.01,0.012}) on the winning idea.\n  - Synthesis: Port best idea to LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP SOTA to test transfer.\n```\n\nI will submit the next two experiments once the current CNN baseline runs (684, 685) complete."
thinking_content: "**Reflecting on project actions**\n\nIt looks like we're currently in a stagnation phase and need to take action. The architect's message guides us to follow specific protocols, including a literature review that we’ve completed. We selected the CNN+PG baseline and have already submitted some variants. Now, we need to focus on generating three new ideas based on that baseline. We've queued submissions and received results for entropy-fixed runs. Although we originally ran many experiments, let's concentrate on the CNN baseline moving forward.**Following the research plan**\n\nI’m planning our next steps. First, we can continue summarizing the literature; we've previewed the beginning but should explore all pages. The system indicated there are many earlier references, which is promising. I wonder if we should store a summary in a private memory or create an archive? \n\nNext, we have submitted variants 684 and 685, and I need to propose two new experiments: an entropy\
  \ schedule and GroupNorm. I should note that we need to ensure BASE_SEED is defined clearly for our submissions to work correctly.**Ensuring network definitions**\n\nI need to confirm that we haven't defined \"create_network\" for reproduction; since that's the case, the default will be used. For our third idea, I'm thinking of applying the entropy schedule, adjusting it from 0.012 to 0.010 mid-training within the CNN baseline. \n\nPreviously, when we tried a dynamic schedule, it collapsed into near-zero solves, likely due to the optimizer count retracing. To avoid issues this time, we should implement the schedule with caution, or maybe even opt for a static piecewise constant weighting for the entropy coefficient instead.**Implementing the training schedule**\n\nTo set up the schedule, I need to create a custom training step for the CNN baseline, like we did before. However, we had a major collapse with the dynamic VLC schedule, which could be due to shape choices or JIT issues. In that\
  \ case, we used a dynamic conditional with _get_update_count(opt_state), which might be problematic.\n\nFor the CNN baseline, I’m thinking of avoiding dynamic elements by using a small linear ramp with jnp.where. There’s still some risk here, but I could set the entropy schedule from 15k down to 0.010 while keeping previous issues in mind. To ensure safety, I could tie the schedule to the time dimension during the unroll.**Planning next steps for experiments**\n\nIt’s time to implement our training schedule properly. We need to add 'update_idx' in hyperparameters to track updates, even though the default system may not pass it along. Since dynamic scheduling has led to problems, I'll consider simpler ideas.\n\nFor idea 2, I plan to apply Huber value loss (δ=1.0) on the CNN baseline, despite earlier negative results with SOTA. Idea 3 involves GroupNorm in the CNN trunk, which requires overriding the default network but could significantly improve training. We should also document our literature\
  \ review and summarize our hypotheses in designated files while preparing the code for submission later when slots are available.**Implementing GroupNorm and Huber loss**\n\nI need to create the Flax Module 'GNResidualCNN', which replicates the default but adds GroupNorm after each convolution. For the network, I’ll use 'num_groups=8', but I’m not sure if I need 'use_bias=False' for the convolution layers—probably not necessary. I will write storage files to outline our plans for submitting the Huber and GroupNorm experiments after experiments 684 and 685 finish. \n\nIn the meantime, I’ll summarize key SOTA trends and establish our baseline and plan, focusing on a simple CNN+PG and implementing a training step with Huber value loss. I'll also ensure to define the GroupNorm network properly. Since the current experiment limit is tight, I’ll avoid submissions until there's room. Additionally, I’m considering whether to log or archive our progress for future reflection."
