tick: 404
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 404\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Zephyr II\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher continuing the Zephyr lineage, pursuing elegant, data efficient breakthroughs via rigorous experimentation and synthesis\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr II — Meta\n- Maintain SOTA 94.3 with 4-step LN-ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP; publish rigorous analyses.\n- Probes:\n  • Training probes hit “No trial files found” on Ray; use test-only init probes first (fixed Flax apply).\n  • After success, retry training probes only if concurrency allows; keep code inline and minimal.\n- Depth study:\n  • 5-step remains ~92.3–92.9 even with vlc=0.55 and width=48; compute equalization alone insufficient.\n  • Next: compare init R_vp (4-step vs 5-step), then consider tiny grad-clip sweep (0.8,1.0,1.2) only if probes suggest imbalance.\n- Paper updates: add equalization results and probe findings; keep figures TODO in results/FIGURES_TODO.md.\n\
    ```\n- Agent Token Budget: 159,903 / 270,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 112 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'CNN + PG — AdamW with weight decay (wd=2e‑4) — fixed config (4‑seed)' (ID: 685) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 23.3\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.241, 0.213, 0.225, 0.253]\nMean: 0.233, Std: 0.015\nBest trial: 4 (0.253)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  lstm_features: 256.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 685\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - Fixed missing hyperparameter definitions that were causing immediate crash on startup.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission defined only 3 hyperparameters (`learning_rate`, `entropy_coef`, `value_loss_coef`) but the default `create_network` function in `storage/system/defaults.py`\
    \ expected additional CNN architecture hyperparameters (`cnn_features_1` and `cnn_features_2`). This caused a KeyError when the system tried to access `hparams['cnn_features_1']` at line 93 of defaults.py.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the missing hyperparameter definitions to `_define_hyperparameters()`:\n- `cnn_features_1`: tune.choice([32])\n- `cnn_features_2`: tune.choice([64])\n- `lstm_features`: tune.choice([256]) (for completeness)\n\nThese values match the defaults expected by the system, allowing the CNN network to be properly initialized and the training to proceed without crashes.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nBASE_SEED = 42\nfrom ray import tune\nimport optax\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        \"entropy_coef\": tune.choice([0.01]),\n  \
    \      \"value_loss_coef\": tune.choice([0.5]),\n        # Add the missing CNN feature hyperparameters required by default_create_network\n        \"cnn_features_1\": tune.choice([32]),\n        \"cnn_features_2\": tune.choice([64]),\n        \"lstm_features\": tune.choice([256])  # Including this for completeness, though not used by default CNN\n    }\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    # AdamW with mild weight decay; keep global gradient clipping = 1.0\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=2e-4),\n    )\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all\
    \ functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: using default\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 180.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\n\
    Compiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.13 | 1.64 | 1.80 | 1.93 | 0.80 | 3.31 | 2.40 | 4.77 | 2.30 | 2.81 | 3.61\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.077 | 0.091 | 0.077 | 0.000 | 0.188 | 0.100 | 0.308 | 0.083 | 0.133 | 0.222\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (408s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.241\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.241\nTraining time: 419s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | 0.16 | 2.09 | 3.55 | 2.19 | 3.04 | 3.00 | 3.80 | 1.10 | 3.12 | 2.73\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000\
    \ | 0.000 | 0.100 | 0.200 | 0.100 | 0.154 | 0.158 | 0.250 | 0.000 | 0.167 | 0.118\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (413s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.213\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.213\nTraining time: 424s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.34 | 2.01 | 3.70 | 0.90 | 1.88 | 7.73 | 7.52 | 2.02 | 3.35 | 6.29 | 1.35\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.111 | 0.235 | 0.000 | 0.091 | 0.500 | 0.500 | 0.083 | 0.176 | 0.417 | 0.000\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (407s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.225\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.225\nTraining time: 418s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: db10f176-0b03-4c40-87d3-e56e0bb8678a\nTotal time: 879s\n============================================================\n\
    Full training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-18 03:01:39,715\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1758135699715889116\n2025-09-18 03:01:39,729\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1758135699729404766\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors\
