tick: 405
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/cnn_pg_baseline_results.csv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,title,mean,std,notes\n  684,CNN+PG baseline (fixed hparams),0.247,0.006,reproduction of system DefaultResidualCNN+PG\n  685,CNN+PG + AdamW(wd=2e-4),0.233,0.015,regresses vs baseline\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/stagnation_protocol/report_outline.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stagnation Protocol I — Report Outline (CNN+PG Track)\n  Title (WIP): Simple Changes on a Simple Baseline: Regularization, Robust Targets, and Normalization on CNN+PG for Sokoban RL\n\n  1. Motivation\n  - Station stagnation; we restart from a robust simple baseline (CNN+PG ~25%).\n  - Goal: explore three single-change ideas absent from archive on CNN baseline.\n\n  2. Baseline and Setup\n  - Baseline: DefaultResidualCNN + PG, fixed hparams (lr=4e-4, ent=0.01, vlc=0.5), 4 seeds.\n  - Reproduction: 0.247 ± 0.006 (Eval 684).\n\n  3. Idea A — Optimizer Regularization\n  - Change: Adam → AdamW(wd=2e-4).\n\
    \  - Result: 0.233 ± 0.015 (Eval 685), regression.\n\n  4. Idea B — Robust Value Targets\n  - Change: MSE → Huber(δ=1.0) value loss.\n  - Status: submitted (Eval 686) — pending.\n\n  5. Idea C — Lightweight Normalization\n  - Change: GroupNorm(num_groups=8) in CNN trunk (heads unchanged).\n  - Status: submitted (Eval 687) — pending.\n\n  6. Analysis Plan\n  - Compare mean±std and solve progression curves; discuss why effects differ vs high-capacity SOTA.\n  - If any idea > baseline, run tiny entropy micro-sweep {0.008,0.01,0.012}.\n\n  7. Synthesis Plan\n  - Port promising idea to LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP SOTA and evaluate transfer.\n\n  8. Conclusion (to be filled after results)\n  - Summarize gains/regressions and implications for low-capacity agents under tight budgets.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/cnn_pg_entropy_schedule.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  CNN + PG with a simple entropy schedule (0.012 -> 0.010 at 15k updates).\n  Baseline: DefaultResidualCNN\
    \ + PG. Single change in training_step.\n  Note: Dynamic schedules can be brittle; we test on the simple CNN baseline only.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  from defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  SWITCH_STEP = 15000\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      from ray import tune\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.012]),  # start value; we will switch to 0.010\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def _get_update_count(opt_state):\n      # opt_state is a tuple for chained transforms; find scalar 'count'\n      try:\n          return jnp.asarray(opt_state[1].count)\n      except Exception:\n          leaves = jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(opt_state)\n          for l in leaves:\n\
    \              if isinstance(l, jnp.ndarray) and l.shape == () and l.dtype.kind in (\"i\", \"u\"):\n                  return l\n          return jnp.asarray(0)\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      observations = batch['observations']\n      actions = batch['actions']\n      rewards = batch['rewards']\n      dones = batch['dones']\n      old_values = batch['values']\n      final_values = batch['final_values']\n\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n\n      B, T = observations.shape[:2]\n      obs_flat = observations.reshape(B * T, *observations.shape[2:])\n      dones_flat = dones.reshape(B * T)\n\n      def loss_fn(p):\n          logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(p, obs_flat, dones_flat)\n          logits = logits_flat.reshape(B, T, -1)\n          values = values_flat.reshape(B, T)\n\n          logp_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits,\
    \ axis=-1)\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          idx = (jnp.arange(B)[:, None], jnp.arange(T), actions)\n          logp = logp_all[idx]\n\n          step_count = _get_update_count(opt_state)\n          entropy_coef = jnp.where(step_count < SWITCH_STEP, 0.012, 0.010)\n\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages) * logp)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * logp_all, axis=-1))\n\n          return policy_loss + 0.5 * value_loss - entropy_coef * entropy\n\n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = jax.tree_util.tree_map(lambda a, b: a + b, params, updates)  # apply_updates equivalent\n      return params, opt_state\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/stagnation_protocol/next_submit_queue_2.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Next queue after 686/687\
    \ finish (respect 2-concurrent limit):\n  - CNN+PG + entropy schedule (0.012 -> 0.010 @15k), file: submissions/cnn_pg_entropy_schedule.py\n  - CNN+PG + constant vlc tests: submit two fixed runs with value_loss_coef ∈ {0.45, 0.55} (reuse system defaults with _define_hyperparameters override)\n  Rationale: extend the three-idea set with safe constants and one cautious schedule on the simple baseline.\n```\n\nI’ll wait for 686/687 to finish, then submit the scheduled variants, compare against baseline (684), and draft the short report following the outline above."
thinking_content: '**Progressing with protocols**


  I''m noticing that we previously had "Advantage z-norm" degrade, but we could test our stable baseline again. The protocol mentions it needs to be different from what’s already in the Archive, though it’s possible we''ve already tried some normalization. The archive may not have tested on the CNN baseline specifically, yet it''s still acceptable to proceed. We have three ideas to move forward with: summarizing our baseline results, preparing code for the CNN baseline, and setting up sweeps for loss coefficients.**Preparing code adjustments**


  I''m getting ready to prepare some code by overriding _define_hyperparameters while keeping the default training step intact. The value loss coefficient is already part of my hyperparameters, which is good. I also need to add "GroupNorm," as the code has create_network. Huber training will modify the training step. I can schedule the next queue file for these code changes and create a "station tasks file" too. Lastly, I’ll gather baseline results while considering how to handle our evaluation subset to avoid token overload.**Managing concurrent experiments**


  I’m currently running two experiments, 686 and 687, so I can’t submit more until those finish. The system limits me to two concurrent runs, which can be frustrating. I’ll hold off on submissions for now and write the code modules for the upcoming experiments to store in a pending queue document. It sounds wise to also draft a report outline. I’ll create “cnn_pg_results.csv” to summarize experiments 684 and 685 and update the results file with necessary details.**Planning final actions**


  I’m ready to outline my final actions. First, I’ll write the baseline results summary in both CSV and MD formats while including a note about the baseline I’ve chosen. Next, I’ll prepare code for the CNN entropy schedule in "cnn_pg_entropy_schedule.py," adjusting the entropy coefficient at 15k. I won’t schedule submissions just yet. I also plan to create the "cnn_pg_vlc_fixed_{45,55}" by overriding the value_loss_coef, but since I can''t submit now, I’ll just document this plan. I’ll format the actions as separate YAML blocks for clarity.'
