parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/cnn_pg_entropy_schedule.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  CNN + PG with a simple entropy schedule (0.012 -> 0.010 at 15k updates).\n  Baseline: DefaultResidualCNN + PG. Single change in training_step.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  from defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  SWITCH_STEP = 15000\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      from ray import tune\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.012]),  # start value; will switch to 0.010\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def _get_update_count(opt_state):\n      # opt_state is a tuple for chained transforms; find scalar\
    \ 'count'\n      try:\n          return jnp.asarray(opt_state[1].count)\n      except Exception:\n          leaves = jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(opt_state)\n          for l in leaves:\n              if isinstance(l, jnp.ndarray) and l.shape == () and l.dtype.kind in (\"i\", \"u\"):\n                  return l\n          return jnp.asarray(0)\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      observations = batch['observations']\n      actions = batch['actions']\n      rewards = batch['rewards']\n      dones = batch['dones']\n      old_values = batch['values']\n      final_values = batch['final_values']\n\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n\n      B, T = observations.shape[:2]\n      obs_flat = observations.reshape(B * T, *observations.shape[2:])\n      dones_flat = dones.reshape(B * T)\n\n      def loss_fn(p):\n          logits_flat, values_flat, _ =\
    \ network.apply(p, obs_flat, dones_flat)\n          logits = logits_flat.reshape(B, T, -1)\n          values = values_flat.reshape(B, T)\n\n          logp_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          idx = (jnp.arange(B)[:, None], jnp.arange(T), actions)\n          logp = logp_all[idx]\n\n          step_count = _get_update_count(opt_state)\n          entropy_coef = jnp.where(step_count < SWITCH_STEP, 0.012, 0.010)\n\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages) * logp)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * logp_all, axis=-1))\n\n          return policy_loss + 0.5 * value_loss - entropy_coef * entropy\n\n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n\
    ```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNN + PG — Entropy schedule 0.012→0.010 @15k (fixed, 4‑seed)\"\ntags: \"baseline, cnn, entropy schedule, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Single‑change vs system CNN+PG: entropy starts at 0.012 then drops to 0.010 at 15k updates. Tests whether mild early exploration helps low‑capacity CNN. Other hparams fixed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from submissions.cnn_pg_entropy_schedule import _define_hyperparameters, training_step, BASE_SEED\n  # Use default network/optimizer; only training_step changes.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNN + PG — value_loss_coef=0.45 (fixed, 4‑seed)\"\ntags: \"baseline, cnn, value loss coef, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Constant‑vlc check on simple CNN baseline. Fixed hparams and default CNN/PG; only vlc differs (0.45 vs default 0.50).\"\ncontent: |\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  from ray import tune\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n   \
    \       \"learning_rate\": tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          \"entropy_coef\": tune.choice([0.01]),\n          \"value_loss_coef\": tune.choice([0.45]),\n          \"cnn_features_1\": tune.choice([32]),\n          \"cnn_features_2\": tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/stagnation_protocol/pending_tick406.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Pending (tick 406):\n  - CNN+PG + Entropy schedule 0.012→0.010 @15k (submission id pending)\n  - CNN+PG + constant vlc=0.45\n  Completed:\n  - Baseline: 0.247 ± 0.006 (Eval 684)\n  - AdamW:    0.233 ± 0.015 (Eval 685) — regression\n  - Huber:    0.181 ± 0.005 (Eval 686) — regression\n  - GN trunk: 0.124 ± 0.009 (Eval 687) — regression\n\n  Next:\n  - After these results, run constant vlc=0.55; then draft the short report (≥5 experiments) per outline.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Coordinating experiment submissions**\n\nI’m considering how to handle the submissions for our experiments. The station requested that we write a paper after testing all ideas, so we should hold off on publishing until we have more results. Currently, we can only submit two experiments at a time. We just finished tests 686 and 687, and since we have no concurrent submissions, I’ll go with the entropy schedule and one constant (vlc=0.45) for now. Next time, I can submit the 0.55.**Finalizing experiment submission**\n\nI created a 'next_submit_queue_2' that includes the schedule and constant vlc tests. I’ll go with the schedule plus vlc=0.45. I have 'cnn_pg_entropy_schedule.py', but I noticed the 'training_step' still uses manual updates. I’d rather use optax.apply_updates to avoid potential issues. I can quickly resave a corrected version before submission, but we'll be importing 'submissions.cnn_pg_entropy_schedule' instead. I need to check if we've already submitted\
  \ the schedule. It looks like we haven't submitted it yet.**Updating and submitting the schedule**\n\nI can now proceed to update the schedule file and submit the schedule along with vlc=0.45. First, I’ll correct 'cnn_pg_entropy_schedule.py' by ensuring it uses optax.apply_updates, including the necessary import for optax. After that, I'll submit the schedule run and the constant vlc=0.45. I might need to create new content for this run that defines the hyperparameters with 'value_loss_coef': [0.45], including 'cnn_features' keys. The time budget seems fine, so I'll update the results log once everything is completed.**Planning submissions and updates**\n\nWe might be at our concurrency limit, so I'll only submit two right now. After that, I can update 'stagnation_protocol/report_outline.md' with the latest idea statuses. Here’s what I need to do: \n\nFirst, I’ll write to the storage to update the schedule file, then submit the schedule and the CNN+PG constant vlc of 0.45. I’ll also write\
  \ to 'stagnation_protocol/pending_tick406.md' to take notes. \n\nFor the content, I’ll import necessary modules and define hyperparameters for learning rates and coefficients, ensuring I don’t overshadow anything. Then I’ll finalize the content blocks!"
