    : tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/stagnation_protocol/reflection_tick407.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Reflection (tick 407)\n  - Simple CNN+PG baseline reproduced (0.247). Three single-change ideas tested:\n    • AdamW(wd=2e-4): 0.233 (regresses)\n    • Huber value: 0.181 (regresses)\n    • GroupNorm trunk: 0.124 (regresses)\n  - Interpretation: On a low-capacity CNN, default PG settings appear well-calibrated; added regularization or robustifying reduces effective learning signal.\n  - Pending: Entropy schedule 0.012→0.010@15k and constant vlc=0.45. Next queue: constant vlc=0.55 (prepared file).\n  - Plan: Complete constants-only grid (vlc ∈ {0.45,0.50,0.55}); if all regress/plateau, finalize report with ≥5 experiments (baseline + 4 variants) and clear negative results. Then, optionally test transfer of the “best of the worst” (if any) to LN‑ConvLSTM to confirm lack of benefit at higher capacity.\n```\n\nI’ll submit vlc=0.55 once a slot frees\
    \ (two are running: 690, 691)."
thinking_content: "**Analyzing experiment requirements**\n\nI need to consider that the protocol requires at least five experiments, while I currently have four plus a baseline. We should also focus on writing the paper after we finish. The station is in a holding pattern. I think I should submit additional experiments soon, but maybe I’ll wait for the two pending results first. In the meantime, I can prepare a writing skeleton for the paper and update the results table. I need to include the entropy sweep data too.**Clarifying experiment data**\n\nIt seems I need to remember that results 678 and 679 were for PG with LN-ConvLSTM, used for the SOTA track, showing 93.6 and 92.8. However, I need to keep these separate from CNN baseline results to avoid confusion. I should log the new CNN results: 684 (baseline 0.247), 685 (0.233), 686 (0.181), and 687 (0.124). I plan to propose additional experiments with a constant VLC of 0.55 and adjust the learning rate between 3e-4 and 4e-4 for single changes.**Updating\
  \ experiment scripts**\n\nI’m thinking we should adjust the 'cnn_pg_entropy_schedule.py' script to use `optax.apply_updates` instead of the manual tree map since we've done that in previous versions. It’s great to confirm that we've switched to using `apply_updates` for consistency. We need to make sure 'BASE_SEED=42' is set for reproducibility as well. After that, I can start preparing the paper's content for submission to the Archive. It'll summarize the baseline reproduction, any negative results, and insights, emphasizing that even negative outcomes can be useful.**Drafting paper while waiting**\n\nWe’re currently mid-run on experiments, but I can start drafting the paper and note that we’re pending results from experiments 690 and 691. It’s probably best to finalize it once those results come in. \n\nThe Automatic System Tips recommend printing logs, so updating the training step to include step_count and maybe R_vp sounds good, despite the simple CNN baseline not having recurrence.\
  \ We might include some 'return' stats as well. \n\nFor now, I should prepare the 'cnn_pg_vlc_55' file for submission and ensure the results file includes the latest data as well.**Preparing documentation and actions**\n\nI think we should create a 'paper draft' in Private Memory for now, since that’s accessible. I'll write to storage the 'cnn_pg_results_table.csv' to include baseline results and variants. Next, we'll prepare the 'cnn_pg_vlc_55' submission file, while defining 'cnn_pg_entropy_constant_010' for the explicit baseline.\n\nI also need to check if I can submit the constant VLC=0.55, but it looks like I might need to queue it since two experiments are running. Lastly, I’ll reflect on our previously generated ideas and write that to storage, then execute the actions we've outlined."
