role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNN + PG — value_loss_coef=0.55 (fixed, 4‑seed)\"\ntags: \"baseline, cnn, value loss coef, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Complete constants-only grid on the simple CNN+PG baseline. Fixed hparams and default CNN/PG; only vlc differs (0.55 vs default 0.50).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from submissions.cnn_pg_vlc_55 import _define_hyperparameters, BASE_SEED\n  # Use default network/optimizer/training; only vlc fixed to 0.55.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/cnn_pg_results_table.csv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,title,mean,std,notes\n  684,CNN+PG baseline (fixed hparams),0.247,0.006,reproduction of DefaultResidualCNN+PG\n  685,CNN+PG + AdamW(wd=2e-4),0.233,0.015,regresses vs baseline\n  686,CNN+PG + Huber value loss (δ=1.0),0.181,0.005,strong regression\n  687,CNN+PG + GroupNorm trunk (GN8),0.124,0.009,strong regression\n  690,CNN+PG — Entropy schedule 0.012→0.010 @15k,0.239,0.016,slight\
    \ regression vs baseline\n  691,CNN+PG — value_loss_coef=0.45,0.244,0.012,near baseline\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Restarting from a Simple Baseline: Regularization, Robust Targets, and Normalization on CNN+PG for Sokoban RL (Stagnation Protocol I)\"\ntags: \"stagnation, baseline, cnn, policy gradient, negative results, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Following Stagnation Protocol I, we restart from the system CNN+PG baseline (~25% mean solve) and test three single‑change ideas absent from the archive for this baseline: AdamW weight decay, Huber value loss, and GroupNorm in the CNN trunk. Across six 4‑seed experiments (including an entropy schedule and constant value_loss_coef variants), all modifications regress or match baseline within noise. We provide a self‑contained setup, results with evaluation IDs, and analysis of why low‑capacity CNNs appear signal‑limited under the station budget. These negative results guide future work\
    \ toward capacity/architecture rather than regularization on simple baselines.\"\ncontent: |\n  1. Motivation and Protocol\n  The Station entered stagnation. Per the Architect's Stagnation Protocol I, we:\n  (i) reviewed archive results; (ii) chose a simple, robust baseline; (iii) proposed three new ideas; (iv) reproduced baseline and ran one‑change variants; (v) synthesized findings; (vi) report all outcomes (including negatives).\n\n  2. Baseline and Setup (Self‑Contained)\n  Task: 8×8 Sokoban; score = mean test solve over 4 seeds, each ≤50M steps or 45 minutes. \n  Baseline model: DefaultResidualCNN (system default) + Policy Gradient (PG) with GAE.\n  Fixed hyperparameters: learning_rate=4e‑4, entropy_coef=0.01, value_loss_coef=0.50; cnn_features_1=32, cnn_features_2=64; BASE_SEED=42 ⇒ seeds {42,43,44,45}.\n\n  Training loop pseudocode (PG with GAE):\n  - For each update:\n    • Collect rollout (64 envs × 20 steps): (obs, act, rew, done, old_values, final_value).\n    • Compute advantages\
    \ = GAE(rew, old_values, done; γ=0.97, λ=0.97, bootstrap=final_value).\n    • returns = old_values + advantages.\n    • Forward pass to get logits, values for all steps.\n    • policy_loss = −E[stop(advantages)·logπ(act|obs)]\n    • value_loss  = 0.5·E[(values − stop(returns))^2]\n    • entropy     = E[H(π(.|obs))]\n    • total_loss  = policy_loss + vlc·value_loss − ent_coef·entropy\n    • θ ← Adam(θ, ∇ total_loss) with global grad‑clip(1.0).\n  - Network: 4 residual conv blocks (32→64), shared MLP(256), policy/value heads(64).\n\n  3. Experiments (4 seeds each; Evaluation IDs)\n  Baseline reproduction:\n  - Eval 684 — CNN+PG baseline (fixed hparams): 0.247 ± 0.006\n\n  Idea A — Optimizer Regularization:\n  - Eval 685 — AdamW(wd=2e‑4): 0.233 ± 0.015 (regression)\n\n  Idea B — Robust Value Targets:\n  - Eval 686 — Huber value loss (δ=1.0): 0.181 ± 0.005 (strong regression)\n\n  Idea C — Lightweight Normalization:\n  - Eval 687 — GroupNorm trunk (GN8): 0.124 ± 0.009 (strong regression)\n\
    \n  Constants and mild schedule for context:\n  - Eval 691 — value_loss_coef=0.45 (constant): 0.244 ± 0.012 (≈ baseline)\n  - Eval 690 — Entropy schedule 0.012→0.010 @15k: 0.239 ± 0.016 (slight regression)\n  - (Pending) CNN+PG value_loss_coef=0.55 (constant) submitted — will be appended post‑completion.\n\n  4. Results Summary and Interpretation\n  - Every modification either matches or underperforms the ~25% baseline; strongest regressions are Huber and GroupNorm.\n  - Entropy scheduling is neutral/slightly negative at this capacity.\n  - Conclusion: On a low‑capacity CNN under tight budget, the system defaults are already near an effective signal/noise balance. Added regularization and robustifying losses reduce effective learning signal, hurting solve rate.\n\n  5. Relation to Archive and Synthesis\n  Archive trends show breakthroughs arise from recurrent capacity, receptive field (dilation), and bottleneck efficiency with appropriate heads (ConvLSTM + attention), or algorithmic\
    \ synergy (PPO with simple heads). Our negative results indicate that, absent such capacity/architectural priors, regularization tweaks on a simple CNN do not unlock planning, aligning with prior evidence that architecture dominates under this budget.\n\n  6. Reproducibility Checklist\n  - Fixed seeds and hparams; station defaults for unmodified parts.\n  - Self‑contained pseudocode and exact evaluation IDs provided.\n  - All experiments use 4 seeds and the Station’s evaluation harness.\n\n  7. Follow‑Up\n  - Complete constants‑only vlc grid by adding vlc=0.55 (pending); report if any deviation helps.\n  - If any constant proves competitive, port to LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP (94.3%) for transfer; otherwise, re‑focus on architectural capacity (e.g., minimal ConvGRU/ConvLSTM on top of CNN) as the next baseline ladder rung.\n\n  Acknowledgments: Thanks to prior lineages for the ConvLSTM, dilation, bottleneck, and PPO insights that frame this study.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Clarifying research steps**


  I’m thinking about the method. For step 5, I should note any negative results, and for step 6, writing a report for the Archive Room with those results is essential. I need to respect the station actions and use the /execute_action commands carefully since they’ll be executed. It seems like we can submit everything now since there are no running experiments. The latest output shows no ongoing experiments, which aligns with what I see.**Reviewing experiment submissions**


  At tick 407, I see there’s no "Running Experiments" entry. Instead, I find the "Submitted Evaluations" list. Previously, at tick 406, experiments 690 and 691 were running, but now their results have arrived, updating the list. Since the "Running Experiments" table is absent, we can submit the next two experiments while adhering to the 2-concurrency rule. I’ll submit the vlc 0.55 constant for the CNN baseline, even though we have the SOTA convlstm result already. I’m not sure about submitting the constant entropy of 0.01 since it''s used in the baseline.**Planning the research paper**


  I need to compile a CSV for all CNN results and write a paper summarizing the baseline and negative results. The Archive requires a minimum of 5 experiments, and since we have 6, I’ll provide the IDs and their mean ± std. I want to emphasize the novelty, noting that there''s a negative synergy with the simple CNN baseline, where robustifying degrades performance. I’ll also include a pseudocode snippet for the CNN+PG training loop, along with minimal self-contained details. It might be useful to add a follow-up plan, though that’s optional. I’ll use the /execute_action command to access the archive and create the paper using YAML. Plus, I should consider updating tokens to save some, but it''s not crucial right now.**Organizing experiment data**


  I want to gather the experiments and create a table with the results. Here’s what I have: Eval 684 (baseline) at 0.247 ± 0.006, 685 (AdamW) at 0.233 ± 0.015, 686 (Huber) at 0.181 ± 0.005, 687 (GroupNorm) at 0.124 ± 0.009, 690 (Entropy schedule) at 0.239 ± 0.016, and 691 (vlc=0.45) at 0.244 ± 0.012. We have six experiments total, satisfying report requirements. Since no improvements came from synthesis, I might consider adding a short test on the SOTA with constant unicode.**Preparing for submission**


  I already completed some steps, but to remain consistent with Protocol, we can propose a port but not run it. The Archive requires a minimum of 5 experiments, which we have. So, let’s proceed by submitting the CNN+PG vlc=0.55 fixed-run and storing the results in a CSV with IDs 690 and 691 included.


  Next, I need to create the Archive paper with a suitable title and abstract, along with methods, pseudocode, and an experiments table. I’ll also plan a follow-up and keep the length moderate. I’ll craft commands for submission and take care to quote titles correctly in the YAML content.'
