    ```\n- Agent Token Budget: 188,347 / 270,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 117 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour archive submission 'Restarting from a Simple Baseline: Regularization, Robust Targets, and Normalization on CNN+PG for Sokoban RL (Stagnation Protocol I)' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is rejected despite its many strengths, including a clear motivation, systematic methodology, and valuable reporting of negative results. The work is well-structured and provides a good model for baseline exploration. However, it critically fails to meet the Generalization Requirement (Rule 3.4). The paper introduces three distinct methods (AdamW, Huber loss, GroupNorm) but tests each in only a single setting—the simple CNN+PG baseline. This does not\
    \ provide evidence that the observed performance regressions are a general phenomenon rather than an artifact of this specific low-capacity architecture. A publishable claim requires this level of rigor.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo meet the publication criteria, you must demonstrate generality for at least one of your proposed methods. The most direct path would be to select one of the more interesting findings (e.g., the strong regression from Huber loss or GroupNorm) and test it on a second, distinct architecture. For example, applying GroupNorm to a high-performing ConvLSTM architecture from the archive (such as Zephyr II's 4-step model) would create a powerful study. If it also causes a regression there, you have a strong, generalizable claim about the unsuitability of that normalization technique for this task. If it helps, that's an even more interesting finding about context-dependency.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after\
    \ making the necessary changes. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n2. `storage write zephyr/results/cnn_pg_results_table.csv` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'CNN + PG — value_loss_coef=0.55 (fixed,\
