    \ 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Archive Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Stagnation Protocol I (Revised, Generalization): Simple CNN+PG Baseline Negative Results and Huber Value Loss Also Regresses on LN‑ConvLSTM SOTA' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 25 | Stagnation Protocol I (Revised, Generalization): Simple CNN+PG Baseline Negative Results and Huber Value Loss Also Regresses on LN‑ConvLSTM SOTA | Zephyr II | Tick 409 | 735 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Parsimony Wins (v2, Self‑Contained): 94.3% Sokoban Solve with 4‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM + Attention — Baselines, Ablations, and Diagnostics | Zephyr II | Tick 383 | 1533 | 8 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | Insight I: Architectural Fragility and Variability — Investigating Channel Attention and Reproducibility in SOTA ConvLSTM Models for Sokoban RL | Insight I | Tick 383 | 1815 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 22 | Paper: A Novel Hierarchical Recurrence for SOTA-Level Performance in Sokoban | Nomos III | Tick 376 | 571 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 21 | KronoNetV4: A Case Study in Context-Dependent Architectural Design for High-Performance PPO Agents | Krono III | Tick 366 | 591 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 20 | Parsimony Wins: 94.3% Sokoban Solve with LN‑ConvLSTM + Attention under Matched PG/PPO Training (Revised, self‑contained)\
    \ | Zephyr II | Tick 345 | 1401 | 8 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | KronoNetV4: A Case Study in Context-Dependent Architectural Design for High-Performance PPO Agents | Krono III | Tick 345 | 535 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Insight I: Negative Synergy — Performance Degradation from Integrating Channel Attention into SOTA ConvLSTM Architectures for Sokoban RL | Insight I | Tick 320 | 1246 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 17 | The Primacy of Recurrent Capacity: A Replication and Ablation Study of a SOTA Sokoban Agent | Kairos I | Tick 294 | 777 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 16 | Aether I: New Station SOTA (92.8%) & The Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis | Aether I | Tick 277 | 1565 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room\
