    \ 5‑step shows lower R_vp, indicating weaker value credit into the trunk.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from submissions.probe_init_rvp_4v5 import test, BASE_SEED\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/5step_gradclip_results.csv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,title,mean,std,notes\n  706,PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — grad‑clip=0.8,0.918,0.004,still below 4‑step SOTA 0.943\n  707,PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — grad‑clip=1.2,0.923,0.008,still below 4‑step SOTA 0.943\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/depth_study_notes.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Depth Study: 5‑step vs 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) under PG (fixed config)\n  Evidence (update counts from logs):\n  - 4‑step (e.g., Evals 512/670): ~39062 updates in ~2700s.\n  - 5‑step (this study):\n    • Eval 706 (clip=0.8): ~32601–32801 updates in ~2710–2727s.\n    • Eval 707 (clip=1.2): ~32501–33101 updates in ~2708–2730s.\n  ⇒ 5‑step performs ~16% fewer SGD updates within the 45‑min\
    \ budget.\n\n  Scores:\n  - 4‑step SOTA: 0.943 mean.\n  - 5‑step: 0.918 (clip=0.8), 0.923 (clip=1.2). Pending control clip=1.0.\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - Deeper recurrence reduces update throughput, likely offsetting any representational gain under the wall‑clock cap.\n  - Grad‑clip tuning (0.8↔1.2) does not close the gap; if control clip=1.0 matches, we conclude compute budget favors 4‑step depth.\n\n  Next:\n  - Run control (clip=1.0) — submitted.\n  - Run init R_vp probe (4 vs 5) — submitted; if R_vp(5) < R_vp(4), it supports weaker value credit into trunk for 5‑step at init.\n  - Draft short addendum with throughput + R_vp findings.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 25}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum #3: 5‑step grad‑clip sweep results and update‑throughput analysis\"\ncontent: |\n  Depth study update (PG, LN‑ConvLSTM(64), fixed config):\n  - 5‑step grad‑clip=0.8 (Eval 706): 0.918 ± 0.004\n  - 5‑step grad‑clip=1.2 (Eval 707): 0.923 ± 0.008\n  Both remain\
    \ below 4‑step SOTA (0.943). From logs, 5‑step performs ~32501–33101 updates vs ~39062 for 4‑step in the same wall‑clock (≈16% fewer updates).\n  Interpretation: deeper recurrence reduces effective SGD steps under the fixed budget; clip tuning does not recover the loss. Control (clip=1.0) is running; R_vp (init value:policy trunk grad ratio) probe submitted to test value‑credit imbalance. We’ll append those results next.\n```"
