parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/5step_gradclip_results.csv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,title,mean,std,notes\n  706,PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — grad‑clip=0.8,0.918,0.004,below 4‑step SOTA 0.943; ~32601–32801 updates\n  707,PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — grad‑clip=1.2,0.923,0.008,below 4‑step SOTA 0.943; ~32501–33101 updates\n  712,PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — grad‑clip=1.0 (control),0.916,0.008,confirms clip tuning doesn’t close the gap\n  716,PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(56) — compute‑equalized (ratio=0.26, clip=1.0),0.928,0.007,updates ~32.1k–35.8k; improved but <39k\n  718,PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(80) — heavy compute control,0.920,0.011,updates ~30601–30701; lower score supports throughput hypothesis\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(48) — compute‑equalized v2 (bottleneck=0.24, clip=1.0)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, convlstm, compute equalization, recurrence\"\nabstract: \"Further lighten 5‑step\
    \ to push update throughput toward ~39k. Fixed PG config; steps=5, convlstm_features=48, bottleneck_ratio=0.24, global grad‑clip=1.0. Tests if throughput recovery narrows the gap to 4‑step SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from submissions.submission_pg_5step_clip1p0 import training_step, create_optimizer, BASE_SEED\n  from submissions.submission_pg_quadstep import PG_Stepped_AttnGap\n  from ray import tune\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([48]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.24]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([5]),\n          'grad_clip': tune.choice([1.0]),\n\
    \      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 25}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum #7: Throughput control confirms hypothesis — 4‑step width=80 drops to 92.0\"\ncontent: |\n  Result for the throughput‑control run (Eval 718):\n  - 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM with convlstm_features=80 (heavier compute) scored 0.920 ± 0.011.\n  - Logs show ~30.6–30.7k updates (vs ~39k typical for 4‑step SOTA).\n  Alongside the 5‑step compute‑equalized improvement (Eval 716: 0.928 ± 0.007; mid‑30k updates), this strengthens the conclusion that\
    \ update throughput under the wall‑clock cap is the primary driver of performance differences, rather than recurrence depth per se. We have submitted a further‑lightened 5‑step (48ch, bottleneck=0.24) to push updates closer to ~39k; we will append results and update counts once complete.\n```"
