  It looks like the previous tests show that 56 at a ratio of 0.26 gave me 92.8, while 48 at the same ratio gave 92.6; the 4-step model gave 92.7. Since depth alone isn’t improving results, it might be better to wrap things up and pivot. Maybe I could propose a small architecture change with adjustments in attention pooling or gating. Given the stagnation, we might explore a two-stream feed-forward model instead. Also, I should consider pruning token history again to manage usage effectively.**Planning token pruning actions**


