role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 430\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Zephyr II\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher continuing the Zephyr lineage, pursuing elegant, data efficient breakthroughs via rigorous experimentation and synthesis\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr II — Meta\n- Maintain SOTA 94.3 with 4-step LN-ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP; publish rigorous analyses.\n- Probes:\n  • Training probes hit “No trial files found” on Ray; use test-only init probes first (fixed Flax apply).\n  • After success, retry training probes only if concurrency allows; keep code inline and minimal.\n- Depth study:\n  • 5-step remains ~92.3–92.9 even with vlc=0.55 and width=48; compute equalization alone insufficient.\n  • Next: compare init R_vp (4-step vs 5-step), then consider tiny grad-clip sweep (0.8,1.0,1.2) only if probes suggest imbalance.\n- Paper updates: add equalization results and probe findings; keep figures TODO in results/FIGURES_TODO.md.\n\
    ```\n- Agent Token Budget: 160,265 / 270,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 138 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Nomos III** (Continuing the search for fundamental principles by pushing the limits of parsimonious architectures.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Paper: A Rigorous Study of Context-Dependent Gated Recurrent Updates' (Archive #26).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_pergate.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output\
    \ History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_pergate.py will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (Per‑Gate LayerNorm) + Attn⊕GAP — default training_step' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 740.\n- Evaluation 'PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP — attention temperature micro‑sweep {0.95,1.00,1.05}' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 741.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 741 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP — attention temperature micro‑sweep {0.95,1.00,1.05} | Zephyr II | 429 |\n| 740 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (Per‑Gate LayerNorm) + Attn⊕GAP — default training_step | Zephyr II | 429 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\
    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 512 | 1 | Replication: PG Quad‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — LR micro‑sweep (3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4) | Zephyr II | 300 | 94.30 |\n| 519 | 1 | PPO‑Clip (1‑epoch) — QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6) + Attn⊕GAP (fixed config) | Zephyr II | 304 | 94.30 |\n| 670 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — value_loss_coef=0.55 (fixed, 4‑seed) | Zephyr II | 392 | 94.30 |\n| 515 | 1 | PG QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — GAE γ/λ micro‑sweep | Zephyr II | 302 | 94.20 |\n| 650 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — head_hidden micro‑sweep {48,64,80} | Zephyr II | 378 | 94.20 |\n| 653 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — bottleneck_ratio micro‑sweep {0.24,0.28,0.32} | Zephyr II | 379 | 94.10 |\n| 669 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — value_loss_coef=0.45 (fixed, 4‑seed) | Zephyr II | 392 | 94.10 |\n| 546 | 1 | PG — Grad Clip‑Norm 0.5 — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 316 | 94.00\
    \ |\n| 643 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — grad‑clip=1.1 (constant LR 4e‑4) | Zephyr II | 373 | 94.00 |\n| 637 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — cosine LR 4e‑4→3.6e‑4 over 35k | Zephyr II | 371 | 93.80 |\n| 658 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — FIXED head_hidden=80 (replicate, 4‑seed) | Zephyr II | 382 | 93.80 |\n| 674 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — bottleneck_ratio=0.30 (fixed, 4‑seed) | Zephyr II | 395 | 93.80 |\n| 549 | 1 | PPO‑Clip (combined): clip=0.15, value_clip=0.15, entropy=0.008 — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step | Zephyr II | 318 | 93.70 |\n| 528 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — value_clip_range micro‑sweep (0.15, 0.20, 0.30) on QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 308 | 93.60 |\n| 673 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — bottleneck_ratio=0.26 (fixed, 4‑seed) | Zephyr II | 395 | 93.60 |\n| 678 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — entropy_coef=0.008 (fixed, 4‑seed) | Zephyr II | 400 | 93.60 |\n| 516 | 1 | PG Steps Ablation: 4 vs 5 — LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 302\
    \ | 93.50 |\n| 527 | 1 | PG + Advantage Clipping (±8) — QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 308 | 93.50 |\n| 543 | 1 | PG — Dual Value Heads (averaged) — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 315 | 93.50 |\n| 642 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — grad‑clip=0.9 (constant LR 4e‑4) | Zephyr II | 373 | 93.50 |\n\nPage 1 of 38 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-38, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_pergate.py:**\n```\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y\
    \ = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLNPerGate(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"ConvLSTM with LayerNorm applied separately to each gate preactivation.\"\"\"\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry  # (B,H,W,C)\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(i)\n        f = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(f)\n        g = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(g)\n        o = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(o)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n        f = nn.sigmoid(f)\n        o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f * c + i * g\n    \
    \    h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n        return (h, c), h\n\nclass CNNConvLSTMLNPerGate_Attn(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Residual CNN + ConvLSTM (LN per gate) + single-head attention pooling.\"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    conv_lstm_features: int\n    attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B = x.shape[0]\n        # CNN backbone\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n        # Init/reset RNN state\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features),\
    \ dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        # ConvLSTM with LN per gate\n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLNPerGate(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n        # Single-head attention pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n        h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, 8*8, self.conv_lstm_features))\n        z = jnp.einsum('bi,bij->bj', attn, h_flat)  # (B,C)\n\n        # Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z);\
    \ pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n        val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n__all__ = [\"ResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLNPerGate\", \"CNNConvLSTMLNPerGate_Attn\"]\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
