role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zephyr II, in the Research Counter. Recap: Two controlled SOTA-adjacent runs are now queued: per-gate LayerNorm ConvLSTM (ID 740) and attention-temperature micro-sweep on the SOTA head (ID 741). Earlier two-stream/GRU pivots underperformed (~0.59–0.60). I’ll stage a corrected “per-gate + stepped” SOTA-style network to submit as soon as a slot frees.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_pergate_stepped.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Per-gate LayerNorm ConvLSTM with internal multi-step recurrence (steps=4),\n  SOTA-like trunk and Attn⊕GAP head. Uses default training_step.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax.nn as jnn\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # Import the per-gate ConvLSTM cell\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_pergate import ConvLSTMCellLNPerGate\n\n  # Hyperparameter space (consumed by the station; tune.choice lists used upstream)\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      from ray import tune\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          # fixed attn_temp = 1.0 (can sweep later)\n      }\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n\
    \                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class PG_Pergate_Stepped_AttnGAP(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      steps: int = 4\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN trunk\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n\n          # RNN state init/reset\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Multi-step ConvLSTM (LayerNorm per gate inside cell)\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLNPerGate(self.convlstm_features)\n          h_out = None\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = cell((h, c), x)\n          rnn_state\
    \ = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          # Attn ⊕ GAP pooling\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = jnn.softmax(attn_logits / self.attn_temp, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          # Heads\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh\
    \ = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      # Map hparams to module; maintain SOTA-like defaults\n      return PG_Pergate_Stepped_AttnGAP(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n\n  # Use default training_step and optimizer from the system\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      import optax\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage\
    \ write zephyr/results/pending_next_tick.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Next tick plan:\n  - If Eval 740 fails (bad class name/arg mapping), resubmit using submission_pergate_stepped.py (internal stepped net, correct per-gate cell).\n  - If Eval 741 (attn_temp sweep) completes, log the best temp and, if >= SOTA parity, confirm with fixed run; otherwise, revert temp to 1.0.\n  - If both underperform, pause architecture pivots and finalize the Depth-vs-Throughput analysis capsule for Archive (already drafted), then run one tiny SOTA-adjacent head_hidden {48,64} confirmation.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Preparing for updates**\n\nI think we should log the content and prepare to update the code, particularly making sure the correct class import is in place for the pergate network. The file specifies the class name, but we used an unknown alias. We can't modify the previous submission since it’s already at 740, but I can prepare an updated one to resubmit if necessary. I need to stick to minimal responses and consider what instructions to follow, especially regarding including identity and reflection.**Creating a concise update plan**\n\nI’m thinking we can outline a clear plan to address the next steps. First, I need to note the corrected class name: CNNConvLSTMLNPerGate_Attn, and if submission 740 fails, we’ll resubmit with this correct import. Since the architecture's baseline is poor, I should also implement fallback to the SOTA micro-sweeps, tracking results. I'll pre-build the updated submission while ensuring to adopt \"rank score\" to compare SOTA. Finally, it’s\
  \ crucial to ensure accuracy in parameter names for the new code submission.**Detailing network setup steps**\n\nI need to include 'convlstm_features' in the hyperparameters and then update the create_network call to use that feature along with the other parameters. It seems like the previous TwoStream approach included steps, but the current class only uses a single ConvLSTM step, which isn’t ideal for performance. The system's default training step appears to process the entire batch flattened, passing the dones mask across. I need to remember how the previous SOTA's network handled steps but did not do so across time. It’s a bit tricky!**Planning for a new network implementation**\n\nI noticed that the SOTA utilized multi-step ConvLSTM within a single call to capture planning efficiently, but the pergate network only supports a single step, which is likely to result in poor performance. I could create a wrapper class using ConvLSTMCellLNPerGate with multiple steps to mimic the stepped\
  \ pattern. I’ll call the new module \"PG_Stepped_Pergate_AttnGAP\" with attention pooling and a default training step, all while ensuring it fits the system’s recognized class names. Let’s prepare the submission with this setup!**Implementing updated submission and planning**\n\nI’m merging our actions and preparing to submit the corrected per-gate stepped network. Since we have experiments currently running, I’ll focus on writing the new submission file instead of immediate submission. I’ll create “zephyr/submissions/submission_pergate_stepped.py” and include the relevant code, ensuring proper imports and defining modules. \n\nI'll draft a pending file for next steps and set our plan to resubmit later after checking for available slots. The aim is to keep it concise while confirming identity and action recap."
