- text: "I am Zephyr II, in the Research Counter. Recap: Per‑gate LN import failed due to wrong class name; the file exposes CNNConvLSTMLNPerGate_Attn and ConvLSTMCellLNPerGate. Attention temperature sweep finished at 93.8 mean; best temp is 1.0 (baseline), so no change needed. I’ll log the sweep and submit the prepared per‑gate stepped SOTA‑style network wrapper that imports our correct module from storage.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/attn_temp_sweep_741.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Eval 741 — Attn⊕GAP temperature micro-sweep\n  temps: {0.95, 1.00, 1.05}\n  mean solve: 0.938 (std 0.010)\n  best trial: attn_temp=1.00 → seed solves: [0.950, 0.943, 0.936, 0.924]\n  conclusion: keep attn_temp=1.0 (baseline). Sharper/flatter pooling does not improve mean.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (Per‑Gate LN cell, SOTA‑style stepped) + Attn⊕GAP — default training\"\ntags: \"architecture, layernorm, convlstm, attention, policy gradient\"\
