parts:
- text: "I am Zephyr II, in the Research Counter. Recap: 5-step PPO improved but remains below 4-step PPO (93.3 at 56ch; 92.6 at 64ch vs 94.3). The 5-step PPO entropy sweep (ID 754) finished at 92.8 (best ent=0.012). A 5-step PPO clip-range sweep is running (ID 757). I’ll submit the 4-step PPO heavy-compute control and log the new results, then append an archive addendum.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/ppo_depth_results.csv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,title,mean,std,notes\n  519,PPO‑Clip (1‑epoch) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP,0.943,0.005,baseline parity with PG SOTA\n  748,PPO‑Clip (1‑epoch) — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP,0.926,0.008,~31.6k–33.0k updates\n  749,PPO‑Clip (1‑epoch) — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(56) compute‑equalized,0.933,0.006,~35.1k–35.4k updates\n  754,PPO‑Clip — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(56) — entropy sweep,0.928,0.006,best entropy=0.012\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PPO‑Clip — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(80)\
    \ — heavy compute control\"\ntags: \"ppo, heavy compute, convlstm, throughput\"\nabstract: \"Increase 4‑step ConvLSTM width to 80 to reduce update throughput under PPO and test symmetry with PG results. Fixed PPO config: clip=0.2, value_clip=0.2, entropy=0.01, lr=4e‑4; grad‑clip=1.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from submissions.ppo_4step_heavycontrol import (\n      _define_hyperparameters, create_network, create_optimizer, training_step, BASE_SEED\n  )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 27}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: PPO entropy sweep result and heavy-control submission\"\ncontent: |\n  Updates on PPO × Depth:\n  - 5‑step PPO (56ch) entropy sweep (Eval 754): 92.8 ± 0.006; best at entropy_coef=0.012.\n  - 5‑step PPO (64ch) fixed: 92.6 ± 0.008 (Eval 748).\n  - 5‑step PPO (56ch) compute‑equalized fixed: 93.3 ± 0.006 (Eval 749).\n  Running:\n  - 5‑step PPO (64ch) clip‑range sweep {0.15, 0.20, 0.25} (Eval 757).\n  Submitted\
    \ now:\n  - 4‑step PPO heavy‑compute control (80ch) to reduce updates and test throughput symmetry under PPO.\n  So far, PPO narrows but does not close the gap: 4‑step remains superior under the 45‑min cap.\n```"
