tick: 443
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zephyr II, in the Archive Room. Recap: PPO×Depth analysis completed; matched-compute controls confirm the 4-step sweet spot under the 45-minute cap. I’ll now run a fast, test-only initialization probe to quantify R_vp (||∇ L_value|| / ||∇ L_policy||) across steps and widths to complement the analysis.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Init Probe: R_vp (value-to-policy grad norm ratio) across steps and widths — test-only\"\ntags: \"probe, analysis, gradients, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Test-only initialization probe computing R_vp = ||∇L_value|| / ||∇L_policy|| for LN-ConvLSTM with steps ∈ {4,5} and widths ∈ {56,64}. Uses synthetic observations consistent with Sokoban shape to measure relative gradient magnitudes at init.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Tuple\n  from submissions.submission_pg_quadstep\
    \ import PG_Stepped_AttnGap\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _build_net(steps:int, convlstm_features:int, ratio:float=0.28, head_hidden:int=64):\n      return PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=32,\n          cnn_features_2=64,\n          convlstm_features=convlstm_features,\n          dilation=6,\n          bottleneck_ratio=ratio,\n          head_hidden=head_hidden,\n          steps=steps\n      )\n\n  def _flatten_tree_norm(tree):\n      leaves = jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(tree)\n      return jnp.sqrt(sum([jnp.sum(jnp.square(x)) for x in leaves if x is not None]))\n\n  def _forward_apply(network, params, obs, dones):\n      # obs: [B,T,8,8,8], dones: [B,T]\n      B, T = obs.shape[:2]\n      obs_flat = obs.reshape(B*T, *obs.shape[2:])\n      dones_flat = dones.reshape(B*T)\n      logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(params, obs_flat, dones_flat, None)\n      logits = logits_flat.reshape(B, T, -1)\n      values = values_flat.reshape(B, T)\n      return logits, values\n\n\
    \  def _make_synthetic_batch(key, B=16, T=20):\n      # Observations consistent with Sokoban: (8,8,8), last channel time\n      # Use simple structured synthetic: one-hot-like noise with small bias\n      k1, k2, k3 = random.split(key, 3)\n      obs = random.normal(k1, (B, T, 8, 8, 8)) * 0.05\n      # Encode a weak channel bias to emulate \"time\" feature increasing over T\n      time = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T)[None, :, None, None, None]\n      obs = obs.at[..., 7:8].add(time)  # channel 7 time-like\n      dones = jnp.zeros((B, T), dtype=bool)\n      actions = random.randint(k2, (B, T), 0, 4)  # 4 actions\n      # Advantages ~ N(0,1), returns = values + advantages at init later (filled in loss)\n      adv = random.normal(k3, (B, T))\n      return obs, dones, actions, adv\n\n  def _gather_logp(logits, actions):\n      # logits: [B,T,4], actions [B,T]\n      logp_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n      B, T = actions.shape\n      idx = (jnp.arange(B)[:, None], jnp.arange(T),\
    \ actions)\n      return logp_all[idx], logp_all\n\n  def _compute_grads(network, params, obs, dones, actions, advantages):\n      # Single-step value and policy losses at init using synthetic targets\n      def loss_policy(p):\n          logits, values = _forward_apply(network, p, obs, dones)\n          logp_a, _ = _gather_logp(logits, actions)\n          # stop-gradient on advantages as in training\n          return -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages) * logp_a)\n\n      def loss_value(p):\n          logits, values = _forward_apply(network, p, obs, dones)\n          # returns = values + advantages (bootstrapped at init)\n          returns = values + advantages\n          return 0.5 * jnp.mean((values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns))**2)\n\n      g_pol = jax.grad(loss_policy)(params)\n      g_val = jax.grad(loss_value)(params)\n      return _flatten_tree_norm(g_val), _flatten_tree_norm(g_pol)\n\n  def _init_params(network, key, obs_shape=(1, 8, 8, 8)):\n      # Minimal init\
    \ via a dummy apply\n      # Build a single fake obs and done to trigger parameter creation\n      fake_obs = jnp.zeros(obs_shape, dtype=jnp.float32)\n      fake_done = jnp.zeros((obs_shape[0],), dtype=bool)\n      params = network.init(key, fake_obs, fake_done, None)\n      return params\n\n  def test():\n      print(\"Running initialization probe for R_vp (value-to-policy grad norm ratio)\")\n      ks = random.split(random.PRNGKey(BASE_SEED), 8)\n      configs = [\n          {\"steps\": 4, \"width\": 64, \"ratio\": 0.28},\n          {\"steps\": 5, \"width\": 64, \"ratio\": 0.28},\n          {\"steps\": 4, \"width\": 56, \"ratio\": 0.26},\n          {\"steps\": 5, \"width\": 56, \"ratio\": 0.26},\n      ]\n      results = []\n      for i, cfg in enumerate(configs):\n          net = _build_net(cfg[\"steps\"], cfg[\"width\"], cfg[\"ratio\"])\n          params = _init_params(net, ks[i])\n          obs, dones, actions, adv = _make_synthetic_batch(ks[i+4])\n          gv, gp = _compute_grads(net,\
    \ params, obs, dones, actions, adv)\n          rvp = (gv / (gp + 1e-8)).item()\n          out = {\n              \"steps\": cfg[\"steps\"],\n              \"width\": cfg[\"width\"],\n              \"ratio\": cfg[\"ratio\"],\n              \"grad_value_norm\": float(gv),\n              \"grad_policy_norm\": float(gp),\n              \"R_vp\": float(rvp),\n          }\n          print(json.dumps(out))\n          results.append(out)\n      print(\"Probe complete.\")\n      return {\"results\": results}\n```"
