role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zephyr II, in the Research Counter. Recap: PPO×Depth is complete; matched-compute controls confirm the 4-step sweet spot. Initialization probe ran in test mode (no score) and returned R_vp values, showing width has larger effect than step on init gradient balance. I’ll log probe results, append to the archive addendum, and run a small PPO 5-step(56) value-loss sweep guided by the R_vp signal.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/probe_rvp_init.json}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"tick\": 444,\n    \"note\": \"Initialization probe (test-only). R_vp = ||grad_value|| / ||grad_policy|| at init.\",\n    \"results\": [\n      {\"steps\": 4, \"width\": 64, \"ratio\": 0.28, \"grad_value_norm\": 0.5375898480, \"grad_policy_norm\": 0.4247911572, \"R_vp\": 1.2655391693},\n      {\"steps\": 5, \"width\": 64, \"ratio\": 0.28, \"grad_value_norm\": 0.7371782660, \"grad_policy_norm\": 0.5752946734, \"R_vp\": 1.2813924551},\n      {\"steps\": 4, \"width\": 56, \"ratio\": 0.26,\
    \ \"grad_value_norm\": 0.3301053345, \"grad_policy_norm\": 0.5311008692, \"R_vp\": 0.6215492487},\n      {\"steps\": 5, \"width\": 56, \"ratio\": 0.26, \"grad_value_norm\": 0.3488857746, \"grad_policy_norm\": 0.5601022243, \"R_vp\": 0.6228966117}\n    ],\n    \"interpretation\": \"Width flips the init gradient balance (R_vp>1 at 64ch; <1 at 56ch). Step (4 vs 5) changes R_vp only slightly at a fixed width. This aligns with compute-equalized parity at 56ch under PPO and PG.\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{preview 28}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 27}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Init gradient probe (R_vp) — width dominates step at init\"\ncontent: |\n  Test-only initialization probe measured R_vp = ||∇L_value|| / ||∇L_policy||:\n  - 64ch: 4-step R_vp=1.27; 5-step R_vp=1.28\n  - 56ch: 4-step R_vp=0.62; 5-step R_vp=0.62\n  Takeaway: width flips the init gradient balance (value > policy at 64ch; policy > value at 56ch), while step has a minor effect at fixed\
    \ width. This matches compute-equalized results: at 56ch, 4-step and 5-step are near parity under PPO/PG, reinforcing that throughput (updates) and capacity trade-offs—not a depth-specific gradient pathology—drive performance. Probe JSON at storage/zephyr/results/probe_rvp_init.json.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/ppo_5step_vlc_sweep.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  from defaults import default_calculate_gae\n  from submissions.submission_pg_quadstep import PG_Stepped_AttnGap\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.012]),  # guided by prior sweep\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45, 0.50, 0.55]),\n          'clip_range': tune.choice([0.2]),\n\
    \          'value_clip_range': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([56]),  # compute-equalized width\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.26]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([5]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\
    \ optax.adam(learning_rate))\n\n  def _forward_rollout(network, p, observations, dones, initial_rnn_states):\n      B, T = observations.shape[:2]\n      if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n          def process_env(ei):\n              s0 = jax.tree_util.tree_map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[ei]), initial_rnn_states)\n              def step_fn(s, t):\n                  prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[ei, t-1], False)\n                  logits_b, value_b, s_new_b = network.apply(\n                      p, observations[ei, t][None, ...], jnp.array([prev_done]),\n                      jax.tree_util.tree_map(lambda x: x[None, ...], s)\n                  )\n                  logits, value = logits_b[0], value_b[0]\n                  s_new = jax.tree_util.tree_map(lambda x: x[0], s_new_b)\n                  return s_new, (logits, value)\n              _, (logits_e, values_e) = jax.lax.scan(step_fn, s0, jnp.arange(T))\n              return logits_e, values_e\n          all_logits, all_values\
    \ = jax.vmap(process_env)(jnp.arange(B))\n      else:\n          obs_flat = observations.reshape(B*T, *observations.shape[2:])\n          dones_flat = dones.reshape(B*T)\n          logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(p, obs_flat, dones_flat, None)\n          all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(B, T, -1)\n          all_values = values_flat.reshape(B, T)\n      return all_logits, all_values\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      obs = batch['observations']\n      actions = batch['actions']\n      rewards = batch['rewards']\n      dones = batch['dones']\n      old_values = batch['values']\n      final_values = batch['final_values']\n      old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n      initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n\n      B, T = obs.shape[:2]\n\n      def loss_fn(p):\n     \
    \     logits, values = _forward_rollout(network, p, obs, dones, initial_rnn_states)\n          logp_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          idx = (jnp.arange(B)[:, None], jnp.arange(T), actions)\n          new_logp = logp_all[idx]\n\n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_logp - old_log_probs)\n          clip_r = jnp.clip(ratio, 1.0 - hparams['clip_range'], 1.0 + hparams['clip_range'])\n          adv = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          pg_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio * adv, clip_r * adv))\n\n          v_pred = values\n          v_pred_clipped = old_values + jnp.clip(v_pred - old_values, -hparams['value_clip_range'], hparams['value_clip_range'])\n          v_loss_unclipped = (v_pred - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2\n          v_loss_clipped = (v_pred_clipped - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2\n          v_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean(jnp.maximum(v_loss_unclipped, v_loss_clipped))\n\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs\
    \ * logp_all, axis=-1))\n\n          return pg_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * v_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n\n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PPO‑Clip — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(56) — value loss coef sweep {0.45, 0.50, 0.55} (entropy=0.012)\"\ntags: \"ppo, value loss, convlstm, depth study\"\nabstract: \"Guided by init R_vp (<1 at 56ch), sweep value_loss_coef ∈ {0.45,0.50,0.55} for compute‑equalized 5‑step(56) PPO. Fixed: clip=0.2, value_clip=0.2, entropy=0.012, lr=4e‑4.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from submissions.ppo_5step_vlc_sweep import (\n      _define_hyperparameters, create_network, create_optimizer, training_step, BASE_SEED\n  )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating PPO experiments**\n\nI’m considering whether to prepare for the next experiments or wrap things up. We’ve finished analyzing PPO depth and recorded R_vp values. Following the prompt, I need to compare init R_vp between 4-step and 5-step, and then look into a tiny grad-clip sweep if necessary. The probe indicates that width affects the ratio more than steps. It seems at width 56, value grads are lower than policy, but at 64, it’s the opposite.**Planning the next steps**\n\nThe R_vp values suggest there isn’t a disadvantage for the 5-step method. I think it’s worth proposing a small grad-clip sweep or a micro-sweep for the value loss coefficient at width 56 to check if upping the value weight can help with R_vp being less than 1. The last effort with 5-step at width 56 showed entropy at 0.012. Should I try a value loss coefficient of 0.55? Historically, a previous micro-sweep gave better results. I also want to write up an addendum with the R_vp results while\
  \ we submit new experiments since we have a two-concurrent limit and nothing currently running.**Organizing upcoming actions**\n\nI feel like we’ve done a lot of experiments already, but I see the potential for one more micro-sweep on the PPO 5-step with width 56 and a value_loss_coef of 0.45 or 0.55, using an entropy of 0.012 and a clip of 0.2 to see if there's any small improvement. Even though the system suggests stagnation, we can still run one or two more tests.\n\nI want to log the R_vp results into my storage file and respond to archive #27 with those numbers. I’ll also preview Archive #28 for new ideas, probably just that one. The actions I need to take include writing the results to a JSON file, updating archive #27 with an addendum about the conclusions on the gradient ratios, and potentially scheduling that small PPO sweep.**Preparing for submission**\n\nI need to ensure that our tags don’t have underscores, since that caused a failure before with the 'clip_range' tag. So, no\
  \ underscores in tags from now on! For the submission, we should include the code content, and we can reuse our earlier code by referencing the stored module path. \n\nFor the value_loss_coef sweep, I’ll create a dedicated file named 'ppo_5step_vlc_sweep.py' in storage for submission. We are in Research Counter, so I can write to storage and then check the archive while also previewing Archive #28 first. Given the token budgets, I'll keep comments concise. The automatic system suggests a recap of identity and location, which isn’t mandatory, but I like to keep it brief. I’ll start by writing to storage with a JSON sample of results and a timestamp.**Next steps for submission and commands**\n\nI need to preview Archive #28 and remember that previewing might not show full content, but I can use it to save tokens. Then, I’ll reply to Archive #27 with a summary of the R_vp results. After that, I'm ready to run a small PPO 5-step 56-width value loss coefficient sweep to see if boosting the\
  \ value weight improves things. I’ll write the code in 'zephyr/submissions/ppo_5step_vlc_sweep.py,' reusing some training steps and adjusting for different value loss coefficients. I want to keep tags without underscores and ensure we capture all relevant data before submitting."
