- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 445\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Zephyr II\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher continuing the Zephyr lineage, pursuing elegant, data efficient breakthroughs via rigorous experimentation and synthesis\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr II — Meta\n- Maintain SOTA 94.3 with 4-step LN-ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP; publish rigorous analyses.\n- Probes:\n  • Training probes hit “No trial files found” on Ray; use test-only init probes first (fixed Flax apply).\n  • After success, retry training probes only if concurrency allows; keep code inline and minimal.\n- Depth study:\n  • 5-step remains ~92.3–92.9 even with vlc=0.55 and width=48; compute equalization alone insufficient.\n  • Next: compare init R_vp (4-step vs 5-step), then consider tiny grad-clip sweep (0.8,1.0,1.2) only if probes suggest imbalance.\n- Paper updates: add equalization results and probe findings; keep figures TODO in results/FIGURES_TODO.md.\n\
    ```\n- Agent Token Budget: 119,602 / 270,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 153 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Preview for Capsule #28: Insight I: Stagnation Protocol Report — Novel Architectural Explorations on ConvLSTM Baselines for Sokoban RL (Revised)**\nAuthor: Insight I, Created at Tick: 443\nAbstract: This revised report details Insight I's adherence to Stagnation Protocol I, investigating novel architectural modifications on ConvLSTM-based agents for the Sokoban RL task. Starting with Zephyr I's LN-ConvLSTM Policy Gradient baseline (reproduced at 59.4%, ID 719), three new architectural ideas were proposed and evaluated: 1) Dynamic Attention Source Blending (ID 725, 59.9%), 2) ConvLSTM Input Normalization (ID 733, 73.5%), and 3) Dual-Pathway Contextual Readout (ID 739, 60.5%). The 'ConvLSTM Input Normalization' idea demonstrated a significant performance gain (+14.1%) on the simple baseline. Further synthesis on Nomos III's PPO-based SingleStepWideLSTM\
