role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zephyr II, in the Research Counter. Recap: PPO×Depth analysis is complete and archived; a 5‑step(56) PPO value‑loss sweep (ID 768) is running. Next, inspired by Insight I’s baseline gains from “ConvLSTM Input Normalization,” I will test a simple, general input normalization on the SOTA 4‑step agent by normalizing observations before the network (per‑channel over H×W), with/without affine and with/without excluding the time channel.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP — input normalization on observations (affine/exclude‑time sweep)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, convlstm, attention, input normalization, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Test a simple input normalization wrapper that normalizes observations per‑channel over H×W before the SOTA 4‑step network. Sweep affine={True,False} and exclude_time_channel={True,False}. Training uses PG defaults (lr=4e‑4, entropy=0.01, value_coef=0.5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n\
    \  from ray import tune\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Tuple\n  from flax import linen as nn\n  from submissions.submission_pg_quadstep import PG_Stepped_AttnGap\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  class InputNormWrapper(nn.Module):\n      base_kwargs: Dict[str, Any]\n      epsilon: float = 1e-5\n      affine: bool = True\n      exclude_time: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, obs, dones, initial_rnn_state):\n          # obs: [B, H, W, C]\n          x = obs\n          C = x.shape[-1]\n          if self.exclude_time and C >= 8:\n              x_main = x[..., :7]\n              x_time = x[..., 7:8]\n              mean = jnp.mean(x_main, axis=(1, 2), keepdims=True)\n              var = jnp.var(x_main, axis=(1, 2), keepdims=True)\n              x_main = (x_main - mean) / jnp.sqrt(var + self.epsilon)\n              if self.affine:\n                  scale = self.param('scale_main', nn.initializers.ones, (1, 1, 1, 7))\n\
    \                  bias  = self.param('bias_main', nn.initializers.zeros, (1, 1, 1, 7))\n                  x_main = scale * x_main + bias\n              x = jnp.concatenate([x_main, x_time], axis=-1)\n          else:\n              mean = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2), keepdims=True)\n              var = jnp.var(x, axis=(1, 2), keepdims=True)\n              x = (x - mean) / jnp.sqrt(var + self.epsilon)\n              if self.affine:\n                  scale = self.param('scale', nn.initializers.ones, (1, 1, 1, C))\n                  bias  = self.param('bias', nn.initializers.zeros, (1, 1, 1, C))\n                  x = scale * x + bias\n\n          base = PG_Stepped_AttnGap(**self.base_kwargs)\n          logits, value, new_state = base(x, dones, initial_rnn_state)\n          return logits, value, new_state\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n\
    \          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          # Input norm sweeps:\n          'affine': tune.choice([True, False]),\n          'exclude_time': tune.choice([True, False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      base_kwargs = dict(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n      return InputNormWrapper(\n          base_kwargs=base_kwargs,\n\
    \          epsilon=1e-5,\n          affine=bool(hparams['affine']),\n          exclude_time=bool(hparams['exclude_time']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```"
thinking_content: "**Preparing code submission**\n\nI’m ready to submit another experiment, so I'm setting up the InputNorm experiment as the second one. The code submission title is \"PG — 4-step LN-ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP — input normalization on observations (affine vs none)\". \n\nI’m using a constant PG config. I plan to implement _define_hyperparameters with 'affine' that tunes choices of True or False. Hyperparameters are passed into the training, and I have to ensure they work with Ray Tune's expected key searching. I’m also considering keeping the normalization across channels while maintaining the time distribution.**Implementing normalization options**\n\nI'm considering whether to add an option to exclude the time channel from normalization, but it could complicate things. Instead, I'll keep it simple with a boolean flag for 'exclude_time'. \n\nIf it's set to True, I'll split observations: normalizing the first seven channels while leaving the last unchanged. If not, I'll normalize\
  \ all eight channels. Next, I need to import the necessary libraries and rely on the default training step since we don't need to define one. I'll also make a note for the experiment archive about testing input normalization and follow YAML quoting rules for any fields that include colons.**Finalizing input normalization setup**\n\nI need to use the \"input normalization\" tag without underscores, which means a space is acceptable in the tag. The rules state that tags can be a comma-separated list but must not have underscores in individual tags. I'll create the YAML accordingly.\n\nI'm also considering writing to a storage file for the wrapper to reuse across experiments, but inlining the code works too. Plus, I’ll log the insight that input normalization has improved baselines, which inspired this test. With one experiment slot free, I can continue working efficiently!**Setting up InputNorm trials**\n\nI'm planning to submit one InputNorm and then run trials comparing \"exclude_time\"\
  \ set to True and False. This will lead to two trials since Ray will pick from choices across four seeds, generating four random hyperparameter combinations. Even though booleans might result in duplicates, it’s manageable. \n\nI’ll define hyperparameters including learning rate, entropy coefficient, value loss coefficient, steps, convlstm_features, and the choices for affine and exclude_time.\n\nThat gives me four combos, and I think I’m ready to proceed! I might update the archive with this plan, but it isn't necessary."
