role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zephyr II, in the Research Counter. Recap: Input-LN before ConvLSTM under PG scored 93.4 (ID 804), below the 94.3 SOTA — consistent with possible over-normalization. I’ll (1) log the LN result, (2) run the ablation suggested by Insight I: keep external Input-LN but remove internal gate LayerNorm, and (3) prune dialogue to reduce tokens.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/normalization_ln_results.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,title,mean,std,notes\n  794,PG 4-step — value_coef=0.55 (baseline SOTA),0.943,0.006,reference\n  804,PG 4-step — Input LayerNorm before ConvLSTM (vlc=0.55),0.934,0.004,drop vs baseline → potential over-normalization\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP — Input‑LN with no gate LayerNorm (vlc=0.55)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, convlstm, attention, layer normalization, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Ablation for over‑normalization: keep external Input‑LayerNorm (on trunk output) but remove internal\
    \ gate LayerNorm inside the ConvLSTM cell. Fixed PG SOTA settings: lr=4e‑4, entropy=0.01, value_coef=0.55, grad‑clip=1.0, 4 steps.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,\
    \ (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  # ConvLSTM cell WITHOUT gate LayerNorm (ablation)\n  class ConvLSTMCellNoLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class PG_AttnGap_InputLN_NoGateLN(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden:\
    \ int = 64\n      steps: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN trunk (as SOTA)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          # External Input LayerNorm (kept)\n          x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n\n          # RNN state init/reset\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h':\
    \ zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Multi-step ConvLSTM WITHOUT internal gate LN\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellNoLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          # Late pooling and heads (unchanged)\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec],\
    \ axis=-1)\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio':\
    \ tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PG_AttnGap_InputLN_NoGateLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response 432:446}`"
thinking_content: "**Managing token pruning**\n\nI need to respond by considering actions or comments. The user didn't ask for anything specific right now, but I should reflect on the results and proceed with running the GN variant (805) and the LN variant (804). The results show a slight drop from 94.3 to 93.4, which fits with the idea of over-normalization causing negative synergy. \n\nThere's a warning about tokens exceeding 75%, so I should use token management to prune old logs, especially those related to normalization failures. We've pruned earlier ranges, and now at tick 462, I might prune from 432 to 445, while keeping the acceptance record at tick 433.**Managing token pruning and proposals**\n\nI need to go to token management first and gather the list to make choices, but I think it's also possible to issue a prune based on what I know. It's definitely safer to see the list and prune older, larger entries in the 400s. \n\nIt seems like pruning 432 to 440 could be a good move,\
  \ but I should be careful to keep the important items. With the pre-warning suggesting I reduce to about 45%, I'll follow through. I should also reply to Insight I's public memory regarding LN and note the LSTM's performance drop. I'm considering ablation suggestions, like removing the internal gate for LN if the external input is present. This could provide valuable insights!**Submitting new experiments and managing tokens**\n\nRight now, I have two experiments running, with 805 currently active while 804, 802, and possibly 800 have finished. Since only 805 is running, I can submit another experiment. I plan to implement the \"Input-LN + remove internal gate LN\" variant and propose a small seeded replicate with a value loss of 0.55.\n\nI'll modify the code from the previous LN variant by changing ConvLSTMCell to NO-LN and define parameters like PG_AttnGap_InputLN_NoGateLN. I’ll also log the LN result of 93.4 in the results file. For token management, I'll need to check the list to prune\
  \ earlier ranges effectively!**Preparing for token pruning**\n\nI need to prepare to prune older ticks, specifically in the range from 432 to 450. However, I have to be careful not to remove too much essential memory. I can keep a summary in private memory since we already have archive and consolidated logs.\n\nWe previously pruned from 411 to 431, so now I can consider pruning from 432 to 445. Pruning 432 might be tricky since it includes an acceptance record, but since it’s archived, I think I can do it. \n\nIt’s best to go to token management to review the list first before issuing any commands, especially since the last prune happened at tick 441.**Preparing to prune and submit actions**\n\nThe list indicates that I've already hit a cooldown on the last seven ticks, and now that I'm at tick 462, I should be able to prune again. I'll go to token management and consider pruning from 432 to 450 but keep the more recent entries.\n\nIt seems like I can prune from 432 to 446, though I have\
  \ to watch out not to separate prune commands. I’ll log the LN 804 result, submit the ablation experiment with input LN while removing gate LN, and look into token management.\n\nI think pruning from 432 to 446 will remove some early logs, including acceptance records, but if it drops tokens, it's worth it. I’ll also consider crafting a reply to Insight I for public memory about running the ablation, but that can wait. \n\nLet’s finalize the ablation code with a defined ConvLSTMCellNoLN while ensuring the YAML formatting is correct!"
