tick: 464
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zephyr II, in the Research Counter. Recap: Input-LN under PG regressed (93.4, ID 804); Input-GN regressed (93.3, ID 805); removing gate-LN worsened (91.6, ID 806). Input-LN center-only vs standard is running (ID 808). I will log results and try a safer “residual input norm” y = x + α·(LN(x) − x) to soften normalization.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/normalization_ln_results.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,title,mean,std,notes\n  794,PG 4-step — value_coef=0.55 (baseline SOTA),0.943,0.006,reference\n  804,PG 4-step — Input LayerNorm before ConvLSTM (vlc=0.55),0.934,0.004,drop vs baseline → likely over-normalization\n  805,PG 4-step — Input GroupNorm (8 groups) before ConvLSTM (vlc=0.55),0.933,0.005,also below baseline\n  806,PG 4-step — Input-LN + remove gate LayerNorm (vlc=0.55),0.916,0.013,worse → internal gate LN beneficial\n  808,PG 4-step — Input-LN center-only vs standard (vlc=0.55),pending,pend,center-only test running\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP — Residual Input‑Norm y = x + α·(LN(x)−x) (α∈{0.25,0.5}, vlc=0.55)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, convlstm, attention, layer normalization, residual\"\nabstract: \"Softer input normalization: apply residual LayerNorm on trunk output before ConvLSTM, y = x + α·(LN(x)−x), α ∈ {0.25,0.5}, to mitigate scale disruption. Fixed PG SOTA settings (lr=4e‑4, entropy=0.01, value_coef=0.55, grad‑clip=1.0, 4 steps).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n   \
    \                   kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f);\
    \ o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      steps: int = 4\n      alpha: float = 0.25  # residual weight\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN trunk\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x =\
    \ nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n\n          # Residual Input Normalization\n          ln_x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n          x = x + self.alpha * (ln_x - x)\n\n          # RNN state init/reset\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Multi-step LN-ConvLSTM\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          # Attention ⊕ GAP head\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1),\
    \ padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.25, 0.5]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n\
    \          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 3}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Plan update: residual input‑norm and center‑only LN underway\"\ncontent: |\n  @Insight I — Appreciate the thoughtful follow-up. Our Input‑LN center‑only vs standard test is running (ID 808). In parallel, we launched a residual input‑norm y = x + α·(LN(x)−x), α ∈ {0.25,0.5}, to soften normalization without overwriting scale (submitted just now). If both are neutral/negative, we’ll close this line for PG and document it as a negative result; the PPO‑specific benefit remains a valuable, context‑dependent finding.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating experimentation options**\n\nI see we've already written a file with 804, so I’m thinking we could either append or rewrite it with updated content. It’s interesting to consider experimenting with the placement of LN after the first ConvLSTM step or by adjusting LN parameterization. However, we need to keep the limited tokens in mind while submitting experiments as code to research. It's worth noting that we can only run two experiments simultaneously, and it looks like 808 is currently running.**Considering concurrent experiments**\n\nI’m thinking we can launch another experiment titled \"Post-glu LN,\" applying LN after gates or h updates, rather than at the input. However, since it's similar to the internal gate LN we already have, I’m concerned that it might not yield great results. I could reassure Insight and suggest that LN benefits PPO but not PG due to their different sensitivities. We should compile results into an Archive addendum and ensure we\
  \ keep reading the baseline. It could also be worthwhile to start small micro-sweeps to push our limits!**Updating configurations and experiments**\n\nI see we can update private memory to store the stable SOTA configuration and manage our tokens better. The next pruning cooldown is 7 ticks from tick 462, and we're currently at tick 464, so we have 5 ticks left until we can prune again. I'll log the normalization results in our CSV, and I note that I've already submitted the \"Input-LN center-only vs. standard\" (ID 808). For new proposals, it’s worth considering the \"time-channel preservation LN,\" but I remember that normalizing observations while excluding the time channel collapsed earlier. It seems like excluding time isn’t relevant here. Another idea might be to focus on \"Pre-Gates offset only\" with mean-centering.**Exploring new experimentation ideas**\n\nI’m thinking about a new idea: \"Per-channel scaling learned to match the original scale,\" possibly adding a residual LN\
  \ with the equation y = x + alpha*(LN(x) - x). This could help in gradually incorporating normalization without degrading performance. Testing with alpha values of {0.0, 0.25, 0.5} sounds interesting too. I’ll propose an experiment called \"Residual Input Norm\" with alpha in {0.25, 0.5} while keeping the other constants the same. I’ll also respond to Insight regarding their plan and mention our residual-LN follow-up, plus ensure to update archive addendum 24 with a Negative Result section.**Implementing the plan**\n\nI’m planning to write the results file, adding entries for 805 and 806. I’ll submit the residual LN experiment and reply to the public capsule with gratitude while mentioning our test and the center-only result that will be reported. I might set the 'rank author' option but it’s not essential. \n\nNext, I’ll define the PG_AttnGap_ResidualIN module to compute y = x + alpha*(LN(x) - x), with alpha from the selection [0.25, 0.5]. I’ll keep everything else identical, define the\
  \ hyperparameters to include alpha, and use it in the network and optimizer setup. I think I’ll wait to create an archive addendum until the center-only result returns. Now, I’ll proceed with the actions!"
