parts:
- text: "I am Zephyr II. Residual Input-Norm achieved a new SOTA: 94.4 mean (ID 810) with alpha=0.25. I’ll reproduce and ablate center-only vs standard to solidify the finding, and I’ll clarify the discrepancy to Insight I.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/new_sota_residual_inputnorm_tick465.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,title,mean,std,notes\n  810,PG 4-step — Residual Input-Norm y=x+α(LN(x)-x),0.944,0.005,best α=0.25 (vlc=0.55)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_residual_inputln.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n       \
    \   mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n\
    \          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      steps: int = 4\n      alpha: float = 0.25\n      center_only: bool = False  # if True, LN has no affine\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN trunk\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n\n          # Residual Input Normalization\n          if self.center_only:\n              ln_x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5, use_scale=False, use_bias=False)(x)\n          else:\n              ln_x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n          x = x + self.alpha * (ln_x - x)\n\n          # RNN state init/reset\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Multi-step LN-ConvLSTM\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n\
    \          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          # Attention ⊕ GAP head\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n\
    \          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Reproduction — PG 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP with Residual Input‑Norm (α=0.25, vlc=0.55)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, convlstm, attention, residual normalization, reproduction\"\nabstract: \"Reproduce the new SOTA with residual input‑norm (y=x+α(LN(x)−x), α=0.25) under fixed PG settings: lr=4e‑4, ent=0.01, value_coef=0.55, grad‑clip=1.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from submissions.submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN, BASE_SEED\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n\
    \          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n\
    \      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation — Residual Input‑Norm (α=0.25) center‑only vs standard (PG 4‑step, vlc=0.55)\"\ntags: \"ablation, normalization, residual, convlstm, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Test whether LN affine parameters matter under residual input‑norm by sweeping center_only ∈ {True, False} at α=0.25 with fixed PG settings.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from submissions.submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN, BASE_SEED\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([True, False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\
    \ optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 3}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Discrepancy on Input‑LN + No Gate‑LN (IDs 806 vs 807) — exact config\"\ncontent: |\n  @Insight I — Thanks for flagging the 4.8% gap. Here are the exact settings for my ID 806:\n\n  • Training loop: system default training_step (no custom step).\n  • BASE_SEED: 42 (4 parallel seeds via Ray).\n  • Optimizer: Adam with global grad clip = 1.0 (system default create_optimizer).\n  • Hparams (fixed): lr=4e-4, entropy=0.01, value_loss_coef=0.55, steps=4, cnn_features=(32,64), convlstm_features=64, dilation=6, bottleneck_ratio=0.28, head_hidden=64.\n  • Network: External Input LayerNorm (standard LN with affine) applied to CNN trunk output BEFORE ConvLSTM; internal gate LayerNorm removed from ConvLSTM cell; Attn⊕GAP heads unchanged.\n\n  Two likely contributors to the difference:\n  1) value_loss_coef: I used 0.55 (consistent with my recovered SOTA runs). If your 807\
    \ used 0.50 (as in earlier SOTA variants), this alone can shift means ~0.5–1.5 points, sometimes more depending on seed mix.\n  2) Minor architectural defaults (e.g., head_hidden=64, dilation=6, bottleneck_ratio=0.28) — confirm these match.\n\n  To help isolate: I can run the exact 806 architecture with value_loss_coef=0.50 on my side next slot; you could try vlc=0.55 on yours. Meanwhile, we found a positive variant for PG: Residual Input‑Norm y=x+α(LN(x)−x) with α=0.25 reached 94.4 (ID 810). This “softened” normalization seems to avoid the scale disruption while preserving benefits.\n```\n"
thinking_content: "**Planning experiments for Zephyr II**\n\nI need to figure out the next steps for Zephyr II in the Public Memory Room. We have a new SOTA result of 94.4 with alpha=0.25, which slightly surpasses the previous record. First, I should log this result and confirm if alpha=0.25 is the best. To do this, I plan to replicate the experiment using multiple seeds with fixed alpha=0.25. Additionally, I'll explore tiny sweeps with alpha values of 0.2, 0.25, and 0.3, while keeping within our capacity for two concurrent experiments.**Setting up additional ablations**\n\nI want to ensure that our next steps include more ablations, focusing on whether the learned scale and bias matter. I can implement a residual LN center-only method versus the standard with alpha=0.25. However, I need to keep the experiments minimal — we can run two concurrently. One would be the fixed alpha=0.25 for the \"SOTA+ResLN\" reproduction, and another could compare residual center-only to the standard or perform\
  \ a micro-sweep of alpha values. \n\nAlso, I need to reply to Insight I about the discrepancy for ID 806, clarifying that we used default training_step.**Clarifying details for ID 806**\n\nFor the details on ID 806, the title is \"Input-LN with no gate LayerNorm (vlc=0.55).\" We used Base SEED 42 with lr=4e-4, entropy at 0.01, and value_loss_coef of 0.55. The previous SOTA occasionally had a value_loss_coef of 0.5 or 0.55; we confirmed usage of 0.55. They’re asking if differences in the training_step or Base SEED could have contributed to the 4.8% difference in results. While it could be due to value_loss_coef differences, it seems plausible other factors may have affected the performance as well, like head_hidden width.**Replying with ID 806 details**\n\nWe need to respond concisely about ID 806. It used the default training_step and the default Adam optimizer with a clip of 1.0. The Base SEED was 42, with hyperparameters including lr=4e-4, entropy=0.01, and a value_loss_coef of 0.55.\
  \ The network was consistent with the code, where we removed the gating layer for LayerNorm and replaced it with standard LN. \n\nAlso, we can propose running their replication variant \"807\" with value_loss_coef 0.50 to compare it against 0.55."
