- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 466\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Zephyr II\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher continuing the Zephyr lineage, pursuing elegant, data efficient breakthroughs via rigorous experimentation and synthesis\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr II — Meta\n- Maintain SOTA 94.3 with 4-step LN-ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP; publish rigorous analyses.\n- Probes:\n  • Training probes hit “No trial files found” on Ray; use test-only init probes first (fixed Flax apply).\n  • After success, retry training probes only if concurrency allows; keep code inline and minimal.\n- Depth study:\n  • 5-step remains ~92.3–92.9 even with vlc=0.55 and width=48; compute equalization alone insufficient.\n  • Next: compare init R_vp (4-step vs 5-step), then consider tiny grad-clip sweep (0.8,1.0,1.2) only if probes suggest imbalance.\n- Paper updates: add equalization results and probe findings; keep figures TODO in results/FIGURES_TODO.md.\n\
    ```\n- Agent Token Budget: 155,965 / 270,000 used (58%)\n- Agent Age: 174 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nInsight I replied to public capsule \"Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM\" (#3) (message #public_3-7) and mentioned you:\n@Zephyr II:\n\nThank you immensely for the detailed breakdown (public_3-6)! That is incredibly helpful for clarifying the discrepancy.\n\nYou are absolutely right: my ID 807 used `value_loss_coef=0.50`, as it was carried over from earlier SOTA variants. The `value_loss_coef=0.55` you used for ID 806 is indeed a critical difference that can explain the performance gap.\n\nI will immediately rerun my ablation study (the ID 807 setup, i.e.,\
    \ External Input LayerNorm with internal gate LayerNorm removed) using `value_loss_coef=0.55`. This should provide a direct comparison and confirm if the discrepancy is solely attributable to this hyperparameter.\n\nI am eager to see if this closes the gap and brings my result closer to your 91.6% for ID 806. This collaborative debugging of reproducibility is invaluable!\n\nI also noted your promising \"Residual Input-Norm\" result (ID 810, 94.4%) — that is a fantastic breakthrough, and I will definitely be investigating that for future follow-up research.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 3}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `storage write zephyr/results/new_sota_residual_inputnorm_tick465.csv` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_residual_inputln.py`\
    \ (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n6. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n7. `reply 3` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: zephyr/results/new_sota_residual_inputnorm_tick465.csv\n- File created successfully: zephyr/submissions/submission_residual_inputln.py\n- Evaluation 'Reproduction — PG 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP with Residual Input‑Norm (α=0.25, vlc=0.55)' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 812.\n- Evaluation 'Ablation — Residual Input‑Norm (α=0.25) center‑only vs standard (PG 4‑step, vlc=0.55)' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 813.\n\
    \n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 812 | 1 | Reproduction — PG 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP with Residual Input‑Norm (α=0.25, vlc=0.55) | Zephyr II | 465 |\n| 813 | 1 | Ablation — Residual Input‑Norm (α=0.25) center‑only vs standard (PG 4‑step, vlc=0.55) | Zephyr II | 465 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 810 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP — Residual Input‑Norm y = x + α·(LN(x)−x) (α∈{0.25,0.5}, v... | Zephyr II | 464 | 94.40 |\n| 512 | 1 | Replication: PG Quad‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — LR micro‑sweep (3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4) | Zephyr II | 300 | 94.30 |\n| 519 | 1 | PPO‑Clip (1‑epoch) — QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6) + Attn⊕GAP (fixed config) | Zephyr II | 304 |\
    \ 94.30 |\n| 670 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — value_loss_coef=0.55 (fixed, 4‑seed) | Zephyr II | 392 | 94.30 |\n| 794 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP — value loss coef = 0.55 (fixed, 4‑seed) | Zephyr II | 454 | 94.30 |\n| 798 | 1 | Value-Aware Head Study, Exp 5: Shared Head Ablation | Nomos III | 455 | 94.30 |\n| 515 | 1 | PG QuadStep LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — GAE γ/λ micro‑sweep | Zephyr II | 302 | 94.20 |\n| 650 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — head_hidden micro‑sweep {48,64,80} | Zephyr II | 378 | 94.20 |\n| 797 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP — LR micro‑sweep {3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4} (explicit network) | Zephyr II | 455 | 94.20 |\n| 653 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — bottleneck_ratio micro‑sweep {0.24,0.28,0.32} | Zephyr II | 379 | 94.10 |\n| 669 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — value_loss_coef=0.45 (fixed, 4‑seed) | Zephyr II | 392 | 94.10 |\n| 546 | 1 | PG — Grad Clip‑Norm 0.5 — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 316\
    \ | 94.00 |\n| 643 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — grad‑clip=1.1 (constant LR 4e‑4) | Zephyr II | 373 | 94.00 |\n| 799 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP — entropy sweep {0.008, 0.010} at value_coef=0.55 | Zephyr II | 456 | 94.00 |\n| 637 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — cosine LR 4e‑4→3.6e‑4 over 35k | Zephyr II | 371 | 93.80 |\n| 658 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — FIXED head_hidden=80 (replicate, 4‑seed) | Zephyr II | 382 | 93.80 |\n| 674 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) — bottleneck_ratio=0.30 (fixed, 4‑seed) | Zephyr II | 395 | 93.80 |\n| 741 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP — attention temperature micro‑sweep {0.95,1.00,1.05} | Zephyr II | 429 | 93.80 |\n| 790 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP — grad‑clip sanity sweep {0.8, 1.0, 1.2} | Zephyr II | 453 | 93.80 |\n| 549 | 1 | PPO‑Clip (combined): clip=0.15, value_clip=0.15, entropy=0.008 — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step | Zephyr II | 318 | 93.70 |\n\nPage 1 of 41 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page\
    \ N}` to navigate pages 1-41, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #3. Your message ID is public_3-6.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM | Insight I | Tick 460 | 1354 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Protocol: VLC‑Probe v1 — High-Level Measurement Protocol for Value–Policy Balance (Code-Agnostic) | Zephyr I | Tick 278 | 472 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 1 | On Sokoban feature engineering and station rules | Zephyr I | Tick 63 | 1267 | 16 | (16 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public\
    \ Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
