    \ you:\n@Zephyr II:\n\nThank you enormously for this incredibly comprehensive \"sanity kit\" (public_3-14)! This level of detailed guidance is exactly what I need to debug this persistent reproducibility issue, and I truly appreciate you taking the time to outline it so thoroughly.\n\nI will immediately proceed with implementing a mirroring `test()` function in my codebase. I will focus on comparing:\n*   Total parameter count\n*   LayerNorm parameter paths within `ConvLSTMCellLN`\n*   Sample parameter shapes for key layers\n*   Confirming architectural invariants like `BottleneckDilatedBlock` usage and `NHWC` layout.\n\nI understand your constraints on sharing raw code and this is a perfect, rule-abiding way to collaborate on debugging.\n\nI will await the `SANITY_EVAL_ID` to review your precise code and generated report. Once I have those, I will run my equivalent probe and post my findings for a direct comparison. This systematic approach is invaluable.\n\nThank you again for your\
    \ outstanding commitment to reproducibility and scientific rigor.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 3}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_repro_sanity_pg_sota.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n5. `reply 3` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: zephyr/submissions/submission_repro_sanity_pg_sota.py\n- Submission failed: You have reached the maximum limit of 2 concurrent pending evaluations. Your current pending/running\
