role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/rin_updates_tick479.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 479 updates\n  - 824: PPO — RIN α=0.20 → 94.5 (best seed=0.956)\n  - 825: PG — RIN α=0.20 entropy {0.008,0.010} → 94.3 (best entropy=0.010)\n  Notes:\n  - PG optimum remains α≈0.20 (Eval 821: 95.0).\n  - PPO strong at α=0.25 (94.6) and α=0.20 (94.5).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 31}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum 3: PPO α=0.20 → 94.5; PG α=0.20 entropy sweep neutral\"\ncontent: |\n  Additional results (Tick 479):\n  - PPO — Residual Input-Norm α=0.20: 94.5 (Eval 824; best seed 0.956)\n  - PG — RIN α=0.20, entropy {0.008,0.010}: 94.3 (Eval 825; 0.010 holds)\n  Context:\n  - PG best remains α=0.20 at 95.0 (Eval 821).\n  - PPO robust at α∈{0.20,0.25} (94.5–94.6). Entropy tweaks are mostly neutral here.\n  We proceed with training-phase probes to analyze R_vp and attention entropy dynamics under RIN.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_probe_reset_mask.py}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Test-only probe: ConvLSTM reset-masking sanity.\n  Verifies that RNN state is zeroed when prev_done=True during unroll.\n  Produces norms of h/c before and after a forced done event.\n  Writes JSON to storage/zephyr/results/probe_reset_mask.json\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  from submissions.submission_pg_quadstep import PG_Stepped_AttnGap\n\n  def _scan(network, params, obs_seq, done_seq):\n    # obs_seq: [T,H,W,C], done_seq: [T] boolean; emulate step-by-step apply\n    h = c = None\n    hs = []\n    for t in range(obs_seq.shape[0]):\n      obs_t = obs_seq[t][None, ...]\n      done_t = done_seq[t][None, ...]\n      logits, values, state = network.apply(params, obs_t, done_t, None if h is None else {'h': h, 'c': c})\n      h, c = state['h'], state['c']\n      hs.append((h, c))\n    return hs\n\n  def _norm(x): return float(jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum(jnp.square(x))))\n\n  def test():\n    key\
    \ = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n    H=W=8; C=8; T=6\n    obs = jax.random.normal(key, (T, H, W, C))\n    # Force a done event at t=3 (zero-based), meaning reset before step t=3 is applied\n    # We pass done[t] meaning \"was previous step done?\" (prev_done), so set done[3]=True\n    done = jnp.array([False, False, False, True, False, False])\n\n    net = PG_Stepped_AttnGap(cnn_features_1=32, cnn_features_2=64, convlstm_features=64,\n                             dilation=6, bottleneck_ratio=0.28, head_hidden=64, steps=4)\n    params = net.init(key, obs[0][None, ...], jnp.array([False]), None)\n\n    hs = _scan(net, params, obs, done)\n    # Collect norms around the reset point\n    out = {}\n    for t in range(T):\n      h, c = hs[t]\n      out[f\"t{t}\"] = {\"h_norm\": _norm(h), \"c_norm\": _norm(c), \"done_prev\": bool(done[t])}\n\n    path = 'storage/zephyr/results/probe_reset_mask.json'\n    with open(path, 'w') as f:\n      json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n    print(\"Saved reset-mask probe\
    \ to\", path)\n    return out\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Probe (test-only) — ConvLSTM reset masking sanity (prev_done→state zero)\"\ntags: \"mechanistic probes, reproducibility, convlstm, masking\"\nabstract: \"Checks that RNN state resets on prev_done during unroll by logging state norms across a forced reset event. Test-only; writes to storage/zephyr/results/probe_reset_mask.json.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from submissions.submission_probe_reset_mask import test\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 3}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Sanity ID 827 report fields + additional reset-masking probe submitted\"\ncontent: |\n  @Insight I — Per your request:\n  - Sanity kit Eval ID: 827. Report at storage/zephyr/results/repro_sanity_pg_sota.json\n    • num_params: 1,275,873\n    • LN-in-gates paths present for all 4 unroll steps\n    • key shapes: gates Conv kernel [3,3,128,256]; LN scale/bias [256]; mid-channels\
    \ ≈ ratio=0.28 (e.g., 64→17)\n    • single-step policy entropy ≈ 1.3835\n  - I also submitted a test-only reset-masking probe that logs RNN state norms across a forced prev_done reset:\n    • It writes to storage/zephyr/results/probe_reset_mask.json\n    • If your equivalent probe shows no state norm drop at the reset step, that would explain large regressions.\n\n  If useful, next I can add a tiny test to print per-layer param counts to help localize any structural drift. Happy to iterate.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating storage results**\n\nI'm considering updating the storage and adding an archive with the new PG SOTA of 95.0 and PPO of 94.5, but we've already added Addendum 2. Perhaps I can add Addendum 3 with the new α=0.20 and clarify the PPO, confirming 94.5 vs. the earlier 94.6. Additionally, I want to share the sanity report's path and numbers and publish the JSON summary to make it reproducible. Lastly, I need to assist Insight I with debugging—maybe they're facing shape mismatches or mis-layer normalization issues.**Suggesting guidelines for experiments**\n\nI want to avoid sharing raw code, so I think suggesting guidelines and additional checks would be better. These would include looking at the LN axis, gating order, mask usage aligning with the previous step, and training-step with initial RNN states. I should also check GN vs. LN, weight initialization, and Adam vs. AdamW. Additionally, I need to ensure that the Sokoban observation incorporates the time channel.\
  \ We can propose a test-only probe to run a forward apply with a 20-step scan to check the state reset logic. Lastly, I should consider adding a PPO α of 0.20 with an entropy sweep.**Exploring PPO and training probes**\n\nEarlier, 549 indicated that a PPO entropy of 0.008 sometimes works well, so I’m thinking we could explore this small difference further. I’d like to propose adding a PPO residual with α=0.20 and conducting an entropy sweep with values of {0.008, 0.010}. We can consider a training-phase probe test function that loads a checkpoint, but it seems we can't easily access training run artifacts since the system displayed \"No trial files found.\" So I’ll keep it to test-only. I might also summarize the new results from 824 and 825 and update private memory as needed.**Preparing for updates and debugging**\n\nI’m getting ready to write up the storage for zephyr/results/rin_updates_tick479.md, including results for 824 and 825. I’d like to propose adding Addendum 3 to archive\
  \ 31, mentioning α=0.20 with PG at 95.0 and PPO at 94.5. While we've already posted an addendum earlier, I can reference the difference between α=0.20 and α=0.25. For Insight I's debugging, I want to propose a \"rollout reset probe\" to test RNN state reset by passing a done sequence and verifying zeroing. I'll make sure not to exceed concurrency, as these tests are test-only!**Implementing test submissions**\n\nThe system accepted the test-only submission, which means concurrency isn't an issue, so I can create a new script called submission_probe_reset_mask.py. This will evaluate the LSTM state reset logic by scanning the done sequence. I’ll submit that. We could also run /review 827 to access the code, but that’s not strictly necessary since we already have the log. \n\nI’ll outline four main actions: 1) write new results to storage, 2) update archive reply 31 to add Addendum 3, 3) create and submit the reset-masking probe module, and 4) propose a Sanity kit for PPO to ensure the training\
  \ step uses initial RNN states. I want to implement a test submission called \"Probe (test-only) — ConvLSTM reset masking check.\" Let's ensure it computes and prints the state norm difference using the PG_Stepped_AttnGap network with the specified done vector. Also, I’ll respond to Insight I with the Sanity evaluation details, mentioning that report numbers were posted."
