tick: 481
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_probe_param_counts.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Test-only probe: per-parameter counts and shapes for PG SOTA network.\n  Initializes PG_Stepped_AttnGap with canonical hparams and writes:\n    - total_param_count\n    - per-leaf param shapes and sizes\n    - aggregated counts by module path prefix\n  Output: storage/zephyr/results/probe_param_counts_pg.json\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  from submissions.submission_pg_quadstep import PG_Stepped_AttnGap\n\n  def _leaf_entries(tree):\n    # Returns list of (path, array) for all leaves in a nested dict-like tree\n    out = []\n    def rec(path, node):\n      if isinstance(node, dict):\n        for k, v in node.items():\n          rec(path + [k], v)\n      else:\n        out.append((\"/\".join(path), node))\n    rec([], tree)\n    return out\n\n  def _aggregate_by_prefix(entries, max_depth=2):\n\
    \    agg = {}\n    for path, arr in entries:\n      parts = path.split(\"/\")\n      prefix = \"/\".join(parts[:max_depth]) if len(parts) >= max_depth else path\n      agg[prefix] = agg.get(prefix, 0) + int(arr.size)\n    return agg\n\n  def test():\n    # Canonical PG SOTA hparams\n    hparams = dict(\n      cnn_features_1=32, cnn_features_2=64,\n      convlstm_features=64, dilation=6,\n      bottleneck_ratio=0.28, head_hidden=64, steps=4\n    )\n    net = PG_Stepped_AttnGap(**hparams)\n\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(42)\n    dummy_obs = jnp.zeros((1, 8, 8, 8), dtype=jnp.float32)\n    dummy_done = jnp.zeros((1,), dtype=jnp.bool_)\n    params = net.init(key, dummy_obs, dummy_done, None)\n\n    # Convert to plain dict if needed\n    tree = params.unfreeze() if hasattr(params, \"unfreeze\") else params\n    entries = _leaf_entries(tree[\"params\"] if \"params\" in tree else tree)\n\n    per_leaf = []\n    total = 0\n    for path, arr in entries:\n      sz = int(arr.size)\n      shape =\
    \ list(arr.shape)\n      per_leaf.append({\"path\": path, \"size\": sz, \"shape\": shape})\n      total += sz\n\n    agg2 = _aggregate_by_prefix(entries, max_depth=2)\n    agg3 = _aggregate_by_prefix(entries, max_depth=3)\n\n    report = {\n      \"hparams\": hparams,\n      \"total_param_count\": total,\n      \"per_leaf\": per_leaf,           # WARNING: long list; use for diffing\n      \"aggregate_by_2\": agg2,         # compact module-level view\n      \"aggregate_by_3\": agg3          # finer module-level view\n    }\n\n    out_path = \"storage/zephyr/results/probe_param_counts_pg.json\"\n    with open(out_path, \"w\") as f:\n      json.dump(report, f, indent=2)\n    print(\"Saved param count report to\", out_path)\n    return {\"total_param_count\": total, \"n_leaves\": len(per_leaf)}\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 3}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Param-count probe staged (test-only) — will submit after current jobs finish\"\ncontent: |\n  @Insight I\
    \ — I’ve staged a per-parameter count probe (test-only) to help pinpoint any structural drift:\n    storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_probe_param_counts.py\n  It initializes the PG SOTA network with canonical hparams and writes:\n    storage/zephyr/results/probe_param_counts_pg.json\n  Contents include total_param_count, every leaf param’s path/shape/size, and aggregates by module prefixes.\n\n  I’ll submit this probe right after the current runs (IDs 832, 833) finish so you can /review and mirror it. If you already have a similar dump on your side, posting the totals and a few top-level aggregates (e.g., ConvLSTMCellLN_*/LayerNorm_0/* sizes) would be enough to spot divergences quickly.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating code and submissions**\n\nI first noticed our earlier sweeps ran at 1.1 and 0.9, yielding results of 94.0 and 93.5, with a possibility of varying RIN. I’m considering testing with a RIN alpha of 0.20 clip sweeps. \n\nWe could perform PPO clip_range and value_clip_range sweeps with RIN, but our current concurrency is limited since there are two runs active. So, I can only stage code to minimize token usage for now.\n\nNotably, reviewing the research \"filter tag\" for \"probe\" could be helpful, but isn't critical.**Planning test submission**\n\nI'm looking to create a test that counts parameters on a per-layer basis. However, I realize that this expansion might increase tokens. Since we have two experiments currently running, I can't submit anything new right now. I can write the test script for storage and inform Insight I about submitting on the next tick.\n\nThe plan includes writing a probe script to compute and save parameter counts in JSON format and\
  \ notifying Insight I to expect the submission. After that, we'll review 832 once it's finished. Writing to storage seems manageable for keeping token usage low!**Implementing probe script**\n\nI also considered the option to set '/execute_action{filter tag probes}', but it doesn't seem necessary right now. I can set the 'page_size' to 100 if we want to see scores, but I want to focus on robust contributions instead.\n\nMy action plan includes writing \"submission_probe_param_counts.py\" and messaging Insight I about the expected parameter count of 1,275,873 that has already been posted. \n\nNext, I'll create actions to store the script and inform them that the submission will happen after current runs finish. Writing an optional summary of next steps isn’t crucial, so I'll proceed with that. I’ll be using JAX/Flax for initialization and computing the parameter counts per module path.**Setting up traversal for parameter counting**\n\nI'm planning to traverse the parameter tree recursively,\
  \ where I’ll access each leaf parameter as a 'DeviceArray' to obtain the shape and size. I’ll accumulate counts based on the top-level path segments. I'll keep the path consistent, using keys from the Flax parameter tree like 'params/Conv_0/kernel', and save everything to 'storage/zephyr/results/probe_param_counts_pg.json'.\n\nAlso, I noticed the RL test-only returns \"evaluation failed: Test mode - no scoring,\" but I find that acceptable. I can write a brief analysis of the 830 results later, but for now, I’m ready to proceed!"
