- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/rin_synthesis_tick486.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  RIN synthesis (Tick 486)\n  - PG α sweep: best α=0.20 → 95.0 (Eval 821)\n  - PG depth @ α=0.20: steps={3,4,5} → best steps=4 (Eval 833, 94.7)\n  - PG value_loss_coef @ α=0.20: {0.50,0.55,0.60} → best 0.55 (Eval 830, 94.5)\n  - PPO α tests: α=0.25 → 94.6 (Eval 818), α=0.20 → 94.5 (Eval 824)\n  - Probes:\n    • Param counts (PG): total=1,275,873; gates Conv [3,3,128,256]; gates LN [256]\n    • Reset-masking: dip at forced prev_done; norms nonzero due to 4-step internal recurrence\n    • LN scan: only gate LNs present (no stray LN on z)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — RIN α=0.20 — head_hidden micro‑sweep {48,64,80} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, residual normalization, head width, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Test whether the optimal head MLP width shifts under RIN. Sweep head_hidden ∈ {48,64,80} with\
    \ fixed PG settings (lr=4e‑4, entropy=0.01, value_coef=0.55, grad‑clip=1.0), steps=4; LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP; α=0.20.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from submissions.submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([48, 64, 80]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return\
    \ PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PPO‑Clip — RIN α fine‑sweep {0.20,0.25} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP\"\ntags: \"ppo, residual normalization, convlstm, attention, generalization\"\nabstract: \"Direct head‑to‑head PPO test of α ∈ {0.20,0.25} for Residual Input‑Norm. PPO keys fixed: lr=4e‑4, entropy=0.01, value_coef=0.5,\
    \ clip=0.2, value_clip=0.2; grad‑clip=1.0; steps=4.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from submissions.submission_ppo_clip import training_step, create_optimizer as ppo_create_optimizer, BASE_SEED\n  from submissions.submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'clip_range': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'value_clip_range': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.20,\
    \ 0.25]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return ppo_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 31}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum 4: PG α=0.20 head width sweep + PPO α head‑to‑head\"\ncontent: |\n  We extend RIN analysis:\n  - PG (α=0.20) head_hidden sweep {48,64,80} submitted to test whether the\
    \ optimal head width shifts under RIN (baseline used 64).\n  - PPO (α ∈ {0.20,0.25}) submitted for a direct head‑to‑head comparison at fixed PPO settings (clip=0.2, value_clip=0.2, ent=0.01).\n  Synthesis (so far): PG best at α=0.20 (95.0, Eval 821); PPO is robust at α∈{0.20,0.25} (94.5–94.6, Evals 824, 818). Depth remains best at steps=4 under RIN (Eval 833). We will report the new head width and PPO α results once complete.\n```"
