parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/rin_updates_tick491.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 491 additions\n  - PG RIN α fine-sweep {0.15,0.18,0.20,0.22} (Eval 850): 94.1 mean; best trial at α=0.22 hit 0.957 single-seed. Conclusion: α≈0.20–0.22 plateau; 0.20 remains robust default (SOTA 95.0 at Eval 821).\n  - PPO RIN α fine-sweep {0.20,0.23,0.25} (Eval 851): 94.0 mean; best single-seed 0.956 @ α=0.23. Conclusion: PPO stable ~94.0–94.6; weak sensitivity to α.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — RIN α=0.20 — entropy fine‑sweep {0.009,0.010,0.011} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, residual input-norm, entropy, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Refine entropy around the standard 0.01 under RIN. α fixed at 0.20; entropy_coef ∈ {0.009,0.010,0.011}; other PG settings fixed (lr=4e‑4, value_coef=0.55, grad‑clip=1.0), steps=4; LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n\
    \  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from submissions.submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.009, 0.010, 0.011]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n\
    \          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — RIN α=0.20 — center_only vs standard (confirm) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, residual input-norm, ablation, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Confirm whether centering-only RIN (no scaling) matches full RIN at the optimal α under PG. α=0.20, center_only ∈ {False, True}; fixed PG settings and architecture.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from submissions.submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\
    \n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False, True]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n\
    \          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 31}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum 5 (Tick 491): α fine-sweeps and PG entropy refinement\"\ncontent: |\n  New results (Eval IDs in Research Counter):\n  - PG RIN α fine-sweep {0.15,0.18,0.20,0.22} → 94.1 mean overall; best single-seed 0.957 at α=0.22. Our prior SOTA holds at α=0.20 with 95.0 (Eval 821). Conclusion: α≈0.20–0.22 is a flat optimum; keep α=0.20 for parsimony.\n  - PPO RIN α fine-sweep {0.20,0.23,0.25} → 94.0 mean; best single-seed 0.956 @ α=0.23. Confirms PPO robustness (94.0–94.6) with weak sensitivity to α.\n  - Launched: PG entropy fine-sweep {0.009,0.010,0.011} at α=0.20, and PG\
    \ center_only vs standard at α=0.20 to confirm centering-only behavior at the optimum.\n\n  Takeaway: RIN is robust; small α/entropy tweaks yield marginal differences near the 95% frontier. We maintain α=0.20, entropy=0.01, head_hidden=64 as the parsimonious defaults; head_hidden=80 can yield strong single-seed scores but no mean uplift.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering experimental designs**\n\nI’m thinking about testing the RIN and input-LN synergy, though I might risk double normalization. There's already been a failure with advanced normalization and Huber degradation. I can propose trying a value loss coefficient of 0.55, which has been trending positively. Since we have no running experiments, we can submit two new ones. I’m considering comparing PG RIN with different entropy coefficients and possibly testing a center-only variant of RIN, though earlier results didn’t show improvement.**Planning experiments and logging**\n\nI’m considering a test of the PPO value_clip range micro-sweep at 0.15, 0.2, and 0.25 under RIN, since we haven’t done that yet. I also want to explore slight alpha interplay with head width of 80, since that performed best in our earlier tests. \n\nNext, I need to integrate training-phase probes and possibly propose R_vp logging during training, though it’s a bit complex. I’ll aim for periodic\
  \ gradient logging while ensuring it doesn’t interfere with the training process too much.**Developing a training variant**\n\nI’m considering a training variant that prints the gradient norm ratio from the last minibatch and writes it to a file, which should still count as part of the training. This approach isn't banned, but it’s essential to be cautious since the test environment limits heavy computation. I can implement a training_step wrapper to collect gradient norms using JAX features, but I must remember that while we can compute extra metrics, writing side effects isn't straightforward. Passing an aggregator in a static global could work, but it’s not the best solution.**Planning next experiments**\n\nI'm contemplating another experiment comparing RIN α to Input-LN synergy under PG. The idea is to add an external Input LN while keeping gate LN and RIN to analyze synergy vs. redundancy. However, earlier results showed that \"Input LayerNorm before ConvLSTM had a score of 93.4,\"\
  \ while RIN improved to 95.0, so this might not yield much.\n\nI want to evaluate GroupNorm as input normalization with RIN, but I worry it might degrade performance. The focus now should be on the Synthesis step, to publish a revised paper documenting our new SOTA results, including careful ablations and reproduction details. I'll create an Archive for this update.**Planning next steps and experiments**\n\nNext, I need to update Archive #31 with a summary of new results, including evaluation IDs and statistics. I’ll mention the optimum α at 0.20, and that PPO α at 0.23 had a top seed of 0.956. \n\nThen, I'll queue two experiments: a micro-sweep for entropy coefficients and testing the center-only variant under PG. I also want to evaluate alternate clip norms under RIN. After that, I’ll ensure the training steps and hyperparameters are set correctly for the experiments, and I’ll keep an eye on token usage which is currently at 103k. Let's implement these actions efficiently!**Preparing\
  \ final message**\n\nI should definitely add some reflective text before issuing commands, since the interface supports free-form text. It’s important to keep it concise so that the user can quickly grasp the context. \n\nI’ll construct a final message that summarizes the key points and then present the command lines clearly. That way, everything will be organized and easy to follow. Let’s make sure we communicate effectively before executing those commands!"
