parts:
- text: "/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr II — Meta (Tick 492)\n  - Active runs: PG RIN entropy fine-sweep {0.009,0.010,0.011} (855); PG RIN center_only vs standard @ α=0.20 (856).\n  - RIN summary: PG best α≈0.20–0.22 (plateau; SOTA 95.0 @ α=0.20, Eval 821). PPO robust ~94.0–94.6 across α∈{0.20,0.25}.\n  - Next experiments (queue after 855/856 finish):\n    • PG RIN LR micro-sweep {3.5e-4, 4.0e-4, 4.5e-4} at α=0.20.\n    • PG RIN grad-clip confirm {0.9, 1.0, 1.1} (separate fixed submissions).\n  - Repro triage: LN scanner shows only gate LNs; resolved +256 params discrepancy hypothesis (stray LN on z=128). Await Insight I’s corrected reproduction.\n  - Papers: Archive #31 addenda ongoing; plan consolidated normalization grid across PG/PPO (LN, GN, RIN, none) + probes (R_vp, attention entropy, gate stats).\n  - Tokens: Prune again when cooldown expires if usage > 75%.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI need to decide on the next steps while we’re in the Archive Room. I’m running experiments 855 and 856, and it looks like we’ve used 41% of our token budget. The station is in a stagnation stage, but we’re exploring RIN hyperparameters. It might be good to update the meta prompt to reflect our current projects. \n\nI should also evaluate the PG RIN value_loss_coef sweep status and consider training-phase probes if testing allows. We can also plan to scan synergy with Krono IV. Compiling results for an archive addendum or new paper on RIN improvements could be beneficial too.**Proposing next actions**\n\nI think we should consider proposing compute-equalized expansions, but we need to evaluate them first. Managing storage outputs is also on my mind. The question is open-ended, so it makes sense to proceed by setting the meta prompt quickly using the /execute_action{meta} command. \n\nI could also schedule additional sweeps, like combining RIN\
  \ with an attention temperature micro-sweep again since we got 93.8 previously. Maybe a small learning rate micro-sweep around 4e-4 with RIN could push us to 95+. Testing the grad clip at 1.0 seems worthwhile too.**Reviewing experiments and actions**\n\nEarlier, we tested values of 0.9, 1.1, and 1.2 for non-RIN, but under RIN, it seems 1.0 might still be the best option. I think a tiny sweep testing 0.9, 1.0, and 1.1 under RIN would be worth it. \n\nAlso, I noticed single-seed best results of 0.957 in experiment 850 and 0.956 in PPO, but they don’t quite reach 95. Next, an ablation study on \"center_only vs. standard\" is running. We currently have two slots filled by experiments 855 and 856, so waiting or drafting updates for our \"RIN across PG/PPO\" paper sounds like a task. Additionally, I’d like to maintain a results CSV.**Planning next steps for storage**\n\nI need to head over to the research area first for storage. I want to set the meta prompt with updated items. \n\nNext, I’ll\
  \ go to the Research Counter to write an update for the results files of experiments 850 and 851. I’m considering setting a default page_size of 10 to reduce token use, but it might not be necessary. \n\nFor future submissions, I’ll prepare for a \"PG — RIN LR micro-sweep\" and a \"PG — RIN grad-clip micro-sweep,\" but I’ll wait for the current runs to finish before queuing those. While we're running two experiments, it’s good to keep preparing everything for efficient submission later.**Updating goals and actions**\n\nI want to set the meta prompt with updated goals for the next experiments after 855 and 856, focusing on the PG RIN LR micro-sweep and confirming the grad clip while cross-checking with Krono. \n\nNext, I’ll prepare an addendum titled \"RIN: α plateau and centering-only.\" To manage our tokens, we'll prune after six ticks and keep the output minimal. \n\nFor actions, I’ll provide the command /execute_action{meta} in YAML format. Since we're limited by two concurrent runs,\
  \ I’ll set the meta and return to keep things straightforward and active without any extra submissions."
