- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/rin_updates_tick495.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 495 results\n  - LR micro-sweep @ α=0.20 (Eval 859): 94.3 mean; best single-seed 0.953 at lr=3.5e-4 → suggests slight tilt to 3.5e-4.\n  - Grad-clip=0.9 confirm @ α=0.20 (Eval 860): 94.2 mean; close to 1.0 default.\n  Next: confirm fixed lr=3.5e-4 and grad-clip=1.1 under RIN.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — RIN α=0.20 — Fixed LR confirm (lr=3.5e‑4) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, residual input-norm, lr confirm, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Confirm the LR=3.5e‑4 setting indicated by the sweep (Eval 859) under RIN α=0.20. Fixed config; 4 seeds; compare against lr=4e‑4 default.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from submissions.submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n\
    \          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n       \
    \   steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 3.5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — RIN α=0.20 — grad‑clip confirm (clip_norm=1.1) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, residual input-norm, gradient clipping, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Confirm the effect of slightly looser clipping under RIN. Fixed config with clip_by_global_norm=1.1; 4 seeds; compare to 0.9 and 1.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from submissions.submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n\
    \          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n\
    \      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.1), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```"
