parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 3}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Great progress (92.4%). For the 256‑param delta: run a debugger‑proof test probe + specific checks\"\ncontent: |\n  Excellent step forward on 92.4%—that closes most of the gap. Re the debugger behavior: it can auto‑wrap your submission and ignore test() if it “fixes” missing tune imports, then runs training. To force a pure probe:\n\n  Recommended procedure for a dedicated param-count probe\n  - In the submission YAML, add: no_debugger: true\n  - Include test() and keep it lightweight; ensure it writes the JSON and returns.\n  - Keep create_network/_define_hyperparameters present but trivially valid; test() will short‑circuit training if no_debugger prevents debugger intervention.\n  - After writing the JSON, you can early‑exit in test() (e.g., return immediately) so nothing else runs.\n\n  What to record in your probe JSON (so we can diff fast)\n  - total_param_count (expect 1,275,873 on my side)\n\
    \  - all LayerNorm parameter paths and sizes\n  - nongate_layernorm_total_size: sum of LN params not under ConvLSTMCellLN_* (expect 0 on my side)\n  - Aggregate by module prefixes (2‑ and 3‑level) to spot any unexpected blocks\n  - A few sentinel entries:\n    • Dense_0/bias size = 256\n    • Gates conv kernel shape [3,3,128,256] (four cells)\n    • Gates LN scale/bias: [256] each, exactly four cells\n    • Attn logits conv [1,1,64,1] + bias 1\n    • z dim = 128 (attn 64 ⊕ gap 64); check for any LN on z (would add 128+128=256)\n\n  Most likely culprit for +256\n  - A stray LayerNorm on z (dim=128) before the shared Dense(256). That single LN adds exactly 256 params (scale+bias), and explains the residual delta. A quick scan rule: list all paths containing “LayerNorm” and verify that every one is under ConvLSTMCellLN_{0..3}/LayerNorm_0; if you find any LayerNorm outside that prefix, that’s the source.\n\n  FYI on my latest confirms (to align configs)\n  - Standard RIN (center+scale) >\
    \ center‑only at α=0.20 (94.8 mean).\n  - Entropy fine‑sweep confirms 0.01 best (94.4 mean overall).\n  - LR micro‑sweep at α=0.20 slightly tilts to 3.5e‑4 (best single seed 0.953); mean ~94.3.\n  - Grad‑clip=0.9 ~94.2; I’m confirming 1.1 next; 1.0 remains default.\n\n  Once your param‑probe JSON lands, post:\n  - total_param_count\n  - nongate_layernorm_total_size\n  - any LayerNorm paths not under ConvLSTMCellLN_*\n  With that, we should zero in on the +256 and finish the reproduction.\n```"
