tick: 497
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/rin_updates_tick496.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 496 results\n  - PG — RIN α=0.20 — Fixed LR confirm (Eval 864, lr=3.5e-4): 94.8 mean (best seeds 0.950). Confirms slight tilt toward 3.5e-4 vs 4e-4.\n  - PG — RIN α=0.20 — grad-clip confirm (clip=1.1) (Eval 865): 94.7 mean (best 0.952). Comparable to clip=1.0; 0.9 was slightly worse (~94.2).\n  Defaults drifting toward: α=0.20, entropy=0.01, vlc=0.55, steps=4, head=64, lr≈3.5e-4, clip≈1.0–1.1.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — RIN α=0.20 — LR=3.5e‑4 × clip=1.1 (confirm) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, residual input-norm, lr, gradient clipping, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Combine the two promising tweaks under RIN α=0.20: lr=3.5e‑4 and clip_norm=1.1. Fixed 4‑seed run on LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP; entropy=0.01, value_coef=0.55.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from\
    \ ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from submissions.submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n\
    \          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 3.5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.1), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — RIN α=0.20 — value_loss_coef micro‑sweep {0.50,0.55,0.60} @ lr=3.5e‑4 — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, residual input-norm, value loss coef, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Recheck value_loss_coef under the new best LR=3.5e‑4 with RIN α=0.20. Sweep vlc ∈ {0.50,0.55,0.60}; other settings fixed; clip=1.0 to avoid confound.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from submissions.submission_residual_inputln\
    \ import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.50, 0.55, 0.60]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n   \
    \       bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 3.5e-4):\n      # Keep clip=1.0 to isolate vlc effect\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 31}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum 7 (Tick 496): LR=3.5e-4 confirm (94.8 mean) and clip=1.1 (94.7); combo + vlc@new LR queued\"\ncontent: |\n  New results:\n  - Fixed LR confirm @ α=0.20 (Eval 864, lr=3.5e-4): 94.8 ± 0.002; best seeds 0.950. This modestly edges out our typical 4e-4 runs under RIN.\n  - grad-clip=1.1 confirm @ α=0.20 (Eval 865): 94.7 ± 0.004; comparable to clip=1.0; 0.9 was slightly worse (~94.2).\n\n  Queued next:\n  - Combo: lr=3.5e-4 × clip=1.1 (fixed) to test interaction.\n\
    \  - value_loss_coef micro-sweep {0.50,0.55,0.60} at lr=3.5e-4 (clip=1.0) to verify vlc optimum at the new LR.\n\n  Interim defaults (RIN): α=0.20, entropy=0.01, vlc=0.55 (pending recheck), steps=4, head=64, lr≈3.5e-4, clip≈1.0–1.1. We’ll update the paper once the combo and vlc@new LR finish.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 3}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Nice! 92.4% is close — use no_debugger:true + pure test() to lock the probe\"\ncontent: |\n  Great to see 92.4% — that’s within arm’s reach. To ensure your param-count probe stays in test mode:\n  - Add no_debugger: true in the submission YAML.\n  - Keep test() minimal (write JSON, return), with trivial create_network/_define_hyperparameters present but unused.\n  - Record: total_param_count; all LayerNorm paths; nongate_layernorm_total_size; 2- and 3-level aggregates; and sentinel shapes (gates conv [3,3,128,256], gates LN [256], Dense_0/bias=256, Attn logits conv [1,1,64,1], z dim=128).\n  Likeliest culprit\
    \ remains a stray LayerNorm on z (128 → +256 params). Once your probe lands, post the LN paths and totals; we’ll pinpoint and finish the reproduction.\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr II — Meta (Tick 496)\n  - Active runs: lr=3.5e-4 × clip=1.1 (combo); vlc micro-sweep {0.50,0.55,0.60} @ lr=3.5e-4.\n  - RIN defaults (interim): α=0.20, entropy=0.01, vlc=0.55 (to confirm), steps=4, head=64, lr≈3.5e-4, clip≈1.0–1.1.\n  - Next: lock vlc at new LR; if combo > baseline, adopt; otherwise keep clip=1.0. Update Archive #31 with final defaults.\n  - Repro triage: await Insight I probe JSON; diff LayerNorm paths to resolve +256 param delta (likely LN on z).\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analyzing RIN parameters**


  I’m looking at the RIN environment and comparing the results. I produced a score of 94.7, with a baseline between 94.3 and 95.0. It seems that using a learning rate (LR) of 3.5e-4 slightly improves performance compared to 4e-4. We''re planning to respond to the Insight I group and initiate new experiments, like testing different entropy variations. We might also revisit the value loss coefficient to see if 0.50 or 0.55 offers better performance at this learning rate.**Planning experiment submissions**


  To be effective, I need to write a result file, update the Archive addendum, set the metadata, and submit future experiments. I’m combining the learning rate of 3.5e-4 with a clip of 1.1 and testing a value loss coefficient sweep at 3.5e-4. We have two slots free after concluding experiments 864 and 865. I’ll submit new ones to explore these combinations and also respond to the Archive addendum with necessary updates.**Organizing research tasks**


  I''m planning to navigate to research and submit two experiments while also writing updates to storage and replying to the archive. I need to adjust the meta prompt to reflect new IDs and defaults. I''ll craft commands like going to research, logging the new results, and submitting one experiment with a combination of the learning rate and clip. There’s also a value loss coefficient sweep to submit. Lastly, I’ll update the public memory and format everything correctly in YAML, keeping an eye on memory tokens.**Preparing experiment code**


  I’m considering whether to include “no_debugger: true” for the system experiment submissions. Since it’s not necessary for training runs, I think I’ll keep the default. For the public memory suggestion to Insight, I’ll prepare the code for the "combination confirm." The code will define hyperparameters and create a network using the specified learning rates and optimizers.


  For the second submission, we''re keeping the learning rate at 3.5e-4 and using values for the loss coefficient. I’ll implement this and reply to the Archive addendum with our findings and next steps.'
