role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_probe_init_rvp_rin.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Test-only probe: Init R_vp (||∇_trunk L_value|| / ||∇_trunk L_policy||)\n  Compares baseline PG_Stepped_AttnGap vs RIN (α=0.20) at initialization.\n  Writes JSON: storage/zephyr/results/probe_init_rvp_rin.json\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from submissions.submission_pg_quadstep import PG_Stepped_AttnGap\n  from submissions.submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  def _flatten_leaves(tree):\n    out = []\n    def rec(path, node):\n      if isinstance(node, dict):\n        for k, v in node.items():\n          rec(path + [k], v)\n      else:\n        out.append((\"/\".join(path), node))\n    rec([], tree)\n    return out\n\n  def _is_head_param(path: str):\n    # Treat shared Dense_0 as trunk; exclude policy/value\
    \ head layers Dense_1..Dense_4\n    return any(seg in path for seg in [\"Dense_1\", \"Dense_2\", \"Dense_3\", \"Dense_4\"])\n\n  def _trunk_grad_norm(grads_tree):\n    # grads_tree is a FrozenDict or dict under \"params\"\n    tree = grads_tree.unfreeze() if hasattr(grads_tree, \"unfreeze\") else grads_tree\n    if \"params\" in tree:\n      tree = tree[\"params\"]\n    s2 = 0.0\n    for path, g in _flatten_leaves(tree):\n      if g is None:\n        continue\n      if _is_head_param(path):\n        continue\n      s2 += float(jnp.vdot(g, g))\n    return float(jnp.sqrt(s2))\n\n  def _policy_value_losses(net, params, obs, done, rng):\n    logits, value, _ = net.apply(params, obs, done, None, rngs=None)\n    # Random actions (4-way) and simple policy loss (advantages=1)\n    key_a, _ = random.split(rng)\n    acts = random.randint(key_a, (obs.shape[0],), 0, 4)\n    logp_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n    logp = logp_all[jnp.arange(obs.shape[0]), acts]\n    L_pi = -jnp.mean(logp)\n\
    \    # Value loss to 0 target\n    L_v = 0.5 * jnp.mean(value ** 2)\n    return L_pi, L_v\n\n  def _rvp_for_network(net, init_key, obs, done):\n    params = net.init(init_key, obs, done, None)\n    # Compute grads of trunk for each loss separately\n    def loss_pi(p):\n      L_pi, _ = _policy_value_losses(net, p, obs, done, init_key)\n      return L_pi\n    def loss_v(p):\n      _, L_v = _policy_value_losses(net, p, obs, done, init_key)\n      return L_v\n    g_pi = jax.grad(loss_pi)(params)\n    g_v  = jax.grad(loss_v)(params)\n    norm_pi = _trunk_grad_norm(g_pi)\n    norm_v  = _trunk_grad_norm(g_v)\n    rvp = norm_v / max(norm_pi, 1e-8)\n    return dict(norm_policy=norm_pi, norm_value=norm_v, R_vp=rvp)\n\n  def test():\n    key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n    B, H, W, C = 16, 8, 8, 8\n    obs = random.normal(key, (B, H, W, C), dtype=jnp.float32)\n    done = jnp.zeros((B,), dtype=jnp.bool_)\n\n    # Baseline (no RIN)\n    net_baseline = PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n      cnn_features_1=32, cnn_features_2=64,\n\
    \      convlstm_features=64, dilation=6,\n      bottleneck_ratio=0.28, head_hidden=64, steps=4\n    )\n    # RIN (α=0.20)\n    net_rin = PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n      cnn_features_1=32, cnn_features_2=64,\n      convlstm_features=64, dilation=6,\n      bottleneck_ratio=0.28, head_hidden=64, steps=4,\n      alpha=0.20, center_only=False\n    )\n\n    res_baseline = _rvp_for_network(net_baseline, random.PRNGKey(1), obs, done)\n    res_rin      = _rvp_for_network(net_rin,      random.PRNGKey(2), obs, done)\n\n    out = {\n      \"baseline\": res_baseline,\n      \"rin_alpha_0.20\": res_rin,\n      \"notes\": \"R_vp = ||grad_trunk(value)|| / ||grad_trunk(policy)|| at initialization, random batch; heads excluded (Dense_1..Dense_4).\"\n    }\n    path = \"storage/zephyr/results/probe_init_rvp_rin.json\"\n    with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n      json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n    print(\"Saved R_vp init probe to\", path)\n    return out\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"\
    Probe (test-only) — Init R_vp: RIN α=0.20 vs baseline (trunk grads)\"\ntags: \"mechanistic probes, normalization, gradients, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Measures R_vp = ||∇_trunk L_value|| / ||∇_trunk L_policy|| at initialization for baseline vs RIN(α=0.20). Heads excluded. Writes to storage/zephyr/results/probe_init_rvp_rin.json.\"\nno_debugger: true\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from submissions.submission_probe_init_rvp_rin import test\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning experiment submissions**\n\nI'm pondering whether to avoid blocking submissions until my current run is done. The probe can go to storage, but I can only submit after completion. I read I can submit another experiment while waiting, so they'll just queue up. I can update the Archive with results and confirm parameters. Checking token usage shows I'm fine, having used 142k out of 270k. I'll create the test-only probe code but wait to submit since both slots are busy.**Setting up storage and submissions**\n\nI'm defining the content for 'submission_probe_init_rvp_rin.py' to include both networks and the test function. I also want to create a plan in 'TODO_next.md.' \n\nFirst, I'll navigate to Public Memory, then write the probe script. For submission, I’ll title it \"Probe (test-only) — Init R_vp: RIN α=0.20 vs baseline\" and set it up with import details and the optional field `no_debugger: true` to confirm it's test-only. I need to check that the code works\
  \ under the standard import path. Do I have any more experiments to consider?**Preparing test code and loss calculations**\n\nI have two slots filled, but that's okay since the test-only submissions will just queue up. I’m considering whether to set the page size back to default, but maybe it’s unnecessary for now. I plan to update the Archive addendum after everything finishes, not right away.\n\nNext, I'll craft the test code. I'll import PG_Stepped_AttnGap and PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN. I'll create a random batch with B=16 environments and set T=20 unroll, but since testing can be simpler, I'll opt for a single step instead. \n\nFor the network's forward signature, I need to ensure the observation shape is [B,H,W,C] while computing logits and values. To compute gradients for the trunk modules, I’ll define a dummy loss function with random actions for calculations.**Setting up trunk parameters and metrics**\n\nI need to identify the trunk parameter paths. I’ll convert the frozen dictionary\
  \ to a nested format and filter out specific keys that start with 'Dense_1', 'Dense_2', 'Dense_3', and 'Dense_4', which are head modules. Instead, I’ll include paths like 'Conv_*', 'BottleneckDilatedBlock_*', 'ConvLSTMCell*', 'Conv_2', and 'Dense_0' among others.\n\nNext, I’ll create helper functions to flatten the leaves and compute the norms. I want to save metrics for both networks to 'probe_init_rvp_rin.json.' It’s test-only, so compliance with allowed domain knowledge shouldn’t be an issue. \n\nThen, I’ll lay out the actions: moving to research, writing the probe file, submitting the test-only with `no_debugger: true`, and perhaps adding a concise note to Public Memory. I'll keep messaging brief and focused, and also remember to use `jax.grad` for value and gradient calculations.**Implementing loss function details**\n\nI need to implement the `loss_policy(params)` function to compute logits using `network.apply(params, obs, done, None)`. It's crucial to initialize the RNN state for\
  \ both networks. The `network.apply` likely returns the RNN state, and it's okay to provide `None` or done parameters as zeros. \n\nFirst, I'll generate observations using `jax.random.normal(key, (B,8,8,8))` and set done to zeros while making the actions random integers from 0 to 4.\n\nThen, for each network, I'll initialize the parameters and compute the loss functions. I’ll use `jax.grad` for calculating the gradients, sum the squared norms for the trunk leaves, and return a dictionary containing `r_vp = norm_value / norm_policy`. I'll make sure to include the `dtype` as float32 and then produce the final output."
