- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Probe (test-only) — Init R_vp: RIN α=0.20 vs baseline (trunk grads)\"\ntags: \"mechanistic probes, normalization, gradients, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Measures R_vp = ||∇_trunk L_value|| / ||∇_trunk L_policy|| at initialization for baseline vs RIN(α=0.20). Heads excluded. Writes to storage/zephyr/results/probe_init_rvp_rin.json.\"\nno_debugger: true\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from submissions.submission_probe_init_rvp_rin import test\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/rin_updates_tick499.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 499 results\n  - Combo (lr=3.5e-4 × clip=1.1) @ α=0.20 (Eval 869): 94.7 mean (best 0.951). No uplift over separate confirms.\n  - vlc micro-sweep @ lr=3.5e-4 (Eval 870): 94.5 mean; best vlc=0.55. Confirms vlc=0.55.\n  Current picture:\n  • Best mean so far remains 95.0 (Eval 821, α=0.20, lr=4e-4, clip=1.0).\n  • Close alternates: lr=3.5e-4 yields 94.8; clip=1.1 yields\
    \ 94.7; combo 94.7.\n  Defaults: α=0.20, entropy=0.01, vlc=0.55, steps=4, head=64, clip=1.0, lr=4e-4 (3.5e-4 acceptable alternative).\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — RIN α=0.20 — Final defaults confirm (lr=4e‑4, clip=1.0) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, residual input-norm, confirm, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Confirm final default config under RIN: α=0.20, lr=4e‑4, clip=1.0, vlc=0.55, entropy=0.01; 4 seeds on LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from submissions.submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\
    \ optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning experiments and defaults**\n\nI’m thinking about our next steps for experiments. We should confirm the final defaults with a specific seed run: LR=3.5e-4, clip=1.0, α=0.20, vlc=0.55, as 1.1 didn’t show improvement. \n\nSince we just utilized concurrency, we have 2 slots open. I want to run a \"Final defaults confirm\" to ensure our config that verifies the best mean of 95.0 and consider using LR=4e-4 since it showed slightly better performance.**Evaluating actions and plans**\n\nI’m considering adding a \"Final baseline confirm\" for α=0.20, lr=4e-4, clip=1.0 just to try and reproduce our previous mean of 95.0, but since we've already evaluated 821, it might not be necessary.\n\nAlternatively, we could assess the head widths of 64 vs. 80 at lr=3.5e-4 to check for improvement, though the 80 width didn’t help earlier. \n\nRegarding the \"Stagnation Protocol,\" we should think about updating the archive while adhering to the environment's instruction style. \n\n\
  Also, we need to reply to Insight I in Public Memory to provide guidance about no_debugger: true and mention that concurrency has been freed, though we covered that previously. \n\nFinally, my token management shows we're at 146,868 tokens used (54%), so I need to produce an answer with appropriate action lines, keeping verbosity low.**Planning next steps**\n\nFrom the last \"Room Output,\" I see we're in Research Counter and not actively running experiments. I think we should propose a few actions:\n\nFirst, let's submit the test-only R_vp probe now. Then, I need to write a summary of results for ticks 497/499. \n\nNext, maybe I could set a final default note or plan. Scheduling a \"Final default confirm\" run with parameters α=0.20, lr=4e-4, and clip 1.0 could be useful, but it's not strictly necessary.\n\nSince we have two slots available, using one for the probe means the other can be for the confirm, especially since test-only submissions are quick. We can even submit a second experiment\
  \ in the same turn!**Submitting tests and experiments**\n\nThe system states that during tests, the station will deliver the questions before my turn ends. Research submissions, however, process sequentially without blocking. \n\nSince there are currently no running submissions, I can submit both a test-only and one training experiment. \n\nFor the training experiment, I consider \"Final default confirm\" with parameters α=0.20, lr=4e-4, clip=1.0, vlc=0.55, and steps=4. We’ve run many similar tests before, with the best being eval 821 with a result of 95.0. Another confirm might yield results around 94.6–95.1 due to randomness. \n\nI could also queue \"center_only vs standard Additional\" at α=0.18 or α=0.22, but that doesn't seem necessary. Keeping a slot open aligns with the station's encouragement to avoid idleness, although the test-only submission uses minimal resources.**Organizing submission and results**\n\nI can store the \"probe_init_rvp_rin\" results once the evaluation is complete,\
  \ though I can’t read them until the next tick. \n\nI’ll submit the test-only probe using `/execute_action{submit 1}` with no_debugger: true, referencing the previously stored module. Since both evaluations 869 and 870 are free now, I’ll resend the probe.\n\nThe YAML will have the title: \"Probe (test-only) — Init R_vp: RIN vs baseline\" along with tags and content to run the test. I might also log results for LR confirmation and update the Archive addendum if necessary. \n\nAfterwards, I plan to submit the results summary file for tick 499 and possibly queue a \"Final defaults confirm\" run while keeping track of concurrency. With a free slot after the test-only submission, I’ll run \"Final PG baseline at α=0.20, lr=4e-4, clip 1.0\" to maintain the top mean of 95. \n\nFinally, I’ll prepare the necessary hyperparameters and summaries before finalizing the submission."
