- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/rin_updates_tick501.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 501 notes\n  - Final-defaults confirm (873, α=0.20, lr=4e-4, clip=1.0): 93.5 mean; one seed under-updated (33.9k vs ~38.9k) likely dragged mean. Treat as outlier.\n  - Stable high means:\n    • lr=3.5e-4, clip=1.0 → 94.8 (864)\n    • clip=1.1 (lr=4e-4) → 94.7 (865)\n    • combo (3.5e-4 × 1.1) → 94.7 (869)\n    • vlc @ lr=3.5e-4 → best 0.55 (870, 94.5)\n  - Decision: adopt lr=3.5e-4, clip=1.0 as defaults under RIN α=0.20; 4e-4 remains acceptable alt.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — RIN α fine‑sweep {0.19,0.20,0.21} @ lr=3.5e‑4, clip=1.0 — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, residual input-norm, alpha sweep, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Refine α around 0.20 under the new default lr=3.5e‑4, clip=1.0. α ∈ {0.19,0.20,0.21}; fixed vlc=0.55, entropy=0.01; steps=4; LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP.\"\ncontent: |\n  import\
    \ sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from submissions.submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.19, 0.20, 0.21]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n\
    \          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 3.5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — RIN α=0.20 — grad‑clip confirm (clip_norm=1.05) @ lr=3.5e‑4 — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, residual input-norm, gradient clipping, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Test intermediate clipping (1.05) under RIN α=0.20 with lr=3.5e‑4. Fixed config; compare against clip=1.0 (94.8) and 1.1 (94.7).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from\
    \ submissions.submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n\
    \          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 3.5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.05), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 31}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum 9 (Tick 501): Defaults set to lr=3.5e‑4, clip=1.0; α/clip micro‑checks queued\"\ncontent: |\n  Update after final-defaults confirm (873) came in low (93.5 mean; one seed under-updated):\n  - We adopt lr=3.5e-4, clip=1.0 as RIN defaults (α=0.20, vlc=0.55, entropy=0.01, steps=4, head=64), based on stable 94.8 (864) and supporting ablations (865/869/870).\n  - Queued micro-checks at lr=3.5e-4: α ∈ {0.19,0.20,0.21} and clip=1.05 to finalize tiny refinements.\n  - Init probe shows RIN raises R_vp (value/policy\
    \ trunk-grad ratio) at init, consistent with robustness near 95%.\n  We will lock the table and figures once these checks finish.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing performance drop**\n\nI'm noticing a big drop in performance. It might be due to changes in the training_step code or maybe the aggregator has shifted. The logs show consistent behavior, though; the issue might lie in cluster limits. Other runs had values around 94.7-94.8, so 93.5 seems low and possibly an outlier. Seed 4 timed out at 33901 updates rather than the normal 38901, which could explain the lower performance. This suggests fewer updates may indeed lead to a drop in performance.**Evaluating learning rates**\n\nThe mean dropped to 93.5, which is lower but still within a reasonable variation, so it’s not time to panic. I think we should keep the default learning rate at 4e-4 or consider adopting 3.5e-4, which has shown slightly better results at 94.8. The outlier at 873 with 93.5 encourages that change. I plan to update the metadata accordingly and finalize the archive. Additionally, I’ll conduct a small micro-sweep to check clip values. Keeping it\
  \ all concise is key!**Planning next actions**\n\nI need to write a results update summarizing the 873 regression, noting the score of 93.5 and interpreting it as variance from lower updates on one seed. I'll start using a learning rate of 3.5e-4 and set the clip to 1.0 as my default.  \n\nNext, I'll submit two experiments: the first being PG RIN with α=0.20, using the same learning rate and clip for replication. I remember the previous logs and need to verify if clip 1.0 was set in earlier adjustments.**Planning experiments and updates**\n\nSince the previous results were 94.8, there's no need to reconfirm, but I think we can refine things by setting up a “PG RIN α=0.20” clip micro-sweep at lr=3.5e-4. I also want to try a “PG RIN α fine-sweep around 0.20” with values {0.19, 0.20, 0.21} to confirm a plateau.  \n\nI'll update Archive #31 with the final defaults and refresh the metadata. My action plan includes writing results on the experiment drop, submitting the micro-sweeps, and responding\
  \ with the addendum to Archive #31. I'll be mindful about concurrency issues while submitting!**Executing actions and submissions**\n\nAt tick 501, it looks like there are no running experiments, but I can see that evaluation 873 has finished with a score of 93.5, meaning both slots are free now. Great!  \n\nI’ll navigate to the Research Counter to submit two new experiments. One will be a \"PG — RIN α=0.20 — grad-clip micro-sweep {1.0, 1.05}\" at lr=3.5e-4. Since varying clip isn't directly supported in the optimizer, I'll keep it as a fixed parameter.  \n\nFor the second submission, I'll do a \"PG — RIN α fine-sweep {0.19, 0.20, 0.21}\" at the same learning rate and clip. I'll also log the results and update Archive #31 with an addendum. I'll ensure to format everything correctly with the YAML rules!"
