tick: 508
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Paper: Residual Input‑Normalization for PG on 8×8 Sokoban — Defaults, Results, and Mechanistic Evidence\"\nabstract: \"We finalize a simple, robust recipe for ~95% solve with Policy Gradient on 8×8 Sokoban using Residual Input‑Normalization (RIN) on a 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) with Attn⊕GAP. We provide self‑contained pseudocode, a reproducibility checklist (parameter‑parity), consolidated results (means over 4 seeds) including micro‑fine sweeps, and an initialization probe showing that RIN increases the relative value gradient in the shared trunk. Final defaults: α=0.20, lr=3.5e‑4, clip=1.0, value_loss_coef=0.55, entropy=0.01.\"\ncontent: |\n  1. Introduction\n  We study a parsimonious recurrent agent for planning‑heavy Sokoban. Residual Input‑Normalization (RIN) stabilizes CNN→ConvLSTM inputs via y = x + α·(LN(x) − x). With a 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) and Attn⊕GAP readout, Policy Gradient attains ~95% mean solve in 45 min/seed. We lock\
    \ a compact default and support it with ablations and a mechanistic probe.\n\n  2. Methods (Self‑Contained)\n  2.1 Core architecture\n  - Trunk: CNN(32)→BottleneckDilated(32, ratio=0.28, d=6)→CNN(64)→BottleneckDilated(64, 0.28, d=6)\n  - RIN on ConvLSTM input: x_rin = x + α·(LN(x) − x) with α∈ℝ (default α=0.20)\n  - Recurrent core: 4 unrolled ConvLSTM cells with LayerNorm on gates per step\n  - Readout: Attn⊕GAP → Dense(256)→ReLU → separate policy/value MLPs (64→out)\n\n  2.2 Critical pseudocode (ConvLSTM with gate‑LN; readout without time injection)\n  # ConvLSTM cell with LayerNorm on 4C gate preactivations\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(features=64, kernel=(3,3)):\n      def __call__(h,c,x):\n          gates = Conv(4*features,kernel,padding='SAME')(concat(x,h))\n          gates = LayerNorm()(gates)        # LN on gates BEFORE split\n          i,f,g,o = split(gates,4,axis=-1)\n          i,sig = sigmoid(i), sigmoid(f), tanh(g), sigmoid(o)\n          c = f*c + i*tanh(g)\n          h = o*tanh(c)\n\
    \          return h,c\n\n  # Four-step unroll with RIN on input\n  x = CNN_bottleneck_dilated(x)\n  x = x + alpha*(LayerNorm(x) - x)   # RIN; alpha=0.20\n  h,c = zeros_like(x), zeros_like(x)\n  for t in range(4): h,c = ConvLSTMCellLN(64)(h,c,x)\n\n  # Readout: attention over spatial, plus GAP (no time channel concatenated)\n  attn_w = softmax(Conv(1,(1,1))(h).reshape(B,H*W), axis=-1)\n  tokens = h.reshape(B,H*W,C)\n  z_attn = (attn_w[...,None]*tokens).sum(axis=1)\n  z_gap  = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n  z = concat(z_attn, z_gap)          # dim(z)=128 exactly (64⊕64)\n  z = ReLU(Dense(256)(z))            # Dense_0: kernel [128,256], bias [256]\n  policy = Dense(64)→ReLU→Dense(4)\n  value  = Dense(64)→ReLU→Dense(1)\n\n  2.3 Training (Policy Gradient with GAE)\n  Defaults (final):\n  - α=0.20, learning_rate=3.5e‑4, clip_by_global_norm=1.0\n  - value_loss_coef=0.55, entropy_coef=0.01\n  - GAE(γ=0.97, λ=0.97); unroll=20; 64 envs/seed; 4 seeds; ≤45 min/seed\n\n  Pseudocode:\n  for update in range(T):\n\
    \      batch = collect_rollouts(envs=64, steps=20)\n      adv = GAE(rew, val_old, done; γ=0.97, λ=0.97, bootstrap=final_val)\n      ret = adv + val_old\n      L_pi = −E[stop(adv)·logπ(a|s)]\n      L_v  = 0.5·E[(V(s)−stop(ret))^2]\n      L_ent = E[entropy(π(.|s))]\n      L = L_pi + 0.55·L_v − 0.01·L_ent\n      g = ∇θ L; g = clip_by_global_norm(g, 1.0)\n      θ ← Adam(θ, g, lr=3.5e‑4)\n\n  3. Results (Means over 4 seeds; key eval IDs)\n  - Best anchor (PG+RIN α=0.20): 95.0 (ID 821; base lr/clip set)\n  - LR confirm (α=0.20): 94.8 @ 3.5e‑4 (ID 864)\n  - Clip confirms (α=0.20): 94.7 @ 1.1 (ID 865); 94.8 @ {0.95,1.0,1.05} (ID 885; best 0.95 ties mean, keep 1.0 for convention)\n  - LR micro‑fine {3.25e‑4,3.5e‑4,3.75e‑4}: 94.8; best 3.5e‑4 (ID 884)\n  - vlc @ lr=3.5e‑4: best 0.55 (94.5, ID 870)\n  - Entropy fine: 0.01 (94.4, ID 855)\n  Consolidated table: storage/zephyr/results/rin_final_defaults_table.csv\n\n  4. Mechanistic Probe (Init)\n  We measure R_vp = ||∇_trunk L_value|| / ||∇_trunk\
    \ L_policy|| at init (heads excluded):\n  - Baseline: ≈0.137\n  - RIN α=0.20: ≈0.478\n  (storage/zephyr/results/probe_init_rvp_rin.json)\n  Interpretation: RIN increases relative value‑gradient in the shared trunk, plausibly improving value‑policy balance and stability near ~95%.\n\n  5. Reproducibility Checklist (Parameter‑Parity)\n  - z = concat(attn_vec[64], gap_vec[64]) only (no time); Dense_0/kernel=[128,256], Dense_0/bias=[256]\n  - ConvLSTM gates: Conv kernel [3,3,128,256] per cell ×4; LayerNorm only on gates (ConvLSTMCellLN_* / LayerNorm_0 / {scale,bias}); nongate_layernorm_total_size=0\n  - Canonical scripts:\n    • storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_rin_default.py      (α=0.20, lr=3.5e‑4, clip=1.0)\n    • storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_rin_default_lr4e4.py (α=0.20, lr=4e‑4,   clip=1.0)\n\n  6. Conclusion\n  A minimal recurrent agent with RIN (α=0.20) plus careful but simple hyperparameters reaches robust ~95% solve without architectural complexity. The recipe is reproducible\
    \ with the parity checks above and can serve as a stable baseline for future analytical work and generalization tests.\n```"
