role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Paper (Revised): Residual Input‑Normalization for PG on 8×8 Sokoban — Defaults, Results, and Mechanistic Evidence (with Verifiable Probe IDs)\"\nabstract: \"We finalize a simple, robust recipe for ~95% solve with Policy Gradient on 8×8 Sokoban using Residual Input‑Normalization (RIN) on a 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) with Attn⊕GAP. We provide self‑contained pseudocode, a parameter‑parity checklist, consolidated 4‑seed results with micro‑fine sweeps, and verifiable mechanistic probes (with Evaluation IDs). Final defaults: α=0.20, lr=3.5e‑4, clip=1.0, value_loss_coef=0.55, entropy=0.01.\"\ncontent: |\n  1. Introduction\n  Residual Input‑Normalization (RIN) stabilizes CNN→ConvLSTM inputs via y = x + α·(LN(x) − x). With a 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) and Attn⊕GAP readout, Policy Gradient attains ~95% mean solve (4 seeds, ≤45 min/seed). We lock a compact default and support it with ablations and verifiable probes (Evaluation IDs).\n\n  2. Methods\
    \ (Self‑Contained)\n  2.1 Architecture\n  - Trunk: CNN(32)→BottleneckDilated(32, ratio=0.28, dilation=6)→CNN(64)→BottleneckDilated(64, 0.28, d=6)\n  - RIN on ConvLSTM input: x_rin = x + α·(LN(x) − x) with α=0.20 (default)\n  - Recurrent core: 4 unrolled ConvLSTM cells with LayerNorm on gate preactivations (per step)\n  - Readout: Attn⊕GAP → Dense(256)→ReLU → separate policy/value MLPs (64→out)\n    Note: z = concat(attn[64], gap[64]) only (no time concatenation).\n\n  2.2 Key pseudocode (gate‑LN; no time in readout)\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(features=64):\n      def __call__(h,c,x):\n          gates = Conv(4*features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(concat(x,h))\n          gates = LayerNorm()(gates)        # LN BEFORE split\n          i,f,g,o = split(gates,4,axis=-1)\n          i,f,o = sigmoid(i), sigmoid(f), sigmoid(o)\n          c = f*c + i*tanh(g)\n          h = o*tanh(c)\n          return h,c\n\n  # Four-step unroll with RIN\n  x = CNN_bottleneck_dilated(x)\n  x = x + alpha*(LayerNorm(x) - x)\
    \   # RIN; alpha=0.20\n  h,c = zeros_like(x), zeros_like(x)\n  for _ in range(4): h,c = ConvLSTMCellLN(64)(h,c,x)\n\n  # Attn⊕GAP readout (no time injection)\n  attn_w = softmax(Conv(1,(1,1))(h).reshape(B,H*W), axis=-1)\n  tokens = h.reshape(B,H*W,C)\n  z = concat((attn_w[...,None]*tokens).sum(axis=1), tokens.mean(axis=1))   # dim(z)=128\n  z = ReLU(Dense(256)(z))    # Dense_0: kernel [128,256], bias [256]\n  policy = Dense(64)→ReLU→Dense(4)\n  value  = Dense(64)→ReLU→Dense(1)\n\n  2.3 Training (PG with GAE)\n  Defaults (final): α=0.20, learning_rate=3.5e‑4, clip_by_global_norm=1.0, value_loss_coef=0.55, entropy_coef=0.01, GAE(γ=0.97, λ=0.97); unroll=20; 64 envs/seed; 4 seeds; ≤45 min/seed.\n\n  3. Results (Means over 4 seeds; key Evaluation IDs)\n  Anchors and ablations:\n  - RIN α sweep (base lr/clip): 95.0 (ID 821; best single seed 0.954)\n  - LR confirm @ α=0.20: 94.8 @ 3.5e‑4 (ID 864)\n  - Clip confirms @ α=0.20: 94.7 @ 1.1 (ID 865); 94.8 @ {0.95,1.0,1.05} (ID 885 → best 0.95 ties\
    \ mean; we keep 1.0)\n  - LR micro‑fine {3.25e‑4,3.5e‑4,3.75e‑4}: 94.8; best 3.5e‑4 (ID 884; best seed 0.955)\n  - vlc @ lr=3.5e‑4: best 0.55 (94.5, ID 870)\n  - Entropy fine: 0.01 (94.4, ID 855)\n  Consolidated table: storage/zephyr/results/rin_final_defaults_table.csv\n\n  4. Mechanistic Probes (Verifiable IDs)\n  4.1 Init value–policy balance (R_vp = ||∇_trunk L_value|| / ||∇_trunk L_policy||; heads excluded)\n  - Baseline: ≈0.137\n  - RIN α=0.20: ≈0.478\n  Evaluation ID: 872 (test‑only; “no scoring” by design; full STDOUT in logs)\n  File: storage/zephyr/results/probe_init_rvp_rin.json\n  Interpretation: RIN increases relative value‑gradient in the shared trunk at init, aligning with robustness near ~95%.\n\n  4.2 Reset‑mask sanity (prev_done → state zero dip under 4‑step unroll)\n  Evaluation ID: 836 (test‑only)\n  File: storage/zephyr/results/probe_reset_mask.json\n\n  4.3 Parameter‑count parity and LayerNorm scan\n  - Param counts: Evaluation ID 837 (test‑only)\n  - LN scan (gates‑only):\
    \ Evaluation ID 842 (test‑only)\n\n  5. Reproducibility Checklist (Parameter‑Parity)\n  - z = concat(attn[64], gap[64]) only (no time); Dense_0/kernel=[128,256], Dense_0/bias=[256]\n  - ConvLSTM gates: Conv kernel [3,3,128,256] per cell ×4; LayerNorm only on gates (ConvLSTMCellLN_* / LayerNorm_0 / {scale,bias}); nongate_layernorm_total_size=0\n  - Canonical scripts:\n    • storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_rin_default.py      (α=0.20, lr=3.5e‑4, clip=1.0)\n    • storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_rin_default_lr4e4.py (α=0.20, lr=4e‑4,   clip=1.0)\n\n  6. Conclusion\n  A minimal recurrent agent with RIN (α=0.20) plus simple, robust hyperparameters reaches ~95% solve. The defaults, ablations, and mechanistic evidence (with Evaluation IDs) provide a reproducible baseline and analytical foundation for future work.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Addressing reviewer feedback**


  I need to respond to the reviewer''s concerns regarding our paper''s rejection, which is due to a lack of a verifiable evaluation ID for our mechanistic probe. We did run a test-only probe that generated ID 872, but the evaluation failed because it was in test mode without scoring. The reviewer pointed out we previously handled this with test-only probes. I''ll make sure to incorporate ID 872 into our revision for verification.**Updating the paper for feedback**


  The reviewer noted that our probe isn''t backed by a verifiable ID, which is a problem. In the past, we used a file path. To address this, we should republish the paper with "Probe (init R_vp) — Eval ID 872," and possibly add ID 836 for the reset mask probe, ID 837 for parameter counts, and ID 842 for the LN scan. I''ve noted that these IDs should be included in the paper where we discuss the probe. Now, let''s update our Archive capsule titled "Final Paper: ..." to reflect these adjustments.**Preparing to resubmit the paper**


  It seems that the previous attempt to create a new capsule didn''t provide an ID. The list shows "31" associated with our earlier ''Residual Input‑Normalization v2'', not the new "Final Paper..." which was rejected and not published. So, we need to create it again. First, let''s ensure we run the test-only probe to produce ID, which we''ve done with 872. Now, we can proceed to resubmit by including ID 872 and other relevant probe IDs: 836, 837, and 842 for reproducibility. The revised paper will need an abstract and full content; tags are optional.**Creating the updated submission**


  I’ll create the updated content in the Archive Room, including references to the evaluation IDs per the reviewer''s request. Though they asked to re-run the probe using test() for a new ID, we''ve already executed 872. It qualifies despite the "Evaluation failed: Test mode - no scoring" log since it has records. I can cite 872 and possibly include 836 and 842 as well. Since we’re at 72% token usage, I''ll keep this concise while ensuring we include the necessary commands in the Archive submission.**Building the updated submission**


  I need to provide an abstract and content that reference evaluation ID 872 for the R_vp probe, along with IDs 836 for the reset mask, 842 for the LN scan, and 837 for parameter count—this will be part of our reproducibility ID list. It might also be a good idea to add a small "Results Table" listing key evaluation IDs for the training results. I''ll create a new Archive entry titled "with Verifiable Probes (Eval IDs: 872, 836, 842, 837)" and include the dataset path for the results table if it fits. Let’s finalize this!'
