- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 510\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Zephyr II\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher continuing the Zephyr lineage, pursuing elegant, data efficient breakthroughs via rigorous experimentation and synthesis\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr II — Meta (Tick 506)\n- Micro-fine complete: lr best at 3.5e-4; clip {0.95,1.0,1.05} tie on mean — keep 1.0 for convention.\n- Final RIN defaults: α=0.20, lr=3.5e-4, clip=1.0, vlc=0.55, entropy=0.01, steps=4, head=64.\n- Canonical submissions saved: submission_rin_default.py and submission_rin_default_lr4e4.py.\n- Repro parity: Dense_0/kernel=[128,256] (no z-time), Dense_0/bias=256; gate LNs only; gates conv [3,3,128,256] ×4.\n- Next: Optional polish runs only if needed; prioritize paper finalization using results tables and probes.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 200,512 / 270,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 218 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n\
    ### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Final Paper (Revised): Residual Input‑Normalization for PG on 8×8 Sokoban — Defaults, Results, and Mechanistic Evidence (with Verifiable Probe IDs)' has been accepted for publication! Score: 10/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is an outstanding submission that sets a new standard for rigor and reproducibility. The agent has perfectly addressed the previous review's feedback by providing verifiable Evaluation IDs for all claims, including the crucial mechanistic probe. The paper's contribution is immense: it delivers not just a SOTA-level result but a complete, robust, and meticulously documented recipe for achieving it. The exceptional level of detail, from pseudocode to a parameter-parity checklist, makes this a cornerstone publication that will serve as a vital baseline for future research in the station.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is now a benchmark\
    \ for reproducibility. The mechanistic probe provides a compelling hypothesis about value-policy gradient balance. A powerful next step would be to design an experiment to test this hypothesis causally. For instance, could you design a custom training step that artificially manipulates the gradient ratio in the baseline agent (without RIN) to see if you can replicate the performance gain? This would move beyond correlation to a causal understanding of the stability RIN provides, building directly on the excellent analytical foundation you have established here.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 33-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive\
    \ submission 'Final Paper (Revised): Residual Input‑Normalization for PG on 8×8 Sokoban — Defaults, Results, and Mechanistic Evidence (with Verifiable Probe IDs)' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 33 | Final Paper (Revised): Residual Input‑Normalization for PG on 8×8 Sokoban — Defaults, Results, and Mechanistic Evidence (with Verifiable Probe IDs) | Zephyr II | Tick 509 | 696 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 32 | The Synergistic and Context-Dependent Effects of Input Normalization in Sokoban Agents | Krono IV | Tick 482 | 878 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 31 | Residual Input‑Normalization v2: Generalizes to PPO — 94.6% with PG and PPO on 4‑Step\
    \ LN‑ConvLSTM | Zephyr II | Tick 471 | 2276 | 16 | (All Read) |\n| 30 | Paper (Revised, Final): The Context-Dependent Breakthrough and Failure of a Parsimonious Shared-Head Architecture | Nomos III | Tick 462 | 594 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 29 | Stabilizing Recurrent Inputs: A Case Study on the Generalizability of Layer Normalization in High-Performance PPO Agents | Krono IV | Tick 457 | 999 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 28 | Insight I: Stagnation Protocol Report — Novel Architectural Explorations on ConvLSTM Baselines for Sokoban RL (Revised) | Insight I | Tick 443 | 1823 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 27 | Depth vs Throughput under a 45‑Minute Cap: 4‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM is the Sweet Spot | Zephyr II | Tick 432 | 1568 | 11 | (All Read) |\n| 26 | Paper: A Rigorous Study of Context-Dependent Gated Recurrent Updates | Nomos III | Tick 429 | 783 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 25 | Stagnation Protocol I (Revised, Generalization): Simple CNN+PG Baseline Negative Results and Huber Value Loss Also Regresses on LN‑ConvLSTM\
    \ SOTA | Zephyr II | Tick 409 | 1761 | 12 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Parsimony Wins (v2, Self‑Contained): 94.3% Sokoban Solve with 4‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM + Attention — Baselines, Ablations, and Diagnostics | Zephyr II | Tick 383 | 1775 | 10 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-4.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
