tick: 514
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Probe (test-only): Init trunk grad ratio R_vp vs β on baseline PG (no RIN) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)\"\ntags: \"probe, causal test, gradients, policy gradient, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Test-only mechanistic probe. Computes R_vp = ||∇_trunk L_value|| / ||∇_trunk L_policy|| at init for baseline PG (no RIN), then applies trunk-only scaling β∈{1.0,1.2,1.5} to value-gradients using a static param mask. Logs trunk/head leaf counts and ratios. No training.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Tuple\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  import numpy as np\n  from flax.core import freeze, unfreeze\n  from flax import traverse_util\n  from submissions.submission_pg_quadstep import PG_Stepped_AttnGap\n  from defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Not used in test(); provided for interface completeness.\n      return {}\n\n  def\
    \ create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      # Baseline (no RIN), matches our standard SOTA backbone sans RIN.\n      return PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=32, cnn_features_2=64,\n          convlstm_features=64, dilation=6,\n          bottleneck_ratio=0.28, head_hidden=64, steps=4,\n      )\n\n  def _build_trunk_mask(params_tree):\n      # Boolean mask tree: True for trunk, False for head layers.\n      pd = unfreeze(params_tree)\n      flat = traverse_util.flatten_dict(pd)  # keys: tuples\n      mask_flat = {}\n      for k in flat.keys():\n          path = \"/\".join(k)\n          # Heuristic: head MLPs are Dense_1..Dense_4 (policy/value heads).\n          is_head = any(tag in path for tag in [\"Dense_1\", \"Dense_2\", \"Dense_3\", \"Dense_4\"])\n          mask_flat[k] = (not is_head)\n      return freeze(traverse_util.unflatten_dict(mask_flat))\n\n  def _count_mask_leaves(mask_tree):\n      md = unfreeze(mask_tree)\n      flat = traverse_util.flatten_dict(md)\n\
    \      trunk = sum(1 for v in flat.values() if v is True)\n      head  = sum(1 for v in flat.values() if v is False)\n      return trunk, head\n\n  def _tree_l2norm_where(grad_tree, mask_tree, want_trunk=True):\n      gd = unfreeze(grad_tree)\n      md = unfreeze(mask_tree)\n      gflat = traverse_util.flatten_dict(gd)\n      mflat = traverse_util.flatten_dict(md)\n      s2 = 0.0\n      for k, g in gflat.items():\n          is_trunk = mflat[k]\n          if bool(is_trunk) == bool(want_trunk):\n              if g is None: \n                  continue\n              s2 += float(jnp.vdot(g, g))\n      return float(np.sqrt(s2))\n\n  def test():\n      print(\"=== INIT TRUNK GRAD RATIO PROBE (BASELINE, NO RIN) ===\")\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(BASE_SEED)\n\n      # Build network and params\n      net = create_network({})\n      obs_dummy = jnp.zeros((1, 8, 8, 8), dtype=jnp.float32)\n      done_dummy = jnp.zeros((1,), dtype=bool)\n      params = net.init(key, obs_dummy, done_dummy, None)\n\
    \      mask = _build_trunk_mask(params[\"params\"])\n      n_trunk, n_head = _count_mask_leaves(mask)\n      print(f\"Mask leaves — trunk: {n_trunk}, head: {n_head}\")\n\n      # Synthetic batch (B,T) consistent with training shapes\n      B, T = 8, 20\n      key, k1, k2, k3 = jax.random.split(key, 4)\n      observations = jax.random.normal(k1, (B, T, 8, 8, 8), dtype=jnp.float32)\n      actions = jax.random.randint(k2, (B, T), 0, 4)\n      dones = jnp.zeros((B, T), dtype=bool)\n\n      # One-pass forward (flattened) to get values for GAE\n      obs_flat = observations.reshape(B*T, 8, 8, 8)\n      dones_flat = dones.reshape(B*T)\n      logits_flat, values_flat, _ = net.apply(params, obs_flat, dones_flat, None)\n      all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(B, T, -1)\n      all_values = values_flat.reshape(B, T)\n      final_values = all_values[:, -1]  # proxy for bootstrap\n\n      # Zero rewards; use model values in GAE to induce nonzero deltas\n      rewards = jnp.zeros((B, T), dtype=jnp.float32)\n\
    \      advantages = default_calculate_gae(\n          rewards, all_values, dones, gamma=0.97, gae_lambda=0.97, next_values=final_values\n      )\n      returns = advantages + all_values\n\n      # Losses\n      def loss_pi_ent(p):\n          l = net.apply(p, obs_flat, dones_flat, None)[0].reshape(B, T, -1)\n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(l, axis=-1)\n          idx = (jnp.arange(B)[:, None], jnp.arange(T), actions)\n          logp = log_probs_all[idx]\n          L_pi = -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages) * logp)\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(l, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          return L_pi - 0.01 * entropy  # entropy coef as in defaults\n\n      def loss_v_only(p):\n          v = net.apply(p, obs_flat, dones_flat, None)[1].reshape(B, T)\n          return 0.5 * jnp.mean((v - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n\n      g_pi = jax.grad(loss_pi_ent)(params)\n      g_v  = jax.grad(loss_v_only)(params)\n\n\
    \      trunk_pi = _tree_l2norm_where(g_pi[\"params\"], mask, True)\n      trunk_v  = _tree_l2norm_where(g_v[\"params\"],  mask, True)\n      R_vp = trunk_v / max(trunk_pi, 1e-8)\n      print(f\"Baseline R_vp (trunk) = {R_vp:.4f}  [||g_v,trunk||={trunk_v:.4f}, ||g_pi,trunk||={trunk_pi:.4f}]\")\n\n      for beta in [1.0, 1.2, 1.5]:\n          # Scale value grads on trunk only\n          def scale_fn(g_leaf, m_leaf):\n              return g_leaf * (beta if m_leaf else 1.0)\n          g_v_scaled = jax.tree_util.tree_map(scale_fn, g_v[\"params\"], mask)\n\n          trunk_v_beta = _tree_l2norm_where(g_v_scaled, mask, True)\n          R_vp_beta = trunk_v_beta / max(trunk_pi, 1e-8)\n          print(f\"β={beta:.2f} → scaled R_vp(trunk) = {R_vp_beta:.4f}  [||g_v,trunk||={trunk_v_beta:.4f}]\")\n\n      print(\"Probe complete.\")\n      return \"OK\"\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating network requirements**\n\nThe network expects an 8x8x8 input, and RIN is applied after the CNN trunk. Applying it to raw observations isn't identical but may help approximate results. I should avoid invalid manipulations that feel unnatural. The previously accepted paper detailed probes inside the network, but for a test-only scenario, we can derive R_vp for a baseline and \"beta gradient scaling\" mapping. Given our current stagnation and lack of specific requests, I should focus on managing tokens and actions.**Planning the implementation steps**\n\nI’d start by submitting a test-only probe to verify the trunk mask and initial R_vp across betas, using the baseline network and mask. This will produce an evaluation ID. \n\nIf a slot opens up, I'd stage a fallback training run with some specific beta values, but we already have one running, so I’ll wait. \n\nI'll also update my private memory to log this plan. I need to implement submission code using just\
  \ the test() function and hyperparameters, possibly referencing PG_Stepped_AttnGap. I will generate a random observation array for further evaluation.**Computing gradients and advantages**\n\nI’m thinking about how to compute gradients and advantages from random numbers. Normally, I’d use the default_calculate_gae, which requires both old and final values. I'll use forward_apply to predict values based on random parameters and set old_values from these predictions.\n\nTo keep things consistent, I want to compute advantages that aren't zero. Setting returns to zeros isn't yielding what I need, but I can derive non-zero advantages from the old values. \n\nUsing the GAE formula, if I set rewards to zero, I find that advantages won’t be zero. That’s a positive outcome!**Executing the forward pass**\n\nI plan to implement the forward pass to compute all_logits and all_values_pred. To calculate advantages, I’ll use default_calculate_gae with rewards set to zero. However, this method expects\
  \ old_values from the dataset, so I need to pass in the predicted values, and maybe I’ll compute final_values using the network on the last observation.\n\nI'll take the last predicted value for each environment and set dones to all False. From there, I'll compute L_pi and L_v just like in the earlier training, followed by their gradients. Lastly, I’ll build the trunk mask based on paths and ensure that the naming conventions align correctly with the layers.**Considering concurrency in evaluations**\n\nI’m looking at how concurrency affects my evaluations. Currently, there's only one running evaluation, 893, and the test-only will run quickly, giving me an immediate ID. Concurrency allows up to two, so that should be fine.\n\nAfter submission, updating the results logging is optional. I have to stay compliant with the system’s YAML quoting rules for colons, which means I should use quotes for titles that include colons. Alright, time to implement that action!"
