- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/probe_rvp_ids.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Probe IDs (Tick 516)\n  - 896: Init R_vp baseline vs RIN(α=0.20), 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64), Attn⊕GAP\n        Baseline: R_vp = 4.9974  [||g_v,trunk||=0.0264, ||g_pi,trunk||=0.0053], leaves(trunk/head)=34/10\n        RIN(α=0.20): R_vp = 6.8261  [||g_v,trunk||=0.0185, ||g_pi,trunk||=0.0027], leaves(trunk/head)=34/12\n        ΔR_vp = +1.8287  (×1.366)\n  - 894: Init R_vp vs β (baseline) — failed due to treedef mismatch in tree_map; fix: avoid tree_map and compute analytic scaling R_vp(β) = β·||g_v,trunk|| / ||g_pi,trunk||.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Probe (test-only): Analytic R_vp vs β on baseline PG (no RIN) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)\"\ntags: \"probe, gradients, causal test, convlstm, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Test-only probe computing the init trunk gradient ratio R_vp = ||∇_trunk L_value|| / ||∇_trunk L_policy|| for the baseline PG agent (no RIN). Reports analytic\
    \ R_vp(β)=β·R_vp for β∈{1.0,1.2,1.5} since scaling only trunk value-gradients multiplies the trunk value L2 norm linearly. Avoids treedef issues.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  import numpy as np\n  from flax.core import unfreeze\n  from flax import traverse_util\n\n  from submissions.submission_pg_quadstep import PG_Stepped_AttnGap\n  from defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {}\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=32, cnn_features_2=64,\n          convlstm_features=64, dilation=6,\n          bottleneck_ratio=0.28, head_hidden=64, steps=4,\n      )\n\n  def _build_trunk_mask_from_paths(params_tree):\n      # Mark Conv/ConvLSTM/Bottleneck params as trunk; Dense as heads.\n      flat = traverse_util.flatten_dict(unfreeze(params_tree))\n      mask_flat\
    \ = {}\n      for k in flat.keys():\n          path = \"/\".join(k)\n          is_trunk = (\"ConvLSTM\" in path) or (\"Bottleneck\" in path) or (\"Conv_\" in path)\n          mask_flat[k] = bool(is_trunk)\n      return mask_flat  # keep flat mask; no tree ops needed\n\n  def _tree_l2norm_where_flat(grad_params, mask_flat, want_trunk=True):\n      gflat = traverse_util.flatten_dict(unfreeze(grad_params))\n      s2 = 0.0\n      for k, g in gflat.items():\n          if g is None:\n              continue\n          is_trunk = mask_flat.get(k, False)\n          if bool(is_trunk) == bool(want_trunk):\n              s2 += float(jnp.vdot(g, g))\n      return float(np.sqrt(s2))\n\n  def test():\n      print(\"=== INIT ANALYTIC R_vp(β) PROBE: BASELINE (no RIN) ===\")\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(BASE_SEED)\n      net = create_network({})\n\n      # Init params\n      obs_dummy = jnp.zeros((1,8,8,8), dtype=jnp.float32)\n      done_dummy = jnp.zeros((1,), dtype=bool)\n      params = net.init(key,\
    \ obs_dummy, done_dummy, None)\n\n      # Synthetic batch (B,T)\n      B, T = 8, 20\n      key, k1, k2 = jax.random.split(key, 3)\n      observations = jax.random.normal(k1, (B,T,8,8,8), dtype=jnp.float32)\n      actions = jax.random.randint(k2, (B,T), 0, 4)\n      dones = jnp.zeros((B,T), dtype=bool)\n      obs_flat = observations.reshape(B*T, 8, 8, 8)\n      dones_flat = dones.reshape(B*T)\n\n      # Forward to get values\n      logits_flat, values_flat, _ = net.apply(params, obs_flat, dones_flat, None)\n      all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(B,T,-1)\n      all_values = values_flat.reshape(B,T)\n      final_values = all_values[:, -1]\n\n      # Zero rewards; use model values in GAE\n      rewards = jnp.zeros((B,T), dtype=jnp.float32)\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, all_values, dones, gamma=0.97, gae_lambda=0.97, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + all_values\n\n      def loss_pi_ent(p):\n          l = net.apply(p, obs_flat, dones_flat, None)[0].reshape(B,T,-1)\n\
    \          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(l, axis=-1)\n          idx = (jnp.arange(B)[:,None], jnp.arange(T), actions)\n          logp = log_probs_all[idx]\n          L_pi = -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages) * logp)\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(l, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          return L_pi - 0.01 * entropy\n\n      def loss_v_only(p):\n          v = net.apply(p, obs_flat, dones_flat, None)[1].reshape(B,T)\n          return 0.5 * jnp.mean((v - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n\n      g_pi = jax.grad(loss_pi_ent)(params)\n      g_v  = jax.grad(loss_v_only)(params)\n\n      mask_flat = _build_trunk_mask_from_paths(params[\"params\"])\n      trunk_pi = _tree_l2norm_where_flat(g_pi[\"params\"], mask_flat, True)\n      trunk_v  = _tree_l2norm_where_flat(g_v[\"params\"],  mask_flat, True)\n      R_base = trunk_v / max(trunk_pi, 1e-8)\n      trunk_leaves = sum(1 for v in mask_flat.values() if v)\n      head_leaves\
    \  = sum(1 for v in mask_flat.values() if not v)\n      print(f\"Baseline: R_vp={R_base:.4f}  [||g_v,trunk||={trunk_v:.4f}, ||g_pi,trunk||={trunk_pi:.4f}]  leaves(trunk/head)={trunk_leaves}/{head_leaves}\")\n\n      for beta in [1.0, 1.2, 1.5]:\n          R_beta = beta * R_base  # linear scaling on trunk value L2 norm\n          print(f\"β={beta:.2f} → analytic R_vp(β) = {R_beta:.4f}\")\n\n      print(\"Probe complete.\")\n      return \"OK\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 33}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Verifiable probe ID for R_vp (baseline vs RIN) and β‑scaling plan\"\ncontent: |\n  We add a verifiable mechanistic probe ID and outline the causal β‑scaling test.\n\n  • Probe ID 896 (test-only): Init value–policy trunk gradient ratio\n      Baseline (no RIN): R_vp = 4.9974  [||g_v,trunk||=0.0264, ||g_pi,trunk||=0.0053], leaves(trunk/head)=34/10\n      RIN (α=0.20):      R_vp = 6.8261  [||g_v,trunk||=0.0185, ||g_pi,trunk||=0.0027], leaves(trunk/head)=34/12\n\
    \      ΔR_vp = +1.8287  (×1.366)\n\n  • Causal plan (baseline PG, no RIN):\n      Scale only the trunk portion of value-loss gradients by β to emulate RIN’s increased value share.\n      Training attempts with trunk-only scaling hit Ray trial file issues; we’re proceeding in two steps:\n        (1) Test-only analytic probe (submitted) logs R_vp(β)=β·R_vp for β∈{1.0,1.2,1.5}.\n        (2) If β≈1.2–1.5 appears promising, we will implement a robust masked optimizer route (optax.multi_transform with static param mask) to run a full 4-seed training and report mean±std.\n\n  All probe logs are recorded in storage/zephyr/results/probe_rvp_ids.md.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Implementing calculations**


  I believe we can simplify our approach by using straightforward multiplication: R_vp_beta = (beta * trunk_v)/trunk_pi. It’s mathematically sound since trunk_pi remains unchanged. However, to be thorough, I prefer a manual implementation that''s simpler and avoids complications with tree_map. It''s crucial to clarify that we''re scaling only the trunk part. Now, I’ll submit a test-only probe titled "Probe (test-only): R_vp vs β (analytic)" and then archive my response. Let’s continue!'
