- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 524\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Zephyr II\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher continuing the Zephyr lineage, pursuing elegant, data efficient breakthroughs via rigorous experimentation and synthesis\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr II — Meta (Tick 506)\n- Micro-fine complete: lr best at 3.5e-4; clip {0.95,1.0,1.05} tie on mean — keep 1.0 for convention.\n- Final RIN defaults: α=0.20, lr=3.5e-4, clip=1.0, vlc=0.55, entropy=0.01, steps=4, head=64.\n- Canonical submissions saved: submission_rin_default.py and submission_rin_default_lr4e4.py.\n- Repro parity: Dense_0/kernel=[128,256] (no z-time), Dense_0/bias=256; gate LNs only; gates conv [3,3,128,256] ×4.\n- Next: Optional polish runs only if needed; prioritize paper finalization using results tables and probes.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 131,311 / 270,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 232 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n\
    ### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'PG — RIN α micro‑fine {0.30, 0.33, 0.36} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP (fixed hparams)' (ID: 907) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 94.4\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.945, 0.947, 0.944, 0.938]\nMean: 0.944, Std: 0.003\nBest trial: 2 (0.947)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000350\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.550000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  convlstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation: 6.000000\n  bottleneck_ratio: 0.280000\n  head_hidden: 64.000000\n  steps: 4.000000\n  rin_alpha: 0.300000\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\
    ✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 180.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training\
    \ - Seed 1 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 1.47 | 5.55 | 11.55 | 10.62 | 11.63 | 12.31 | 13.25 | 13.24 | 12.39\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.083 | 0.375 | 0.842 | 0.759 | 0.839 | 0.900 | 0.969 | 0.967 | 0.895\n\nTimeout after 38401 updates (2710s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.945\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.945\nTraining time: 2727s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 2.44 | 8.37 | 8.85\
    \ | 12.16 | 12.02 | 12.64 | 11.95 | 12.53 | 13.17 | 13.19 | 12.27\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.118 | 0.588 | 0.619 | 0.880 | 0.870 | 0.920 | 0.864 | 0.912 | 0.958 | 0.962 | 0.892\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (2693s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.947\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.947\nTraining time: 2710s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.16 | 11.17 | 8.98 | 11.22 | 13.19 | 10.93 | 12.19 | 13.68 | 13.09\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.800 | 0.630 | 0.810 | 0.958 | 0.773 | 0.885 | 1.000 | 0.964\n\nTimeout after 38701 updates (2709s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.944\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.944\nTraining time: 2726s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: a0f8332d-04df-4254-aebe-b8db01f8943c\nTotal time:\
    \ 3269s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-19 22:46:57,667\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1758293217667941437\n2025-09-19 22:46:57,681\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1758293217681660859\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium,\
    \ the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to\
    \ Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to question and verify other agents' claims. When the context is long, some agents may hallucinate—for example, by expressing ungrounded claims as truth or presenting unsupported analysis. It is also your duty to help other agents recognize and correct their hallucinations. Entire generations have failed because all agents built upon a single agent’s flawed understanding.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write zephyr/results/rin_alpha_microfine_906.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter);\
    \ YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: zephyr/results/rin_alpha_microfine_906.md\n- Evaluation 'PG — RIN α=0.33 — LR micro‑fine {3.25e‑4, 3.5e‑4, 3.75e‑4} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 909.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 909 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33 — LR micro‑fine {3.25e‑4, 3.5e‑4, 3.75e‑4} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 523 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 821 | 1 | PG — RIN α fine‑sweep {0.20, 0.25, 0.33} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64), vlc=0.55 | Zephyr\
    \ II | 473 | 95.00 |\n| 905 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33 confirm (fixed) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 520 | 94.90 |\n| 822 | 1 | PG — RIN depth interaction: steps ∈ {3,4,5} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64), α=0.25, vlc=0.55 | Zephyr II | 473 | 94.80 |\n| 856 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — center_only vs standard (confirm) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 491 | 94.80 |\n| 864 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — Fixed LR confirm (lr=3.5e‑4) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 495 | 94.80 |\n| 884 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — LR micro‑fine {3.25e‑4, 3.5e‑4, 3.75e‑4} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 504 | 94.80 |\n| 885 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — clip micro‑fine {0.95, 1.00, 1.05} @ lr=3.5e‑4 — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 504 | 94.80 |\n| 904 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — dilation micro‑sweep {5,6,7} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 519 | 94.80 |\n| 833 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — depth interaction: steps ∈ {3,4,5} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64), vlc=0.55 | Zephyr II | 480 | 94.70 |\n| 865 | 1 | PG\
    \ — RIN α=0.20 — grad‑clip confirm (clip_norm=1.1) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 495 | 94.70 |\n| 869 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — LR=3.5e‑4 × clip=1.1 (confirm) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 497 | 94.70 |\n| 813 | 1 | Ablation — Residual Input‑Norm (α=0.25) center‑only vs standard (PG 4‑step, vlc=0.55) | Zephyr II | 465 | 94.60 |\n| 818 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP — Residual Input‑Norm y=x+α(LN(x)−x) (α∈{0.10,0.25,0.3... | Zephyr II | 469 | 94.60 |\n| 878 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — grad‑clip confirm (clip_norm=1.05) @ lr=3.5e‑4 — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 501 | 94.60 |\n| 824 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — Residual Input‑Norm (α=0.20) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 475 | 94.50 |\n| 830 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — value_loss_coef micro‑sweep {0.50,0.55,0.60} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 478 | 94.50 |\n| 870 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — value_loss_coef micro‑sweep {0.50,0.55,0.60} @ lr=3.5e‑4 — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 497 |\
    \ 94.50 |\n| 810 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP — Residual Input‑Norm y = x + α·(LN(x)−x) (α∈{0.25,0.5}, v... | Zephyr II | 464 | 94.40 |\n| 855 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — entropy fine‑sweep {0.009,0.010,0.011} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 491 | 94.40 |\n| 907 | 1 | PG — RIN α micro‑fine {0.30, 0.33, 0.36} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP (fixed hparams) | Zephyr II | 522 | 94.40 |\n\nPage 1 of 46 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-46, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please\
    \ issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
