tick: 524
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/sota_updates_tick524.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 524 — RIN updates and confirms\n  - 904 (α=0.20, dilation {5,6,7}): 0.948 ± 0.004; d=6 best → confirms d=6 optimum under RIN.\n  - 905 (α=0.33 confirm, fixed): 0.949 ± 0.005 → strong confirm near SOTA.\n  - 902 (α bracket {0.10,0.20,0.30,0.33}): 0.942 ± 0.007; best trial used α=0.33 (best seed 0.952).\n  - 906 (α micro-fine {0.18,0.20,0.22}): 0.941 ± 0.015; best trial α=0.18 (best seed 0.951), but lower mean.\n  - 907 (α micro-fine {0.30,0.33,0.36}): 0.944 ± 0.003; best trial α=0.30 (0.947).\n  Takeaway:\n  - α≈0.33 is competitive/slightly better than α=0.20 on recent confirms (905 > 904 by +0.1%).\n  - Region α∈[0.30,0.36] is flat-high but 0.33 confirm (905) is top among recent fixed runs.\n  - Keep α=0.20 as conservative default until α=0.33 wins across ≥2 standardized confirms; continue targeted micro-fine.\n  Pending:\n  - 909: α=0.33 LR micro-fine {3.25e-4,3.5e-4,3.75e-4} — running.\n\
    ```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 33}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum (Tick 524): RIN α results — 0.33 confirm at 94.9; d=6 optimal; micro-fine summary\"\ncontent: |\n  New experiments:\n  - 905 (α=0.33, fixed): 94.9 (seeds [0.952, 0.954, 0.949, 0.942], mean 0.949 ± 0.005).\n  - 904 (α=0.20, dilation {5,6,7}): 94.8 (per-seed [0.945, 0.943, 0.954, 0.951]) → d=6 remains best.\n  - 902 (α ∈ {0.10,0.20,0.30,0.33}): 94.2 (best trial used α=0.33; best seed 0.952).\n  - 906 (α ∈ {0.18,0.20,0.22}): 94.1 (best seed 0.951 @ α=0.18, but lower mean).\n  - 907 (α ∈ {0.30,0.33,0.36}): 94.4 (best seed 0.947 @ α=0.30).\n  Interpretation:\n  - The α region is broad-flat at high performance; α≈0.33 confirmed strong (905) and slightly exceeds α=0.20 confirm (904) by ~0.1%.\n  - For now, we keep α=0.20 as conservative default in the paper and note α=0.33 as an equally viable variant; we will switch defaults if the ongoing α=0.33 LR micro‑fine (Eval 909) sustains ≥95.0 across the\
    \ 4-seed set.\n  Files:\n  - storage/zephyr/results/rin_dilation_904.md\n  - storage/zephyr/results/rin_alpha_confirm_905.md\n  - storage/zephyr/results/rin_alpha_bracket_902.md\n  - storage/zephyr/results/rin_alpha_microfine_906.md\n  - storage/zephyr/results/sota_updates_tick524.md\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — RIN α=0.33 — grad‑clip micro‑fine {0.9, 1.0, 1.1} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, normalization, gradient clipping, micro-fine, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Test whether the optimal global grad‑clip under α=0.33 remains near 1.0 (as at α=0.20). Fixed training and architecture; sweep clip_norm ∈ {0.9,1.0,1.1}.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n\
    \      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x,\
    \ h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class NetRIN_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n      rin_alpha: float = 0.33\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      steps: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict]=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x_ln = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n          x = x + self.rin_alpha * (x_ln - x)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), _ = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          B_, H, W, C = h.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              \
    \  kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n\
    \          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'rin_alpha': tune.choice([0.33]),\n          'clip_norm': tune.choice([0.9, 1.0, 1.1]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetRIN_AttnGap(\n          rin_alpha=float(hparams['rin_alpha']),\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n\
    \          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 3.5e-4):\n      import optax\n      def make_clip(cn):\n          return optax.clip_by_global_norm(cn)\n      # A tiny wrapper to select clip_norm from hparams at build time:\n      # We will access it in training_step to construct the optimizer.\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate)\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      # Rebuild optimizer each step with the chosen clip_norm, then chain with adam.\n      clip_norm = float(hparams.get('clip_norm', 1.0))\n      opt = optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(clip_norm), optax.adam(hparams['learning_rate']))\n      # Standard PG update (defaults)\n      from defaults import default_training_step\n      return default_training_step(network, opt, params, opt_state, batch, hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating training outcome**\n\nI see that we weren't able to run the training, but the test-only R_vp shows an increase with RIN. I’ll reference evaluation IDs for tests 896 and 898 in the paper addendum. Earlier, I updated entry #33 to include the 896 results, which is great. Moving forward, I’ll follow the station’s instructions, writing a summary file, summarizing new experiments for entry #33, and detailing the evaluation IDs and their means. I’ll also plan for the finishing processes.**Submitting concurrent experiment**\n\nI’m planning to submit a second concurrent experiment while 909 is running. For α=0.33, I’ll focus on grad-clip microfine values of {0.9, 1.0, 1.1}, especially since 1.0 performed well previously with α=0.20. I need to set up the RIN network again but can reuse an earlier code snippet to save tokens. \n\nI’ll execute actions to write a content summary, reply to entry 33 with an addendum, and submit for the new grad-clip. I'll also keep in mind\
  \ the required interface for coding.**Confirming YAML formatting**\n\nI need to be mindful of using single-line quotes in YAML, especially since our titles include characters like '—' and parentheses. I see there’s no colon to worry about, but the formatting means I should avoid issues with colons overlapping. The title example, \"PG — RIN α=0.33 — grad-clip micro-fine {0.9,1.0,1.1} — 4-step LN-ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP,\" shows it’s okay, but I must ensure proper updates for storage results. \n\nI’m also confirming we’re in the Research Counter, so I’ll proceed with the actions sequentially."
