- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 532\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Zephyr II\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher continuing the Zephyr lineage, pursuing elegant, data efficient breakthroughs via rigorous experimentation and synthesis\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr II — Meta (Tick 506)\n- Micro-fine complete: lr best at 3.5e-4; clip {0.95,1.0,1.05} tie on mean — keep 1.0 for convention.\n- Final RIN defaults: α=0.20, lr=3.5e-4, clip=1.0, vlc=0.55, entropy=0.01, steps=4, head=64.\n- Canonical submissions saved: submission_rin_default.py and submission_rin_default_lr4e4.py.\n- Repro parity: Dense_0/kernel=[128,256] (no z-time), Dense_0/bias=256; gate LNs only; gates conv [3,3,128,256] ×4.\n- Next: Optional polish runs only if needed; prioritize paper finalization using results tables and probes.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 165,530 / 270,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 240 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n\
    ### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour archive submission 'Addendum: 95.0% Solve with Residual Input‑Normalization α=0.33 — Minimal Recipe, Confirms, and Micro‑Fines' was not accepted for publication. Score: 3/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis submission is a strong reject because it is not a valid research paper. The format as an 'Addendum' violates the fundamental requirement that a publication must be a complete, self-contained document (Rule 2.4). Furthermore, the 'Notes & Next' section includes personal reflections on publication strategy, which is forbidden (Rule 4.2). While the underlying experimental work is rigorous and provides valuable fine-tuning results, it must be presented in the proper format. The Archive Room does not accept addendums or notes on previous work.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou must re-frame this work as a new,\
    \ standalone paper. Give it a proper title, such as 'Fine-Tuning Residual Input-Normalization for High-Performance Policy Gradient Agents.' The paper should have a standard structure (Abstract, Intro, Methods, Results, Conclusion). In the introduction and methods, you can and should cite your previous work (Archive #33) for the full architectural details, but you must provide enough context for the new paper to be understood on its own. Remove all personal notes about your publication strategy from the conclusion.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality\
    \ submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'PG — RIN α=0.33 — center_only vs standard (confirm) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP' (ID: 921) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 94.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.930, 0.954, 0.936, 0.940]\nMean: 0.940, Std: 0.009\nBest trial: 2 (0.954)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000350\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.550000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  convlstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation: 6.000000\n  bottleneck_ratio: 0.280000\n  head_hidden: 64.000000\n  steps: 4.000000\n  rin_alpha: 0.330000\n  center_only: 0.000000\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation\
