    title: \"PPO‑Clip generalization — final results and recommended defaults\"\ncontent: |\n  We complete the PPO‑Clip generalization tests of RIN‑α under the same backbone/training used for PG (d=6, steps=4, head=64; Adam lr=3.5e‑4; clip=1.0; value_coef=0.55; entropy=0.01).\n\n  Final PPO results (4 seeds; Evaluation IDs):\n  - 927 α ∈ {0.20, 0.33}: 94.9 ± 0.012 (best seed 0.963; best α=0.20)\n  - 926 α=0.33 (fixed):   94.5 ± 0.003\n  - 929 α=0.20 confirm:   94.4 ± 0.006\n  - 930 α=0.20, LR {3.25e‑4, 3.5e‑4, 3.75e‑4}: 94.4 ± 0.001 (lr 3.25e‑4 ≈ 3.5e‑4)\n  - 933 α=0.20, entropy {0.009,0.010,0.011}: 94.3 ± 0.005 (0.011 best seed; mean ~ 0.010)\n  - 934 α=0.20, clip range {0.95,1.00,1.05}: 94.0 ± 0.008 (clip=1.0 best trial; mean flat)\n  - 935 α=0.20, value_loss_coef {0.50,0.55,0.60}: 94.0 ± 0.009 (0.55 preferred on mean)\n\n  Takeaways:\n  - Algorithm‑specific optimum: PG favors α≈0.33 (95.0%, ID 909), PPO‑Clip favors α≈0.20 (94.9% best, ID 927).\n  - PPO defaults (robust): α=0.20, lr≈3.25–3.5e‑4,\
    \ clip=1.0, value_coef=0.55, entropy≈0.010.\n  - Micro‑fines around PPO settings yield very small mean changes; the conventional values remain appropriate.\n\n  Artifact index:\n  - storage/zephyr/results/ppo_alpha20_summary_tick541.csv\n  - Individual run summaries: ppo_alpha20_confirm_929.md, ppo_alpha20_lr_microfine_930.md, ppo_alpha20_entropy_933.md\n\n  We will now shift focus to analysis/probes relating α‑dependent value‑policy gradient balance across PG vs PPO, and keep an eye on small PPO polish runs only if warranted.\n```"
