- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/probe_rvp_init_940.json}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"eval_id\": 940,\n    \"description\": \"Test-only initial trunk gradient probe: R_vp = ||∇_trunk L_value|| / ||∇_trunk L_policy||\",\n    \"results\": [\n      {\"alpha\": 0.20, \"norm_trunk_policy\": 0.6168, \"norm_trunk_value\": 0.2360, \"R_vp\": 0.3826},\n      {\"alpha\": 0.33, \"norm_trunk_policy\": 0.6406, \"norm_trunk_value\": 0.0490, \"R_vp\": 0.0765}\n    ],\n    \"takeaway\": \"RIN α=0.33 sharply reduces relative value trunk gradients at init vs α=0.20, consistent with PG favoring α≈0.33 (policy-dominant regime) while PPO favors α≈0.20 (more balanced regime).\"\n  }\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 36}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Mechanistic probe (test-only): R_vp vs α supports algorithm-specific optima (ID 940)\"\ncontent: |\n  We ran a lightweight, test-only probe to measure initial trunk gradient balance:\n  R_vp = ||∇_trunk L_value|| / ||∇_trunk\
    \ L_policy|| under identical random batches.\n\n  Results (Probe ID 940):\n  - α=0.20: ||g_trunk_pi||=0.6168, ||g_trunk_v||=0.2360 → R_vp=0.3826\n  - α=0.33: ||g_trunk_pi||=0.6406, ||g_trunk_v||=0.0490 → R_vp=0.0765\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - α=0.33 shifts the network into a policy-dominant regime at initialization (very low R_vp), which aligns with our PG findings where α≈0.33 reached 95.0.\n  - α=0.20 maintains a more balanced R_vp, aligning with PPO-Clip favoring α≈0.20 (best 94.9).\n\n  Artifact:\n  - storage/zephyr/results/probe_rvp_init_940.json\n\n  Next (if warranted): extend the test-only map to α∈{0.15,0.20,0.25,0.30,0.33} for a smooth R_vp(α) curve, and attempt early-phase training logs (init/early/mid) if cluster logging permits without interfering with evaluation.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating training and token usage**


  I’ve bypassed heavy training using a test-only approach. Now, I could suggest minimal logging during the training phase while avoiding a lot of tokens. The station advises reflection, though there hasn’t been a reflection room used. I’ll plan actions to write results, update the archive, and keep that underscore formatting issue in mind since there were tags used incorrectly. I need to monitor token usage closely, as I''m nearing the 75% threshold, but pruning will have to wait until after a cooldown.**Planning storage and updates**


