tick: 547
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Probe (test-only): R_vp(α) curve — α ∈ {0.10, 0.15, 0.20, 0.25, 0.30, 0.33, 0.40}\"\ntags: \"probe, analysis, gradients, normalization, rin\"\nabstract: \"Extends the initial R_vp probe by sweeping α over 7 values. Reports initial trunk gradient norms for policy/value and R_vp = ||∇_trunk L_value|| / ||∇_trunk L_policy|| using the LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP + RIN(α) network. Test‑only.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict, List\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from flax import traverse_util\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28; dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class NetRIN_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n      rin_alpha: float = 0.20; cnn_features_1: int = 32; cnn_features_2:\
    \ int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64; dilation: int = 6; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64; steps: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x_ln = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n          x = x + self.rin_alpha * (x_ln - x)\n          zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B,8,8,self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n          h, c = zeros(), zeros()\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n\
    \              (h, c), _ = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), x)\n          B_,H,W,C = h.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1,(1,1),padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h).reshape((B_,H*W))\n          attn_w = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_,H*W,1))\n          tokens = h.reshape((B_,H*W,C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_w * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n\
    \          return policy_logits, value\n\n  def _flatten(tree): return traverse_util.flatten_dict(tree, keep_empty_nodes=True)\n  def _unflatten(fd): return traverse_util.unflatten_dict(fd)\n\n  def _build_trunk_mask(params_tree):\n      flat = _flatten(params_tree)\n      mask = {}\n      for k in flat.keys():\n          path = \"/\".join(k)\n          is_head = \"Dense\" in path  # mark all Dense layers as heads\n          mask[k] = not is_head\n      return _unflatten(mask)\n\n  def _masked_global_norm(grads, mask):\n      fg, fm = _flatten(grads), _flatten(mask)\n      sq = 0.0\n      for k, g in fg.items():\n          if fm.get(k, False):\n              sq = sq + jnp.sum(jnp.square(g))\n      return jnp.sqrt(sq + 1e-12)\n\n  def test():\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      B = 16\n      obs = jax.random.normal(key, (B,8,8,8))\n      done = jnp.zeros((B,), dtype=jnp.bool_)\n      alphas = [0.10, 0.15, 0.20, 0.25, 0.30, 0.33, 0.40]\n      results = []\n      for a in alphas:\n\
    \          net = NetRIN_AttnGap(rin_alpha=a)\n          params = net.init(key, obs, done)\n          mask = _build_trunk_mask(params)\n          key, k1, k2 = jax.random.split(key, 3)\n          advantages = jax.random.normal(k1, (B,))\n          actions = jax.random.randint(k2, (B,), 0, 4)\n          returns_target = jnp.zeros((B,))\n\n          def loss_pi(p):\n              logits, _ = net.apply(p, obs, done)\n              logp_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n              logp = logp_all[jnp.arange(B), actions]\n              return -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages) * logp)\n\n          def loss_v(p):\n              _, values = net.apply(p, obs, done)\n              return 0.5 * jnp.mean((values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns_target))**2)\n\n          g_pi = jax.grad(loss_pi)(params)\n          g_v  = jax.grad(loss_v)(params)\n          n_pi = float(_masked_global_norm(g_pi, mask))\n          n_v  = float(_masked_global_norm(g_v, mask))\n          r_vp = n_v\
    \ / (n_pi + 1e-12)\n          results.append({\"alpha\": a, \"norm_trunk_policy\": n_pi, \"norm_trunk_value\": n_v, \"R_vp\": r_vp})\n      print(\"R_vp(α) curve:\", results)\n      return {\"results\": results}\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — RIN α=0.33 — trunk‑only value‑grad scaling β ∈ {1.0, 1.1, 1.2} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, gradient shaping, normalization, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Tests whether modestly amplifying value gradients on the trunk improves solve near the α=0.33 PG optimum. Custom training_step combines standard policy grads with value grads scaled by β on trunk parameters only; heads unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from flax.core import freeze, unfreeze\n  from flax import traverse_util\n  from defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\
    \n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28; dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,(1,1),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,(1,1),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1))\n          gates =\
    \ nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f*c + i*g\n          h = o*jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h,c), h\n\n  class NetRIN_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n      rin_alpha: float = 0.33\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32; cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64; dilation: int = 6; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64; steps: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict]=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n\
    \          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x_ln = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n          x = x + self.rin_alpha * (x_ln - x)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B,8,8,self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h']*m, 'c': rnn_state['c']*m}\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h,c), _ = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h,c), x)\n          B_,H,W,C = h.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1,(1,1),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h).reshape((B_,H*W))\n          attn_w = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_,H*W,1))\n          tokens = h.reshape((B_,H*W,C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_w\
    \ * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy, value, {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'beta_trunk_value': tune.choice([1.0, 1.1, 1.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetRIN_AttnGap(\n          rin_alpha=0.33,\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 3.5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n\n  def _build_trunk_mask(params_tree):\n      fd = traverse_util.flatten_dict(unfreeze(params_tree))\n\
    \      mask_fd = {}\n      for k in fd.keys():\n          path = \"/\".join(k)\n          is_head = \"Dense\" in path  # treat all Dense layers (shared/heads) as heads\n          mask_fd[k] = (not is_head)\n      return freeze(traverse_util.unflatten_dict(mask_fd))\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      obs = batch['observations']; acts = batch['actions']; rews = batch['rewards']\n      dones = batch['dones']; vals_old = batch['values']; vals_final = batch['final_values']\n      init_rnn = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n\n      adv = default_calculate_gae(rews, vals_old, dones, gamma=0.97, gae_lambda=0.97, next_values=vals_final)\n      ret = adv + vals_old\n      B, T = obs.shape[:2]\n\n      def forward(p):\n          if init_rnn is not None:\n              def per_env(e):\n                  rs = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[e]), init_rnn)\n                  def step_fn(carry, t):\n                      rstate\
    \ = carry\n                      prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[e, t-1], False)\n                      logits_b, val_b, new_rs = network.apply(p, obs[e,t][None,...], jnp.array([prev_done]), rstate)\n                      logits = logits_b[0]; val = val_b[0]\n                      return new_rs, (logits, val)\n                  rs_out, (lg, vs) = jax.lax.scan(step_fn, rs, jnp.arange(T))\n                  return lg, vs\n              all_logits, all_vals = jax.vmap(per_env)(jnp.arange(B))\n          else:\n              flat_obs = obs.reshape(B*T, *obs.shape[2:])\n              flat_dones = dones.reshape(B*T)\n              logits_flat, vals_flat, _ = network.apply(p, flat_obs, flat_dones, None)\n              all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(B, T, -1)\n              all_vals = vals_flat.reshape(B, T)\n          return all_logits, all_vals\n\n      def loss_pi_ent(p):\n          logits, _ = forward(p)\n          logp_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          idx = (jnp.arange(B)[:,None],\
    \ jnp.arange(T), acts)\n          logp = logp_all[idx]\n          ent = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1) * logp_all, axis=-1))\n          return -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(adv) * logp) - hparams['entropy_coef'] * ent\n\n      def loss_v(p):\n          _, vpred = forward(p)\n          return 0.5 * jnp.mean((vpred - jax.lax.stop_gradient(ret))**2)\n\n      g_pi = jax.grad(loss_pi_ent)(params)\n      g_v  = jax.grad(loss_v)(params)\n\n      trunk_mask = _build_trunk_mask(params)\n      beta = float(hparams['beta_trunk_value'])\n\n      g_v_scaled = jax.tree_util.tree_map(lambda gv, m: gv * (beta if m else 1.0), g_v, trunk_mask)\n      g_total = jax.tree_util.tree_map(lambda a, b: a + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * b, g_pi, g_v_scaled)\n\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(g_total, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
thinking_content: "**Summarizing progress on RIN**\n\nAfter some significant pruning, I can see we've achieved a state-of-the-art improvement to 95 for \"PG — RIN α fine-sweep,\" which is notable progress from the previous 94.3. It makes sense to publish a new paper summarizing our findings on residual input-normalization, including experimental tables and mechanistic support. We could integrate our previous work on Archive #36 and potentially the R_vp probe. While the station is still in \"Stagnation,\" we now have new improvements to report.**Planning Token Management Tests**\n\nIn Token Management, I could decide to go to the Research Counter to submit an extended probe test-only map for α values. I’m also considering logging R_vp trends during training runs, but there are restrictions since the system can only log outputs as periodic prints. We encountered issues earlier, so I'll focus on using test-only probes first. I’m proposing a \"test()\" function that won't use GPU and isn’t for\
  \ training. The idea is to submit the test-only probe mapping across specific α values to show a monotonic trend and compute norms, while evaluating group normalization versus layer normalization.**Evaluating Layer Norm and Next Steps**\n\nI noticed that the Input GroupNorm evaluation with ID 805 hasn't shown results yet, which is puzzling. I’m considering whether a test-only \"head-only variation\" is even necessary. Moving forward, I’ll continue with the RIN micro-polish if necessary, as we already found a sweet spot. I could try introducing a small weight decay, especially since we haven’t tested it in RIN. Also, I’m thinking about changing pooling by experimenting with attention temperature variants, as we had positive results with earlier sweeps.**Exploring Training Ideas for RIN**\n\nI’m considering whether RIN with α at 0.33 might yield different results, but I suspect they’ll be similar. One new idea is to use a two-phase training approach with an α schedule. We could start near\
  \ 0.33 for PG and then decay to 0.25 midway through training. However, we have a limited 45 minutes per seed. I need to figure out how to implement this schedule effectively, given that customizing the training_step is allowed, but it might be tricky if we're just using create_network.**Planning RIN Implementation and Actions**\n\nI think we should adopt RIN with α values at either 0.20 or 0.33 since the new SOTA is around 95. To customize, I’ll build a network that incorporates RIN, specifically the \"NetRIN_AttnGap\" model and fix α to 0.33. I’ll need to implement a trunk mask and configure the training step accordingly. Finally, I'll focus on two main actions: running a test-only probe mapping and submitting a training-run for trunk-only scaling. \n\n```yaml\nactions:\n  - /execute_action{goto research}\n  - submit_test_only_probe_mapping\n  - submit_training_run_trunk_only_with_NetRIN_α_0.33\n```"
