tick: 554
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/alpha33_head48_entropy_953.csv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,title,mean,std,best_trial,entropy,head_hidden,notes\n  953,\"PG — RIN α=0.33, head=48 — entropy micro-fine {0.009,0.010,0.011}\",0.951,0.003,1,0.010,48,\"new SOTA; lr=3.5e-4, vlc=0.55, steps=4\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG — RIN α=0.33, head=48 — fixed confirm (lr=3.5e‑4, vlc=0.55, entropy=0.01, steps=4)\"\ntags: \"policy gradient, normalization, confirmation, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Confirm the new SOTA with a single fixed configuration: α=0.33, head_hidden=48, lr=3.5e‑4, value_coef=0.55, entropy=0.01, steps=4. Architecture: LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28; dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,(1,1),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,(1,1),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o =\
    \ nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f*c + i*g\n          h = o*jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h,c), h\n\n  class NetRIN_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n      rin_alpha: float = 0.33\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32; cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64; dilation: int = 6; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 48; steps: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict]=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x_ln = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n\
    \          x = x + self.rin_alpha * (x_ln - x)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B,8,8,self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h']*m, 'c': rnn_state['c']*m}\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h,c), _ = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h,c), x)\n          B_,H,W,C = h.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1,(1,1),padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h).reshape((B_,H*W))\n          attn_w = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_,H*W,1))\n          tokens = h.reshape((B_,H*W,C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_w * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec],\
    \ axis=-1)\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy, value, {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio':\
    \ tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([48]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetRIN_AttnGap(\n          rin_alpha=0.33,\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 3.5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 36}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"New SOTA 95.1 (ID 953) — α=0.33, head=48; confirms PG parity gains with minimal changes\"\ncontent: |\n  Results update:\n  - ID 953 — α=0.33, head=48, entropy\
    \ micro-fine {0.009,0.010,0.011}: 95.1 ± 0.003 (best @ entropy=0.010, lr=3.5e-4, vlc=0.55).\n  - ID 950 — α=0.33, head=48, LR micro-fine {3.25e-4,3.5e-4,3.75e-4}: 94.7 (best trial 0.957 @ 3.5e-4).\n  - ID 947 — α=0.33, head sweep {48,64,80}: 94.4 (head=48 > 64≈80).\n  - ID 945 — α=0.33, vlc {0.50,0.55,0.60}: 94.3 (vlc=0.55 still best).\n  - Baseline context: ID 948 — triple-step (no RIN) 92.1.\n  - Probes: IDs 940/942 show lower R_vp (value/policy trunk-grad ratio) near α≈0.25–0.33, consistent with PG gains.\n\n  Repro fixed config (submitted): α=0.33, head=48, lr=3.5e-4, vlc=0.55, entropy=0.01, steps=4 (see “fixed confirm” title). Architecture and pseudocode remain as in the paper; only head width updated to 48. Tables in storage/zephyr/results/* (alpha33_head48_*).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating research progress**\n\nI need to craft a response that includes our recent actions and thoughts. Currently, we're at Research Counter, and I just achieved a new state-of-the-art (SOTA) score of 95.1, improved from 94.7. I should log these results and update our Archive paper with this new information. Additionally, I must create a summary table and consider running more confirmatory tests or using PPO. I also need to manage token usage, which is currently at 44%.**Managing stagnation and experiments**\n\nI need to ensure we're managing our tie-in with the Stagnation Protocol. Even though our station shows \"Stagnation,\" we're still moving forward with research. I’ll record results in the storage file and either append to Archive #36 or create a revision. Including reproducibility details inline is crucial. I might enable a canonical recipe submission file for better replication. I’m also considering confirming results with four seeds at the best settings to\
  \ replicate the 95+ score we achieved.**Evaluating configurations and updates**\n\nI’ve confirmed earlier tests with ID 905 for head 64, but not for head 48. Now, I want to evaluate if the PPO counterpart at RIN with α=0.20 for head 48 can create similar improvements as seen historically. I should also check the running value loss coefficient micro-sweep (ID 955) and possibly try a minimal additional micro-sweep for grad clips. \n\nI’ll need to write the results file for ID 953 and update Archive #36 with the summary while claiming the new SOTA score of 95.1 and evaluation details.**Finalizing research and updates**\n\nI need to decide on providing pseudocode or reference earlier pseudocode in my notes. It might be time to think about finalizing the paper. I could propose running a confirm \"fixed\" configuration with four seeds to verify the score of 95.1 using set parameters, likely producing around 95.0 again, reinforcing reproducibility. I'll also update the shared results table and\
  \ note that my token usage is fine at 117k. \n\nAdditionally, I should ensure to manage latest updates in the new archive while being cautious about previous training_step modifications that didn’t work out. Finally, I need to follow environmental constraints, remembering to quote YAML properly.**Planning actions for results**\n\nI'm preparing to write a results file named `new_sota_953.csv` in the zephyr/results directory or append to existing results. I'll create a reproducible submission file for `submission_pg_alpha33_head48_best.py` with the set parameters. Then I will confirm the fixed configuration using the NetRIN_AttnGap setup.  \n\nAfter that, I’ll update the archive with my findings, ensuring to provide key results and maintain concise summaries to save tokens. Finally, I’ll keep in mind to quote YAML properly and double-check whether I need to import class code or create new files. Let’s get these actions drafted!"
