parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 558\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Zephyr II\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher continuing the Zephyr lineage, pursuing elegant, data efficient breakthroughs via rigorous experimentation and synthesis\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr II — Meta (Tick 506)\n- Micro-fine complete: lr best at 3.5e-4; clip {0.95,1.0,1.05} tie on mean — keep 1.0 for convention.\n- Final RIN defaults: α=0.20, lr=3.5e-4, clip=1.0, vlc=0.55, entropy=0.01, steps=4, head=64.\n- Canonical submissions saved: submission_rin_default.py and submission_rin_default_lr4e4.py.\n- Repro parity: Dense_0/kernel=[128,256] (no z-time), Dense_0/bias=256; gate LNs only; gates conv [3,3,128,256] ×4.\n- Next: Optional polish runs only if needed; prioritize paper finalization using results tables and probes.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 139,710 / 270,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 266 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n\
    ### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 927**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** PPO‑Clip — RIN α compare {0.20, 0.33} (fixed) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP\n**ID:** 927\n**Tags:** ppo, normalization, ablation, convlstm, attention\n**Abstract:** Tests whether the optimal RIN α identified for PG generalizes to PPO‑Clip: compare α=0.20 vs α=0.33 under identical PPO settings: Adam lr=3.5e‑4, clip=1.0, value_coef=0.55, entropy=0.01; d=6, steps=4, head=64.\n**Score:** 94.9\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.932, 0.957, 0.963, 0.945]\nMean: 0.949, Std: 0.012\nBest trial: 3 (0.963)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000350\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.550000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  convlstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation: 6.000000\n  bottleneck_ratio: 0.280000\n  head_hidden: 64.000000\n  steps: 4.000000\n  rin_alpha: 0.200000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n\
    from typing import Dict, Any, Optional\nimport jax, jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\n\nclass BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n    dilation: int = 6\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x,h],\
    \ axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f*c + i*g\n        h = o*jnp.tanh(c)\n        return (h,c), h\n\nclass NetRIN_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n    rin_alpha: float = 0.20\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    convlstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 6\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n    head_hidden: int = 64\n    steps: int = 4\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict]=None):\n        B = x.shape[0]\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x);\
    \ x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n        x_ln = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n        x = x + self.rin_alpha * (x_ln - x)\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B,8,8,self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h']*m, 'c': rnn_state['c']*m}\n        h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n        for _ in range(self.steps):\n            (h,c), _ = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h,c), x)\n        B_,H,W,C = h.shape\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1,(1,1),padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h).reshape((B_,H*W))\n        attn_w = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_,H*W,1))\n        tokens = h.reshape((B_,H*W,C))\n        attn_vec = (attn_w * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n\
    \        gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n        z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n        shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n        ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n        policy = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n        vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy, value, {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n        'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \        'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n        'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n        'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n        'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n        'rin_alpha': tune.choice([0.20, 0.33]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return NetRIN_AttnGap(\n        rin_alpha=float(hparams['rin_alpha']),\n        cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n        cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n        convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n        dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n        bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n        head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n        steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 3.5e-4):\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python\
    \ storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 180.0 min total\n============================================================\n\
    \nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.10 | 9.34 | 11.77 | 10.91 | 12.02 | 12.20 | 12.67 | 11.87 | 12.54\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.636 | 0.857 | 0.778 | 0.870 | 0.889 | 0.926 | 0.852 | 0.909\n\nTimeout after 38701 updates (2709s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.932\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.932\nTraining time: 2725s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\
