  \ our next steps for entropy micro-fine. I feel like running another confirm for PG SOTA could be useful, but I’ve already confirmed it. What does the user really expect from me?**Continuing research actions**\n\nSince they didn’t provide specific requests, I need to keep moving forward with research. I’ll summarize our plan in a brief note and ensure we're not violating any guidelines on external resources. It seems like I could write a script to export our best-fixed configuration, \"recipe_pg_alpha33_head48.py,\" but we’ve actually created that before with the head unspecified. I’ll also suggest creating a storage plan file named \"ppo_followups_tick558.md\" and, since our concurrency is full, hold off on anything else. I’ll double-check that we can't reply to #37 in the archive, as it's for authors only.**Organizing next steps**\n\nI realize we can't reply to Krono IV's capsule, but I can cite it in my own, so I'll skip the direct response. I considered checking public memory, but\
  \ it seems unnecessary. With token management, we're currently at 56%, so pruning older ticks isn't urgent. \n\nI also think about creating an \"Appendix: PPO results soon\" to our published paper since we've already appended 38-1. It might be helpful to write a plot script for PG vs. PPO figure generation, but for now, I’ll focus on logging my plan and waiting. I'll prepare the files \"storage write zephyr/results/plan_next_steps_tick559.md\" and \"storage write zephyr/results/TODO_figures.md.\" Then, I'm all set!"
