tick: 560
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/ppo_results_tick560.csv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,title,mean,std,best_setting,notes\n  966,\"PPO α=0.20 — head_hidden {48,64,80}\",0.946,0.010,\"head=80\",\"lr=3.5e-4, clip=0.2, vclip=0.2, vlc=0.55, ent=0.01, steps=4\"\n  967,\"PPO α=0.20 — policy clip_range {0.15,0.20,0.25}\",0.942,0.008,\"clip=0.20\",\"head=64; vclip=0.2 fixed; other settings as above\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PPO‑Clip — α=0.20, head=80 — entropy micro‑fine {0.009,0.010,0.011} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP\"\ntags: \"ppo, normalization, entropy, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"With α=0.20 and head_hidden=80 (best from head sweep), sweep entropy_coef ∈ {0.009,0.010,0.011} under clip=0.2, value_clip=0.2, lr=3.5e‑4, value_coef=0.55, steps=4.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Optional\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from ray import tune\n  from submissions.submission_ppo_clip\
    \ import training_step, create_optimizer as ppo_create_optimizer, BASE_SEED\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28; dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,(1,1),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,(1,1),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1))\n\
    \          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f*c + i*g\n          h = o*jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h,c), h\n\n  class NetRIN_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n      rin_alpha: float = 0.20\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32; cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64; dilation: int = 6; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 80; steps: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict]=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x);\
    \ x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x_ln = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n          x = x + self.rin_alpha * (x_ln - x)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B,8,8,self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h']*m, 'c': rnn_state['c']*m}\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h,c), _ = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h,c), x)\n          B_,H,W,C = h.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1,(1,1),padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h).reshape((B_,H*W))\n          attn_w = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_,H*W,1))\n          tokens\
    \ = h.reshape((B_,H*W,C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_w * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy, value, {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.009, 0.010, 0.011]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'clip_range': tune.choice([0.20]),\n\
    \          'value_clip_range': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([80]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'rin_alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetRIN_AttnGap(\n          rin_alpha=float(hparams['rin_alpha']),\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float =\
    \ 3.5e-4):\n      return ppo_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PPO‑Clip — α=0.20, head=80 — LR micro‑fine {3.25e‑4,3.5e‑4,3.75e‑4} (clip=0.2, vclip=0.2) — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP\"\ntags: \"ppo, normalization, learning rate, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"With α=0.20 and head_hidden=80 (best so far), sweep learning_rate ∈ {3.25e‑4,3.5e‑4,3.75e‑4} under clip=0.2, value_clip=0.2, entropy=0.01, value_coef=0.55, steps=4.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Optional\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from ray import tune\n  from submissions.submission_ppo_clip import training_step, create_optimizer as ppo_create_optimizer, BASE_SEED\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28; dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n\
    \          y = nn.Conv(mid,(1,1),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,(1,1),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f*c + i*g\n          h = o*jnp.tanh(c)\n          return\
    \ (h,c), h\n\n  class NetRIN_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n      rin_alpha: float = 0.20\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32; cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64; dilation: int = 6; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 80; steps: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict]=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x_ln = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n          x = x + self.rin_alpha * (x_ln - x)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n  \
    \            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B,8,8,self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h']*m, 'c': rnn_state['c']*m}\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h,c), _ = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h,c), x)\n          B_,H,W,C = h.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1,(1,1),padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h).reshape((B_,H*W))\n          attn_w = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_,H*W,1))\n          tokens = h.reshape((B_,H*W,C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_w * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z);\
    \ shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy, value, {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.25e-4, 3.5e-4, 3.75e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.010]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'clip_range': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'value_clip_range': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n       \
    \   'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([80]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'rin_alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetRIN_AttnGap(\n          rin_alpha=float(hparams['rin_alpha']),\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 3.5e-4):\n      return ppo_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI see the user provided the results from the PPO sweeps but didn't ask a specific question. The findings include the best policy clip and head settings, with values indicating that clip 0.2 and head 80 seem optimal. It also appears that the overall mean didn’t improve compared to an earlier trial. My next steps will be to record these results and run additional experiments with the specified parameters for entropy and learning rates. Only two concurrent experiments are allowed.**Queuing experiments**\n\nI need to queue two experiments: first, an entropy micro-fine with head=80, and second, a learning rate (LR) micro-fine with the same head and a clip range of 0.2. Alternatively, I am considering running a value clip range micro-sweep to explore potential synergy. While the previous plan said to do entropy first, both can run concurrently. I’ll prioritize entropy and the value clip range sweep while keeping the learning rate fixed at 3.5e-4, which\
  \ was effective in prior trials. I also need to log results and create code for submission.**Formatting YAML and submissions**\n\nI need to ensure proper YAML quoting for any strings that contain colons. So, I checked titles like \"PPO‑Clip — RIN α=0.20,\" but it only has an equals sign and no colons. I confirm that we’re good there. \n\nI’ll move forward by creating two submissions and one storage write, while staying within the token limit. The first storage write will be saved as \"zephyr/results/ppo_head_clip_results_tick560.csv,\" capturing results 966 and 967. \n\nThe first submission will focus on entropy micro-fine, and the second on LR micro-fine. I might also consider the value clip range micro-sweep since it could be beneficial.**Clarifying submission plan**\n\nI want to follow the earlier plan for submissions with the order: first, entropy micro-fine, then LR micro-fine, and finally a value clip confirmation. I'll queue the first two. \n\nIt’s essential to ensure the code aligns\
  \ with the previous patterns, particularly using the NetRIN_AttnGap and fixing rin_alpha. \n\nShould I include BASE_SEED? Previous PPO submissions didn’t declare it but imported it from earlier modules. The default is 42 if not explicitly defined. I should verify whether BASE_SEED was consistently imported in previous messages.**Preparing submission details**\n\nI noticed that previous submissions imported BASE_SEED along with the training step and optimizer. Since we want to stay consistent, I'll include BASE_SEED or default it to 42. Consistency is better!\n\nNext, I’ll set the optimizer to use ppo_create_optimizer with the learning rate and define hyperparameters based on earlier instructions. I need to write the storage file and create two submissions.\n\nThe storage path will contain results for entries 966 and 967, and I’ll ensure the titles, tags, and abstracts for each submission are properly formatted. I'll also quote YAML elements correctly, so I can proceed with the execution."
