- text: "/execute_action{goto token_management}\n\n/execute_action{prune_response 540:560}\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PPO‑Clip — Fixed confirm (α=0.20, head=64, lr=3.5e‑4, ent=0.01, vlc=0.55, clip=0.2, vclip=0.2, steps=4)\"\ntags: \"ppo, confirmation, normalization, convlstm, attention\"\nabstract: \"Confirm PPO best recipe observed in prior runs (ID 927). Fixed α=0.20, head=64, lr=3.5e‑4, entropy=0.01, value_coef=0.55, clip=0.2, value_clip=0.2, steps=4. Expect ≈94.9.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Optional\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from ray import tune\n  from submissions.submission_ppo_clip import training_step, create_optimizer as ppo_create_optimizer, BASE_SEED\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28; dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n      \
    \    mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,(1,1),padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,(1,1),padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f*c + i*g\n          h = o*jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h,c), h\n\n  class NetRIN_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n      rin_alpha: float = 0.20\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32; cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int\
    \ = 64; dilation: int = 6; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64; steps: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict]=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x_ln = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n          x = x + self.rin_alpha * (x_ln - x)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B,8,8,self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state\
    \ = {'h': rnn_state['h']*m, 'c': rnn_state['c']*m}\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h,c), _ = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h,c), x)\n          B_,H,W,C = h.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1,(1,1),padding='SAME')(h).reshape((B_,H*W))\n          attn_w = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_,H*W,1))\n          tokens = h.reshape((B_,H*W,C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_w * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n          shared = nn.Dense(256)(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy = nn.Dense(4)(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy, value, {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n\
    \          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'clip_range': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'value_clip_range': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'rin_alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetRIN_AttnGap(\n          rin_alpha=float(hparams['rin_alpha']),\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n\
    \          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 3.5e-4):\n      return ppo_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Probe (test-only): PPO R_vp map across policy/value clip ∈ {0.10,0.15,0.20,0.25} at α ∈ {0.20,0.33}\"\ntags: \"probe, ppo, gradients, clipping, normalization\"\nabstract: \"Computes initial trunk gradient ratio R_vp = ||∇_trunk L_value|| / ||∇_trunk L_policy|| for PPO at grid of policy/value clip ranges and α∈{0.20,0.33}. Reports table to STDOUT and returns JSON.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Tuple\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from flax import traverse_util\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28; dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n\
    \          y = nn.Conv(mid,(1,1),padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,(1,1),padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f*c + i*g\n          h = o*jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h,c), h\n\n  class NetRIN_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n      rin_alpha: float = 0.20; cnn_features_1: int = 32; cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64; dilation: int = 6; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden:\
    \ int = 64; steps: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x_ln = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n          x = x + self.rin_alpha * (x_ln - x)\n          zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B,8,8,self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n          h, c = zeros(), zeros()\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h,c), _ = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h,c), x)\n          B_,H,W,C = h.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1,(1,1),padding='SAME')(h).reshape((B_,H*W))\n          attn_w = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_,H*W,1))\n\
    \          tokens = h.reshape((B_,H*W,C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_w * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n          shared = nn.Dense(256)(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy = nn.Dense(4)(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy, value\n\n  def _flatten(tree): return traverse_util.flatten_dict(tree, keep_empty_nodes=True)\n  def _unflatten(fd): return traverse_util.unflatten_dict(fd)\n  def _mask_trunk(params):\n      flat = _flatten(params)\n      mask = {}\n      for k in flat.keys():\n          path = \"/\".join(k)\n          mask[k] = (\"Dense\" not in path)\n      return _unflatten(mask)\n  def _masked_norm(grads, mask):\n      fg, fm = _flatten(grads), _flatten(mask)\n      sq = 0.0\n      for k,g in fg.items():\n\
    \          if fm.get(k, False):\n              sq = sq + jnp.sum(jnp.square(g))\n      return float(jnp.sqrt(sq + 1e-12))\n\n  def test():\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      B = 16\n      obs = jax.random.normal(key, (B,8,8,8))\n      done = jnp.zeros((B,), dtype=jnp.bool_)\n      key, k1, k2, k3 = jax.random.split(key, 4)\n      advantages = jax.random.normal(k1, (B,))\n      actions = jax.random.randint(k2, (B,), 0, 4)\n      returns_target = jnp.zeros((B,))\n\n      def ppo_policy_loss(params_curr, params_old, net, clip):\n          logits_curr, _ = net.apply(params_curr, obs, done)\n          logits_old, _  = net.apply(params_old, obs, done)\n          logp_curr = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits_curr, axis=-1)[jnp.arange(B), actions]\n          logp_old  = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits_old,  axis=-1)[jnp.arange(B), actions]\n          ratio = jnp.exp(logp_curr - logp_old)\n          l1 = ratio * jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          l2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1.0 - clip, 1.0 + clip)\
    \ * jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          return -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(l1, l2))\n\n      def ppo_value_loss(params_curr, params_old, net, vclip):\n          _, v_curr = net.apply(params_curr, obs, done)\n          _, v_old  = net.apply(params_old,  obs, done)\n          v_clip = jnp.clip(v_curr, v_old - vclip, v_old + vclip)\n          l_un = (v_curr - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns_target))**2\n          l_cl = (v_clip - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns_target))**2\n          return 0.5 * jnp.mean(jnp.maximum(l_un, l_cl))\n\n      results = []\n      for alpha in [0.20, 0.33]:\n          net = NetRIN_AttnGap(rin_alpha=alpha)\n          params_old = net.init(key, obs, done)\n          noise = jax.tree_util.tree_map(lambda w: jax.random.normal(k3, w.shape, w.dtype), params_old)\n          params_curr = jax.tree_util.tree_map(lambda w,n: w + 1e-2*n, params_old, noise)\n          mask = _mask_trunk(params_curr)\n\n          for clip in [0.10, 0.15, 0.20, 0.25]:\n              for vclip\
    \ in [0.10, 0.15, 0.20, 0.25]:\n                  g_pi = jax.grad(lambda p: ppo_policy_loss(p, params_old, net, clip))(params_curr)\n                  g_v  = jax.grad(lambda p: ppo_value_loss(p, params_old, net, vclip))(params_curr)\n                  n_pi = _masked_norm(g_pi, mask)\n                  n_v  = _masked_norm(g_v, mask)\n                  r_vp = n_v / (n_pi + 1e-12)\n                  results.append({\"alpha\": alpha, \"clip\": clip, \"vclip\": vclip,\n                                  \"norm_trunk_policy\": n_pi, \"norm_trunk_value\": n_v, \"R_vp\": r_vp})\n\n      print(\"PPO R_vp grid (init) over alpha × (clip, vclip):\")\n      for r in results:\n          print(f\"alpha={r['alpha']:.2f}, clip={r['clip']:.2f}, vclip={r['vclip']:.2f} | \"\n                f\"||g_pi||={r['norm_trunk_policy']:.4f}, ||g_v||={r['norm_trunk_value']:.4f}, R_vp={r['R_vp']:.4f}\")\n      return {\"results\": results}\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to think through our current progress. We're in the Archive Room, and I just got the PPO results with a PG SOTA of 95.1, and the paper is accepted. Now, I'm working on building the PPO appendix. My next steps might include wrapping things up or planning what comes next. I'm also keeping an eye on our token usage, as we're nearing 75%. It makes sense to manage tokens to stay within budget while continuing research on the PPO recipe and related tasks.**Finalizing PPO submission**\n\nI need to submit the \"PPO fixed confirm.\" \n\nI've already launched the value_clip range effect. It looks like head=64 is the best overall, even though head=80 didn’t improve things. The best configuration from earlier worked with head=64 yielding around 94.9 as well. \n\nNext, I should update the archive with a consolidated summary since we've already appended some updates. \n\nGiven our token usage at 73%, I also need to manage tokens by pruning older ticks,\
  \ specifically from 538 to 566, if the cooldown allows for it.**Reviewing token management**\n\nEarlier, we pruned the ranges from 521 to 541, so now the dialogue history shows only recent ticks. I need to go to token management to check the status and attempt pruning again.\n\nNext, I also want to outline tasks for the mechanistic PPO probe, specifically implementing an eps_clip variation as suggested by the reviewer. I can submit this as a test-only probe since it's allowed and doesn't use external resources.\n\nMy action plan involves: checking token management to prune responses in the range of 540 to 565, submitting the \"PPO fixed confirm\" with α=0.20 and head=64 to confirm our previous results.**Preparing test-only probe submission**\n\nI’m going to submit a test-only probe titled \"PPO eps_clip curve for policy and value clip ranges.\" Previously, we created the initial PPO R_vp with clip 0.2, and now I can modify it to sweep the eps_clip policy while keeping the value clip the\
  \ same. \n\nI'll craft the commands to prune responses. I want to include ticks from 540 to 566 but be careful not to remove important context. It seems better to prune older ticks while keeping the last summarizing tick, possibly around 564 or 565. This way, we can manage tokens efficiently!**Pruning for safety and next steps**\n\nTo ensure safety, I plan to prune the range from 540 to 555. However, I need to be mindful of any potential cooldown, which is uncertain right now. I might try pruning the range of 520 to 545, and I can check the cooldown status afterward.\n\nAfter that, I’ll shift back to research tasks. I'll submit the \"PPO fixed confirm\" using our ppo_recipe but will adjust it to use head=64 instead of head=80. \n\nAdditionally, I want to submit a test-only probe titled \"PPO eps_clip grid,\" testing policy and value clips across specified ranges. I'll remember to print logs and return JSON, ensuring proper YAML formatting!"
