role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/ppo_head64_valueclip_984.csv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,title,mean,std,best_setting,notes\n  984,\"PPO α=0.20, head=64 — value_clip_range {0.15,0.20,0.25}\",0.943,0.010,\"value_clip=0.20\",\"No gain vs fixed recipe (95.1); vclip tighter/looser underperform\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PPO‑Clip — α=0.20, head=64 — grad‑clip confirm (clip_norm=1.1) — fixed config\"\ntags: \"ppo, gradient clipping, confirmation, convlstm, normalization\"\nabstract: \"Test small change to global gradient‑norm clip for PPO fixed recipe (ID 981 was 95.1 at clip=1.0). Here set clip_norm=1.1; all else fixed: lr=3.5e‑4, ent=0.01, vlc=0.55, policy clip=0.2, value clip=0.2, steps=4.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Optional\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from submissions.submission_ppo_clip\
    \ import training_step, BASE_SEED\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28; dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,(1,1),padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,(1,1),padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f*c + i*g\n  \
    \        h = o*jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h,c), h\n\n  class NetRIN_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n      rin_alpha: float = 0.20\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32; cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64; dilation: int = 6; bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64; steps: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict]=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x_ln = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n          x = x + self.rin_alpha * (x_ln - x)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B,8,8,self.convlstm_features),\
    \ dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h']*m, 'c': rnn_state['c']*m}\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h,c), _ = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h,c), x)\n          B_,H,W,C = h.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1,(1,1),padding='SAME')(h).reshape((B_,H*W))\n          attn_w = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_,H*W,1))\n          tokens = h.reshape((B_,H*W,C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_w * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n          shared = nn.Dense(256)(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy = nn.Dense(4)(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(shared);\
    \ vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy, value, {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'clip_range': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'value_clip_range': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'rin_alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetRIN_AttnGap(\n          rin_alpha=float(hparams['rin_alpha']),\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n\
    \          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 3.5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.1), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 38}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Minor ablation: value_clip (head=64) neutral; queued grad‑clip=1.1 confirm\"\ncontent: |\n  Added result: head=64 value_clip_range {0.15,0.20,0.25} scores 94.3 (ID 984), confirming no gain vs fixed PPO 95.1 (ID 981).\n  New run queued: PPO fixed recipe with grad‑clip=1.1 (rest unchanged) to test slight relaxation beyond clip=1.0.\n  Artifacts: results/ppo_head64_valueclip_984.csv\n```"
thinking_content: "**Exploring gradient clipping and updates**\n\nI'm looking into the gradient clip values of 1.05 or 1.1 for PPO, as earlier experiments with PG tested clipping. PPO seems to use clipping ratio rather than gradient norm. I could consider proposing a small gradient norm clip variation, or I might test head_hidden sizes like 56, 64, and 72 near 64 for PPO, though 64 appears to win for simplicity. I also want to change the value loss coefficient micro-sweep before finalizing \"Synthesis\" in Archive.**Planning next steps for analysis**\n\nI need to outline some tasks, like writing a results file for value_clip head64 with a value of 984. I might also submit a small gradient norm clip sweep for the PPO head with α=0.20, matching earlier tiny grad-clip sweeps. I should establish parity between PG and PPO and finalize the paper analysis. Even though we did a final paper (#38), an addendum noting \"PPO reached 95.1\" could be useful. Storing the \"SOTA checkpoint code recipe\"\
  \ in storage is also on my to-do list.**Updating and testing configurations**\n\nI need to update the results file for 984 and make use of the second available running slot since only 985 is active. I plan to submit a PPO head64 grad-clip micro-sweep using optimizer clip norms of {0.9, 1.0, 1.1} to see if we can achieve greater than 95.1. I’ll need to customize the optimizer code for that. I also want to consider testing steps of 3, 4, and 5, but given earlier findings, the sweet spot seemed to be 4. For now, the priority is on the grad clip micro-sweep. I’ll proceed with the necessary file write and submission.**Updating and executing tasks**\n\nI need to add a brief reply to Archive #38 stating that \"value_clip head64 yields 94.3,\" which isn't helpful, but we previously reported 95.1 in the last reply (#38-6). I’ll also be mindful of the token budget and keep messages concise. The action commands I’ll produce include a storage write for 984 and submitting the new experiment with \"\
  PPO α=0.20, head=64 – grad-clip micro-fine {0.9, 1.0, 1.1}.\" I’ll craft the code using a customized create_optimizer method to incorporate the clip norm parameter from hparams.**Defining optimizer and planning experiments**\n\nI believe I should define the create_optimizer to include the \"grad_clip\" parameter used in clip_by_global_norm. However, since create_optimizer expects a learning_rate as a float, I can’t pass additional parameters directly. Instead, I could define my own create_optimizer and use a default constant value for grad_clip. I also want to consider how to incorporate this method into the training_step, where we could use gradient clipping manually. \n\nFor now, I’ll write the results for 984, update Archive #38 to note that the value-clip didn’t help, and maybe schedule one more run with a fixed grad clip of 1.1. I’ll ensure everything follows the required structure.**Importing necessary modules and finalizing**\n\nI realized that I didn’t import optax in the earlier\
  \ PPO submission, so I'll make sure to include that. I’ll keep the code minimal and use head_hidden set to 64. Now, it's time to prepare the final response, ensuring that I keep commentary light. I'll focus on implementing the necessary changes and tidy up the code before we finalize everything. Let's get this done!"
