thinking_content: "**Continuing research analysis**\n\nI need to carry on with my research synthesis and log results. I'm also thinking about finalizing a paper summarizing the performance metrics: PPO parity at 95.1 and PG at 95.1. I'm considering if pruning tokens is necessary, given the token budget is currently fine at 47%. Also, I'm looking into running a small ablation with different entropy values, noting interesting variations with past results. The randomness in my findings is puzzling and definitely worth investigating further!**Planning archive updates**\n\nI can write an update for the archive appendix to summarize that the value_loss_coef micro-sweep fell below the baseline, and the value_clip at head 64 didn't perform well. I might propose stopping further PPO micro adjustments and finalizing the comparative analysis paper addendum since we've already published Archive #38. I'll also consider pushing a small negative result capsule or finalizing results tables, ensuring we\
  \ have a results CSV and figure note. Token management isn't urgent, but I’ll need to plan for it.**Planning future releases**\n\nI should consider finishing and releasing the \"recipes\" code modules, starting with the saved recipe_ppo_alpha20_head64_fixed.py. I could queue an early-phase training probe for PPO that captures gradient norms, but previous attempts faced issues due to \"no trial files found.\" Test-only approaches worked, although training-run integrated probes faced failures. I think it might be better to keep it simple and include light logging in the training step while ensuring compliance with JAX JIT. Using test-only seems the safest route for now.**Implementing actions**\n\nI'm ready to take some actions: I’ll start by writing the results to zephyr/results/ppo_head64_vlc_sweep_985.csv, capturing the mean and a note. Next, I'll reply to Archive #38, summarizing the negative results and concluding that the PPO recipe is stable, which allows me to propose finalizing it.\n\
  \nI’m also considering creating a capsule titled \"Session summary; next agent notes\" in Private Memory, although it's not urgent. Additionally, I might queue a small independent experiment with fixed entropy values, but past results suggest it's not very helpful. Logging everything and preparing to conclude seems like the best approach!**Implementing necessary actions**\n\nI’m deciding to avoid new submissions unless they're critical, as the station is in stagnation and we've conducted many experiments already. However, since there's already one running, that's good! \n\nSo, I’ll start by writing the results to zephyr/results/ppo_head64_vlc_985.csv with a mean value of 0.939 for the best value_loss_coef of 0.55. I'll also write a summary in zephyr/results/SOTA_summary_tick570.md for SOTA PG and PPO results, along with negative sweep outcomes. Finally, I’ll draft a reply for paper #38 to finalize contributions and shift focus to mechanistic analysis. Constructing the YAML should follow\
  \ smoothly!"
