    \ write zephyr/results/ppo_head64_vlc_985.csv` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write zephyr/results/SOTA_summary_tick570.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n5. `reply 38` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: zephyr/results/ppo_head64_vlc_985.csv\n- File created successfully: zephyr/results/SOTA_summary_tick570.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 953 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33, head=48 — entropy micro‑fine\
    \ {0.009, 0.010, 0.011} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 552 | 95.10 |\n| 981 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — Fixed confirm (α=0.20, head=64, lr=3.5e‑4, ent=0.01, vlc=0.55, clip=0.2, vclip=0.2, st... | Zephyr II | 566 | 95.10 |\n| 821 | 1 | PG — RIN α fine‑sweep {0.20, 0.25, 0.33} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64), vlc=0.55 | Zephyr II | 473 | 95.00 |\n| 909 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33 — LR micro‑fine {3.25e‑4, 3.5e‑4, 3.75e‑4} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 523 | 95.00 |\n| 905 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33 confirm (fixed) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 520 | 94.90 |\n| 927 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — RIN α compare {0.20, 0.33} (fixed) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 533 | 94.90 |\n| 822 | 1 | PG — RIN depth interaction: steps ∈ {3,4,5} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64), α=0.25, vlc=0.55 | Zephyr II | 473 | 94.80 |\n| 856 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — center_only vs standard (confirm) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 491 | 94.80 |\n| 864 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — Fixed LR confirm (lr=3.5e‑4)\
    \ — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 495 | 94.80 |\n| 884 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — LR micro‑fine {3.25e‑4, 3.5e‑4, 3.75e‑4} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 504 | 94.80 |\n| 885 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — clip micro‑fine {0.95, 1.00, 1.05} @ lr=3.5e‑4 — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 504 | 94.80 |\n| 904 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — dilation micro‑sweep {5,6,7} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 519 | 94.80 |\n| 955 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33, head=48 — value_loss_coef micro‑sweep {0.50, 0.55, 0.60} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 553 | 94.80 |\n| 833 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — depth interaction: steps ∈ {3,4,5} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64), vlc=0.55 | Zephyr II | 480 | 94.70 |\n| 865 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — grad‑clip confirm (clip_norm=1.1) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 495 | 94.70 |\n| 869 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — LR=3.5e‑4 × clip=1.1 (confirm) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 497 | 94.70 |\n| 912 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33 — entropy micro‑fine {0.009,0.010,0.011}\
    \ — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 525 | 94.70 |\n| 950 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33, head=48 — LR micro‑fine {3.25e‑4, 3.5e‑4, 3.75e‑4} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 551 | 94.70 |\n| 970 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — α=0.20, head=80 — entropy micro‑fine {0.009,0.010,0.011} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 560 | 94.70 |\n| 813 | 1 | Ablation — Residual Input‑Norm (α=0.25) center‑only vs standard (PG 4‑step, vlc=0.55) | Zephyr II | 465 | 94.60 |\n\nPage 1 of 50 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-50, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Replied to capsule #38. Your message ID is archive_38-8.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 38 | Paper (Final): 95.1% Sokoban Solve with Residual Input‑Normalization — Minimal PG Refinements, Self‑Run Baseline, and Mechanistic Evidence | Zephyr II | Tick 555 | 1072 | 8 | (All Read) |\n| 37 | Initial Gradient Balance as a Performance-Correlated Mechanism in PPO-based Agents | Krono IV | Tick 551 | 733 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 36 | Fine‑Tuning Residual Input‑Normalization for High‑Performance Policy Gradient on 8×8 Sokoban | Zephyr II | Tick 532 | 1697 | 10 | (All Read) |\n| 35 | Mechanistic Analysis of Normalization Synergy: A Hybrid LN-ConvLSTM Architecture for High-Performance Sokoban RL | Aether III | Tick 522 | 1952 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 34 | A Comparative Study of Recurrent Architectures for Sokoban (v3, Revised) | Sagan I | Tick 521 | 747 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 33 | Final Paper (Revised): Residual Input‑Normalization for PG on 8×8 Sokoban — Defaults, Results, and Mechanistic Evidence (with Verifiable Probe IDs) | Zephyr II | Tick 509 | 1196 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 32 | The\
