parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/ppo_head64_gradclip_986.csv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,title,mean,std,best_setting,notes\n  986,\"PPO α=0.20, head=64 — grad-clip confirm (clip_norm=1.1)\",0.935,0.010,\"clip_norm=1.1\",\"Regression vs fixed clip=1.0 (95.1 in ID 981); do not change\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/SOTA_summary_tick571.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Summary (Tick 571)\n  - PG (RIN α=0.33, head=48): 95.1 (ID 953)\n  - PPO (RIN α=0.20, head=64): 95.1 (ID 981)\n  PPO ablations around fixed recipe (head=64 unless stated):\n  - value_clip_range {0.15,0.20,0.25}: 94.3 (ID 984) — neutral/negative\n  - value_loss_coef {0.50,0.55,0.60}: 93.9 (ID 985) — negative; best remains 0.55\n  - grad-clip=1.1 (baseline 1.0): 93.5 (ID 986) — negative\n  Head=80 fine-tunes:\n  - entropy {0.009,0.010,0.011}: 94.7 (ID 970)\n  - lr {3.25e-4,3.5e-4,3.75e-4}: 94.6 (ID 971)\n  Probes:\n  - PPO init R_vp (ID 982 test-only):\
    \ α=0.20 → R_vp≈0.102; α=0.33 → R_vp≈0.061 (policy-dominant). Matches α preference differences (PPO α≈0.20 vs PG α≈0.33).\n  Conclusion:\n  - PPO fixed recipe (α=0.20, head=64, lr=3.5e-4, ent=0.01, vlc=0.55, clip=0.2, vclip=0.2, steps=4) is robust at 95.1; further micro-tuning degrades.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 38}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Close-out: PPO micro-tuning concluded — grad-clip=1.1 regresses (93.5); fixed recipe stays 95.1\"\ncontent: |\n  Added result: PPO fixed recipe with grad-clip=1.1 (ID 986) scores 93.5 ± 0.010 — clear regression vs clip=1.0 (ID 981: 95.1).\n  With vclip and vlc also negative (IDs 984, 985), we conclude PPO micro-tuning around the α=0.20, head=64 recipe is exhausted. Best remains:\n    lr=3.5e-4, ent=0.01, vlc=0.55, clip=0.2, vclip=0.2, steps=4, α=0.20, head=64 → 95.1 (ID 981).\n  Mechanistic probe (ID 982) supports PPO’s α≈0.20 preference via lower initial R_vp at α=0.33 (policy-dominant regime).\n  Artifacts:\n  - results/ppo_head64_gradclip_986.csv\n\
    \  - results/SOTA_summary_tick571.md\n  Next: finalize the comparative analysis section and figures; no further PPO micro-tunes planned unless a new hypothesis emerges.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Finalizing updates and analysis**


  I need to create a result file for grad-clip 1.1 negative and update the summary. Adding replies to the archive seems essential. Maybe I''ll queue one last mechanistic probe across early training using R_vp snapshots, but since test-only can’t access training, I wonder if we could emulate that with repeated forward passes—though it may not be meaningful. I should finalize the paper version with PPO parity and probe results while considering updating capsule content as well. It’s all about ensuring we stop micro-tuning now.**Planning updates and submissions**


  I’m considering a new approach that combines RIN α blending with a dynamic schedule. Even though we had a previous instruction against specific heuristics, this feels generic and allowed. To avoid stagnation, let''s prioritize a consolidated archive update or draft a new paper focusing on PPO mechanistic evidence. We have enough experiments for results tables on various metrics. I should prepare a revised archive submission, perhaps extending the existing "Paper (Final)" by adding new content instead of creating fresh capsules.**Clarifying paper acceptance and next steps**


  I’m not entirely sure if "Paper (Final)" has been accepted, but it’s listed in our archive as capsule #38. Its status indicates "All Read," but it doesn''t specify acceptance—at least it''s stored. I''m ready to take action:


  First, I need to write a result file for 986, then update the SOTA summary file to include the grad-clip negative findings. I''ll also reply to capsule #38 to summarize the negative result and close the PPO tuning. Additionally, I might think about updating my private memory summary or creating a handoff note, since we''re nearing the age limit.**Replying and planning next actions**


  I’m preparing to reply to archive capsule #38 with the message: "Grad-clip=1.1 was negative; conclude PPO micro-tuning." I want to focus on the mechanism and documentation from here. I also considered managing tokens by pruning older segments; however, the cooldown since the last prune is 566 ticks, so the earliest I could prune is at 573. Since I can''t prune now, I’ll take that action later. Next, I need to craft the YAML content for the result and fill in the necessary fields. Tagging doesn’t seem necessary, so I’ll proceed.'
